[{"sha":"cf057b4bcdb77ad67014f7dabe71e71f2366c95e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNmMDU3YjRiY2RiNzdhZDY3MDE0ZjdkYWJlNzFlNzFmMjM2NmM5NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T03:38:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T03:38:36Z"},"message":"fix(sdk)!: disambiguate `read_file` line gutters (#4561)\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> This is a breaking change for callers that parse raw `read_file`\noutput. The line-number gutter no longer uses `cat -n`-style padding and\na tab separator; parsers should expect line markers followed by two\nspaces before the source content.\n\n`read_file` returns file contents with line numbers so agents can\nreference and edit specific lines. Before this PR, those line numbers\nwere rendered like `cat -n`: a fixed-width line-number gutter followed\nby a tab.\n\nBefore:\n\n```text\n     1\tdef build_config():\n     2\t\treturn {\"enabled\": True}\n```\n\nThat format is hard to interpret when the source line itself starts with\na tab. In the example above, line 2 has two tabs in a row: one tab from\nthe `read_file` gutter and one tab from the source indentation. A model\ncan mistake both tabs for source content, then send an over-indented\n`old_string` to `edit_file`.\n\nThis PR changes the SDK formatter so the line marker is followed by two\nspaces before the original source content.\n\nAfter:\n\n```text\n1  def build_config():\n2  \treturn {\"enabled\": True}\n```\n\nNow the gutter is visually and textually distinct from the file\ncontents: the first two spaces separate the line marker from the source,\nand any tabs after that are actual source indentation.\n\nLong-line continuation markers still work the same way. They now use the\nsame two-space separator:\n\n```text\n  2  first wrapped chunk\n2.1  second wrapped chunk\n2.2  third wrapped chunk\n```\n\nThe file contents, line numbers, pagination behavior, and\ncontinuation-marker semantics are unchanged. Only the raw text\nformatting of the line-number gutter changes.","tree":{"sha":"7d9922c4e697dc5fb484589635f0c5819359df65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7d9922c4e697dc5fb484589635f0c5819359df65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cf057b4bcdb77ad67014f7dabe71e71f2366c95e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVa88CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqQAQAKkKba1N2sQwSb3p5SSfL7tZ\n3QIDmRVvBq+crC2TMTSg3+UvwFSZTRIIdeyBY/VZG8EHVNvAae/OeL4x4+wYQ04d\nw7U7rlEXGQ+V/5rlQH2Gc8lveKplDN7qZ5UCaiULQL/3yC+3vtW+BsjNP/I4QPuE\n3bFJ9MkZFbkjuLmrYICHfCvKUyTqDpQfwQjvbTfSHFG7LJeP+2CSaAFczuR4nZmk\nfxv2wIEq53SCQHD7htwSkWrNYFLGJuteX6PLvN/hVhfs6OeaMckTEOOQ8ygwkXKR\nlM6+HkRyVAkO59e62n7MZsodcmbqNGy7amHOtygct7/jbtOXmbL4tg7t0+knUq8i\nD+pB12grKDxbg3WabzXeiG4EzuATkArSOD1cL/kM1Vz1LClEt3iCkc6LerqaJdx1\nRiICVAt9Xdlbsbyq8cjv6WTaMv5NKxmO91ZvHmqWXFhHkiIvnLKNkQpL2/6e1A42\nDsJ5n+Nsy1G1i83yOeKA6EcL6iCCUvUTwt2hvC4CafAr0T5ub06vt/jaz919MJWw\nqL5tODDpq/bWKIV5ZceSzLgLpHaiW1rQtmB02QL0FkHVqtaVhqmRghxwhSvwQKLn\nnU6GEKerkrIEhQAOHtJZDRWLmPIy5p/+qPLz0NSsnhCvZGN6PwdooxE5hTJBEue9\nd66XbSu6Rg5m2WDJ8Jfo\n=wL4d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7d9922c4e697dc5fb484589635f0c5819359df65\nparent 718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784000316 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784000316 -0400\n\nfix(sdk)!: disambiguate `read_file` line gutters (#4561)\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> This is a breaking change for callers that parse raw `read_file`\noutput. The line-number gutter no longer uses `cat -n`-style padding and\na tab separator; parsers should expect line markers followed by two\nspaces before the source content.\n\n`read_file` returns file contents with line numbers so agents can\nreference and edit specific lines. Before this PR, those line numbers\nwere rendered like `cat -n`: a fixed-width line-number gutter followed\nby a tab.\n\nBefore:\n\n```text\n     1\tdef build_config():\n     2\t\treturn {\"enabled\": True}\n```\n\nThat format is hard to interpret when the source line itself starts with\na tab. In the example above, line 2 has two tabs in a row: one tab from\nthe `read_file` gutter and one tab from the source indentation. A model\ncan mistake both tabs for source content, then send an over-indented\n`old_string` to `edit_file`.\n\nThis PR changes the SDK formatter so the line marker is followed by two\nspaces before the original source content.\n\nAfter:\n\n```text\n1  def build_config():\n2  \treturn {\"enabled\": True}\n```\n\nNow the gutter is visually and textually distinct from the file\ncontents: the first two spaces separate the line marker from the source,\nand any tabs after that are actual source indentation.\n\nLong-line continuation markers still work the same way. They now use the\nsame two-space separator:\n\n```text\n  2  first wrapped chunk\n2.1  second wrapped chunk\n2.2  third wrapped chunk\n```\n\nThe file contents, line numbers, pagination behavior, and\ncontinuation-marker semantics are unchanged. Only the raw text\nformatting of the line-number gutter changes.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T03:38:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf057b4bcdb77ad67014f7dabe71e71f2366c95e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf057b4bcdb77ad67014f7dabe71e71f2366c95e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf057b4bcdb77ad67014f7dabe71e71f2366c95e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c"}]},{"sha":"718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcxOGM2NTJiNTc3NTBjYjNkOTI5YzE2YjdmYjQ1MDlkZjRlM2EwMGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T03:37:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T03:37:55Z"},"message":"chore(code): remove Debug Console startup tip (#4712)\n\nRemoves the `Press Ctrl+\\ to open the Debug Console and inspect session\nstate and logs` entry from the startup tip registry (`_TIPS`) in\n`startup_tip.py`. The Debug Console feature and its `Ctrl+\\` keybinding\nare unchanged — only the splash-screen tip advertising it is dropped.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0702cd28-7b3a-abc2-3e0c-1338cf5102e6)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"20228b1ce74baeda3a895791dc73145a18da1d4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/20228b1ce74baeda3a895791dc73145a18da1d4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVa8TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiisQAFbI73dkMx80WQLRqWzA3Y91\nu3VQrIrrHPBVOgMgi2Ozg+CPhB5KYKU5/tUHIbuvMfvvylc7ndyZqzsRpZ1UlgGx\ndpOZ3v9IK4gQlpIg2ERnBZoce0BIsbbDEs0eakBZ+qkNutNlNd6ECkO2utvEuLi9\n6WkMd3VxYYuPBvkx25u20q9fWX59H58KNwR7HalQBJx3bYY796GskvNX41U30GwC\nr0wKSXD+tqrsxAKzQ3ydUCEx468lH89mB6+cu0YZybeF/7eHw1lisUe4J9+Vwvct\n/6KJS69KJpL9YlJ27RAFkK0DSPFWPHi3lypZOOOuiEI5XuOce8OypnZhmyZtF/Zv\ntrEdYSs/AdSZ7MKDNGw/QN048u+Bv7eyR/9xzK37rimOK1PVpF75RfL3T1Kn76S6\nTeS5kv4vKZ90GVitNA8nbMWxk61Q1zW9CxF8H7jVOqUmTlA2y2U0S2QU18SQsB47\n6lKvp6BZrvROZkyqq68goNJYPFfIZzIvGdN8jGVga1D14GlNu8jCnJXg30qm5bcP\nwbYJ2CaW+Nef9wqkDwZX/tyd28A0N7rY8sd30U71impfguUa21sJlyCs9EZPLyCJ\nYnkXrXRFqN+p+25W7k8FgufFSJcpwaulVTZW+rjnBRvzgmUrTCc/CkpcnxDRi623\nQBxtnQhi8lbCFDbxtiuW\n=LzrB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 20228b1ce74baeda3a895791dc73145a18da1d4d\nparent 83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1784000275 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784000275 -0400\n\nchore(code): remove Debug Console startup tip (#4712)\n\nRemoves the `Press Ctrl+\\ to open the Debug Console and inspect session\nstate and logs` entry from the startup tip registry (`_TIPS`) in\n`startup_tip.py`. The Debug Console feature and its `Ctrl+\\` keybinding\nare unchanged — only the splash-screen tip advertising it is dropped.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0702cd28-7b3a-abc2-3e0c-1338cf5102e6)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-14T03:37:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/718c652b57750cb3d929c16b7fb4509df4e3a00c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504"}]},{"sha":"83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgzMjExOTQwYTJjZGY0YzUyYWMyMWE2Y2RlODY0NzcxNmE5OTg1MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-14T03:26:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-14T03:26:16Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): report remaining lines for paginated reads (#4540)\n\nCloses #2142\n\nCredit to @kevinWangSheng for making an earlier attempt at this!\n\n`read_file` now reports when a paginated read returns only part of a\ntext file, including the source-line range returned, total line count,\nremaining line count, and next offset to pass for the following page.\n\nExternal backends implementing the current `BackendProtocol` continue to\nwork unchanged.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, callers could request a limited window and receive\nline-numbered content, but they had to infer whether more lines existed\nand what offset would resume the read. That was especially fragile for\nsandboxed reads that can be byte-capped before the requested line window\nis fully rendered.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Extended `ReadResult` with optional pagination metadata for the\nreturned source-line range, total line count, and next offset. The\nexisting error and file-data fields remain unchanged, so external\nbackends do not need to adopt the new metadata immediately.\n- Updated the built-in state, store, filesystem, and sandbox backends to\npopulate that metadata for text reads. Sandbox-backed reads keep line\ncounting bounded for large files and avoid advancing past content hidden\nby output-size limits.\n- Updated `FilesystemMiddleware` to turn the metadata into the\nmodel-facing notice. If its own token limit shortens the result further,\nit recalculates the visible range and resume offset so subsequent reads\ndo not skip lines.\n- Added backend and middleware coverage for partial reads, EOF, offsets,\noutput truncation, and compatibility, plus an end-to-end eval for the\nresulting agent behavior.\n\n## Example output\n\nA partial read now includes the returned line range, total line count,\nand next offset:\n\n```text\n     1\tone\n     2\ttwo\n\n[Read 2 lines (lines 1-2 of 5 total). 3 lines remaining from offset 2.]\n```\n\nOffset reads report the original source-line range instead of starting\nthe notice from line 1:\n\n```text\n     3\tthree\n     4\tfour\n\n[Read 2 lines (lines 3-4 of 5 total). 1 line remaining from offset 4.]\n```\n\nReads that reach EOF keep the existing output shape and omit the footer:\n\n```text\n     1\tone\n     2\ttwo\n     3\tthree\n```\n\n## Evaluation\n\nThe `test_read_file_remaining_lines_notice_enables_tail_jump` eval asks\nthe agent to find the last non-empty line of a 301-line file using\n`read_file` directly. The target value is outside the first 100-line\npage, so the agent must determine where to read next.\n\nBoth `main` and this PR returned the correct value. With the\nremaining-line notice, both tested models used the first page's metadata\nto jump near the tail in one additional read:\n\n| Model | Version | Agent steps | Tool calls | Duration |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| GPT-5.5 | `main` | 4 | 6 | 13.1s |\n| GPT-5.5 | This PR | 3 | 2 | 8.4s |\n| Claude Sonnet 4.6 | `main` | 4 | 3 | 8.1s |\n| Claude Sonnet 4.6 | This PR | 3 | 2 | 5.5s |\n\nAcross three additional runs per model and version, this PR used exactly\ntwo tool calls in all six runs, while `main` required three to six\ncalls. The eval preserves correctness as a hard requirement and records\nthree agent steps, two tool calls, and two direct `read_file` calls as\nthe expected efficient trajectory.","tree":{"sha":"301d9bf8928548da9e2ac4ac45fb22e6dfa9bf9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/301d9bf8928548da9e2ac4ac45fb22e6dfa9bf9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVaxYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlK8QAJP1bJ537aJa3tZ6o+1CS03Q\n81eNoIS31gub8G15zfGO5hYY0nDH7a66E5bjrkuChdXILZAT02pvHO57PjMJ23zL\nd685vRRR/C5Jm2k5UB7/EFhzpByTqog4FmVSJhg8fqo/QqEaiJT7dTu/WnfQvIeb\ncaUHxq5Qs78RxcDmsCi/3v4jYxIK6nECV+6UAXrKLrcu+6Zi+5C+eKxunItF2FUF\nKRDyz3EaRjv21eUMhwmpJvxlcyFpvwlOn+tXXkUQOqhhibl9JmHCgt4o3i++9onM\nBkExLmvXsb2fhiwlWl90COkbtsb4On/Tfqs74Qn7iyxYfTIVRRT7UMLZ9EUAO0+u\niIzv9pIlGEXJ1faGPnG3sDSlLk0QISyEpptLteZ6ExUzbmwvf3wbSbW8e95FtXug\nL6sZ98wUodNtJp4DxVbcugwXzE0YYHcLD6oXnDv0HJbQQ4uUxosul0c/0j8yaFCm\nN9HueynhkoKqPd+MnZsaeZbBy+PQ9oxzIpkp8Kjt22UQ69RzJ8wV4Yj+sBlXxrIT\n0N8eetTeCLaA76PhsyyrpR6ri06HjQ8JBAmcpPXuLMS9MBYJ0Y91FxG9m8N7zbIu\n87plnA5PyNPv3QGYsQdJjZPJNI1eCCB5h+T7/7OWrmG8pQ/Fzk61V/vK870fhS4L\nC5vk5Ss6On0/KBpAGprb\n=Gw0J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 301d9bf8928548da9e2ac4ac45fb22e6dfa9bf9e\nparent 2678b1680d8928e72e8efae00632a694c9b2737a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783999576 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783999576 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): report remaining lines for paginated reads (#4540)\n\nCloses #2142\n\nCredit to @kevinWangSheng for making an earlier attempt at this!\n\n`read_file` now reports when a paginated read returns only part of a\ntext file, including the source-line range returned, total line count,\nremaining line count, and next offset to pass for the following page.\n\nExternal backends implementing the current `BackendProtocol` continue to\nwork unchanged.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, callers could request a limited window and receive\nline-numbered content, but they had to infer whether more lines existed\nand what offset would resume the read. That was especially fragile for\nsandboxed reads that can be byte-capped before the requested line window\nis fully rendered.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Extended `ReadResult` with optional pagination metadata for the\nreturned source-line range, total line count, and next offset. The\nexisting error and file-data fields remain unchanged, so external\nbackends do not need to adopt the new metadata immediately.\n- Updated the built-in state, store, filesystem, and sandbox backends to\npopulate that metadata for text reads. Sandbox-backed reads keep line\ncounting bounded for large files and avoid advancing past content hidden\nby output-size limits.\n- Updated `FilesystemMiddleware` to turn the metadata into the\nmodel-facing notice. If its own token limit shortens the result further,\nit recalculates the visible range and resume offset so subsequent reads\ndo not skip lines.\n- Added backend and middleware coverage for partial reads, EOF, offsets,\noutput truncation, and compatibility, plus an end-to-end eval for the\nresulting agent behavior.\n\n## Example output\n\nA partial read now includes the returned line range, total line count,\nand next offset:\n\n```text\n     1\tone\n     2\ttwo\n\n[Read 2 lines (lines 1-2 of 5 total). 3 lines remaining from offset 2.]\n```\n\nOffset reads report the original source-line range instead of starting\nthe notice from line 1:\n\n```text\n     3\tthree\n     4\tfour\n\n[Read 2 lines (lines 3-4 of 5 total). 1 line remaining from offset 4.]\n```\n\nReads that reach EOF keep the existing output shape and omit the footer:\n\n```text\n     1\tone\n     2\ttwo\n     3\tthree\n```\n\n## Evaluation\n\nThe `test_read_file_remaining_lines_notice_enables_tail_jump` eval asks\nthe agent to find the last non-empty line of a 301-line file using\n`read_file` directly. The target value is outside the first 100-line\npage, so the agent must determine where to read next.\n\nBoth `main` and this PR returned the correct value. With the\nremaining-line notice, both tested models used the first page's metadata\nto jump near the tail in one additional read:\n\n| Model | Version | Agent steps | Tool calls | Duration |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| GPT-5.5 | `main` | 4 | 6 | 13.1s |\n| GPT-5.5 | This PR | 3 | 2 | 8.4s |\n| Claude Sonnet 4.6 | `main` | 4 | 3 | 8.1s |\n| Claude Sonnet 4.6 | This PR | 3 | 2 | 5.5s |\n\nAcross three additional runs per model and version, this PR used exactly\ntwo tool calls in all six runs, while `main` required three to six\ncalls. The eval preserves correctness as a hard requirement and records\nthree agent steps, two tool calls, and two direct `read_file` calls as\nthe expected efficient trajectory.","verified_at":"2026-07-14T03:26:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/83211940a2cdf4c52ac21a6cde8647716a998504/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"