pagents/issues/4650))\n([70829c5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b))\n* Set `prompt_cache_key` for OpenAI models\n([#4632](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4632))\n([8cf57ac](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d))\n* Support Fireworks `/routers` model ids\n([#4591](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4591))\n([1c08d27](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1))\n* `/model` Ctrl+N toggle for names vs raw specs\n([#4592](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4592))\n([518c322](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f))\n* `/tools` slash command\n([#4649](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4649))\n([b1600a8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c))\n* Add `-s` alias for `--skill`\n([#4620](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4620))\n([c9b7ac2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87))\n* Configurable chat cursor style\n([#4687](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4687))\n([a22484b](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3))\n* Expand environment variables in MCP config\n([#4681](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4681))\n([4f5d7be](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860))\n* Hide diff widget for credential files\n([#4593](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4593))\n([4c49a24](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596))\n* In-app Debug Console\n([#4564](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4564))\n([4f94a30](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043))\n* Offer abort in `/threads` cwd-switch prompt\n([#4583](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4583))\n([aaeac99](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870))\n* Resume threads in-TUI with `/threads -r [ID]`\n([#4609](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4609))\n([d442673](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da))\n* Show `(debug enabled)` on splash when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set\n([#4584](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4584))\n([f10b877](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Avoid repeated startup auto-update stalls\n([#4648](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4648))\n([12a9c9d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12a9c9d6813a83e5eeff9feed0c4068d1fcc69c4))\n* Infer Fireworks provider from qualified model IDs\n([#4594](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4594))\n([4d2aa8a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea))\n* Capture input typed before TUI startup\n([#4684](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4684))\n([ef9a4a8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2))\n* Detach owned `langgraph dev` server from terminal\n([#4642](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4642))\n([d1f3afe](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417))\n* Infer additional model providers\n([#4675](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4675))\n([4ceed24](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1))\n* Preserve `Ctrl+D` deletion in non-empty input\n([#4626](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4626))\n([306bd89](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/306bd893f214237b6b4eede7c2ce0eaff66f5527))\n* Quit with `Ctrl+D` at end of prompt\n([#4678](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4678))\n([2f8c111](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02))\n* Reap langgraph dev server when startup is cancelled\n([#4629](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4629))\n([904ff05](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4))\n* Reject `--auto-approve` in headless mode\n([#4617](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4617))\n([997be16](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/997be1643aff6d6900b8b8c95832cdf93be8c0d7))\n* Route explicit `--stdin` + `--skill` to headless path\n([#4611](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4611))\n([724e24a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595))\n* Skip Esc prompt-restore once output generation begins\n([#4582](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4582))\n([14f384f](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f))\n* Remove misleading agent names from help\n([#4671](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4671))\n([ac15732](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b))\n* Support plain `exit` quit command\n([#4543](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4543))\n([e6f10a1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e6f10a149051128677c9f6f37663922054a7ac26))\n* Sync `ask_user` active-question highlight with focus\n([#4599](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4599))\n([e4c29b5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb))\n* Wrap MCP viewer navigation\n([#4677](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4677))\n([cffc732](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca))\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n* Load MCP servers concurrently during graph build\n([#4659](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4659))\n([c5345cc](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020))\n\n---\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T15:08:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/def6369aed1a8dcb857db52285fa2e8976bdcd07","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/def6369aed1a8dcb857db52285fa2e8976bdcd07","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/def6369aed1a8dcb857db52285fa2e8976bdcd07/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875"}]},{"sha":"68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY4OTM2YzkzNTM4ZDMyOTdhYzExNjdlZTYyMDRmMzNhYTUzYmM4NzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T14:50:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T14:50:05Z"},"message":"ci(infra): run CodSpeed benchmarks nightly only (#4689)\n\nFollowing #4686\n\n---\n\nCodSpeed reports exhausted macro-runner budgets through a separate\nGitHub App check before the Actions job starts. Marking the job with\n`continue-on-error` therefore cannot make that check advisory: pull\nrequests still show `CodSpeed Macro Runners — Macro Runners budget\nexceeded`, and the benchmark jobs remain queued.\n\nRun macro benchmarks only from the scheduled or manually dispatched\nnightly workflow. This preserves strict wall-time measurements on\nCodSpeed's dedicated runners while removing macro-runner requests from\npull request and normal push CI.\n\nThis trades per-PR macro reports for predictable runner usage and\npost-merge nightly regression detection.","tree":{"sha":"3f822dad1fa4152dd4c247466316dabdc68b1cb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3f822dad1fa4152dd4c247466316dabdc68b1cb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVPsdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/y8QAFaECDdC55hl6Lc7pEIjBhFh\npeDxFMkfYYzSmLw67Agh3iBcu4npP3ca5ig1WtFgG+vSm9Vg+GWoUNCppo+0xWTb\nM73ZBIEgZEnPoycoFEuLbwaN/3DK+8FOtmOMYtPBTnc9ELkDiYDWoW/PXn3VLt9A\nVIiuqvjKKLjuBjFxKC6hXQZ9ACRr27iaJk268Xv+2FMDqiCtBpYOJEbKc1ltaWe0\nb8zdXy9bnBHTpyoyrGo13hjzV+ZZr2jCXatXSDX4NkwMNHebQkyv7EIgnjmWvrt5\nWLcEABTImsR8T9IcGp4ORWm/7fG7Us3o81uS4nwPoZAjJnJkf+LN72ECSVBlMy1Q\n2xdBektqqqiH05HUAhXsUyRMvyS14VUIxxWV20BueNsLwbUY+FnxwmUYa/DdUrAJ\nBOqIaZHH/JqCWMHqNMW1wS6gr80THyOv2HW6ppKvAXeLEQnd8G/VZ/yOmgeZMtT3\n9n5zPQXmk+qZwusA1Q0VU0ZZAgrZECQao65pBwl+Pxw8/LEIqrrB4Lv/i1I1jAek\no+CIspFYOaGDUWmbBaRI9h0L31ipvSGfiLGjzuBrD46VumMHl3P5o58YRXa32fWX\nf9IE5yeYUDulxihYDE10IrBppVA27GQX7AsnSKKs8MV+GJ/Q0VB+ir2APXySkU7v\nCa70TQe8AdcU94qA78+Q\n=ruVV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3f822dad1fa4152dd4c247466316dabdc68b1cb9\nparent 4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783954205 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783954205 -0400\n\nci(infra): run CodSpeed benchmarks nightly only (#4689)\n\nFollowing #4686\n\n---\n\nCodSpeed reports exhausted macro-runner budgets through a separate\nGitHub App check before the Actions job starts. Marking the job with\n`continue-on-error` therefore cannot make that check advisory: pull\nrequests still show `CodSpeed Macro Runners — Macro Runners budget\nexceeded`, and the benchmark jobs remain queued.\n\nRun macro benchmarks only from the scheduled or manually dispatched\nnightly workflow. This preserves strict wall-time measurements on\nCodSpeed's dedicated runners while removing macro-runner requests from\npull request and normal push CI.\n\nThis trades per-PR macro reports for predictable runner usage and\npost-merge nightly regression detection.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T14:50:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68936c93538d3297ac1167ee6204f33aa53bc875/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860"}]},{"sha":"4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRmNWQ3YmUxYjQwNzNkZWUzNDZlNWE5NzQ4NDE3MjE2NDZmYTQ4NjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T14:23:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T14:23:45Z"},"message":"feat(code): expand environment variables in MCP config (#4681)\n\nDeep Agents Code now expands `${VAR}` and `${VAR:-default}` references\nin `.mcp.json` server commands, arguments, environment values, URLs, and\nheaders.\n\n---\n\nUsers who share `.mcp.json` files currently have to hard-code\nmachine-specific paths and credentials outside remote headers. This\nmakes otherwise portable MCP configuration fail for stdio servers and\nremote URLs.\n\nThis resolves `${VAR}` and `${VAR:-default}` in `command`, `args`,\n`env`, `url`, and `headers` when each server activates. Missing or\nmalformed references report the exact config field and disable only the\naffected server. OAuth login follows the same behavior.\n\nExpansion remains behind the existing project MCP trust checks, so\nunapproved project configuration cannot read environment values or\ninitiate connections.","tree":{"sha":"1d7bc51d43fbd6cd2229215929ac1764d97402c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1d7bc51d43fbd6cd2229215929ac1764d97402c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVPTxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMu8QAJRc3gvIVoSQE9i9Cey5cZYR\ncsaXuJr9NZ1zmywK3ep8Td2OTd6L6rwSCe0FOAAUpiAsDK0EgNaPG9J0/wRCtqDe\npSorDaEoRZoQdMW+XkBdhOCySYaaspDCMTC6RvRRIykdUe9FglyB2BgWeIiXB4Uo\njCIZBB8Anvc5G+yzS20X8f8YaXsnNPh40M5kNGyu683eB/04Bei7y0UBkvliGR8R\nMrX9A71O0twoEu9IuaFHpapNXnPq6YT7L9Nw8vF9HdCxlPGaqztjBoCYhzERozAY\nmNTuj8hqBkqHwFep1Qk459IhytgN3RJbpjaxOtBPi9ZStCZ7cwcc1k1pdQu6HKoy\ncF4prM/Hu9lSMRMi7aCCRePeS6qhqEan5zCHxDEYL2yq8u1NpdmcYSDDe6KMRYiq\nMUk4qkHqPqXDBeFkMJmMd7Dyv7QvMamS9Fjgbl7CrOoJF4qiOWFg3tUDI6WVcO2B\npNa2JqTnRAb9Rd32JGwA4ds58ncs/wIx9wXq8QsjI9UNDFFas73vzd0lH2AbKSb0\nRsNKTjKa6lmRZ6bbUcxUxCB5YNTDlL9k9CC+J5CGR99cerMq4A1K3Y8j8EDbyWru\nA/JphuRydCYMkqd6IqnBwivi26oycIudEbIqe3SNymRZjbMglDSuhFGdvg9Af+Yq\nXcpf27z1LeCgyPKMRm52\n=dxcg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1d7bc51d43fbd6cd2229215929ac1764d97402c1\nparent a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783952625 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783952625 -0400\n\nfeat(code): expand environment variables in MCP config (#4681)\n\nDeep Agents Code now expands `${VAR}` and `${VAR:-default}` references\nin `.mcp.json` server commands, arguments, environment values, URLs, and\nheaders.\n\n---\n\nUsers who share `.mcp.json` files currently have to hard-code\nmachine-specific paths and credentials outside remote headers. This\nmakes otherwise portable MCP configuration fail for stdio servers and\nremote URLs.\n\nThis resolves `${VAR}` and `${VAR:-default}` in `command`, `args`,\n`env`, `url`, and `headers` when each server activates. Missing or\nmalformed references report the exact config field and disable only the\naffected server. OAuth login follows the same behavior.\n\nExpansion remains behind the existing project MCP trust checks, so\nunapproved project configuration cannot read environment values or\ninitiate connections.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T14:23:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f5d7be1b4073dee346e5a974841721646fa4860/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3"}]},{"sha":"a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEyMjQ4NGJhMmUwMDFmZDYyZmJmZjBmZTkxNmYxYjNiOTM4ODlmYzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T14:23:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T14:23:37Z"},"message":"feat(code): add configurable chat cursor style (#4687)\n\nDeep Agents Code now supports `block` and `underline` chat input cursor\nstyles through `[ui].cursor_style` or `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_CURSOR_STYLE`.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code previously rendered the chat input cursor as a block\nwith no way to change its shape. Users can now choose an underlined\ncursor while preserving the block cursor as the default.\n\nThe preference can be saved in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`:\n\n    [ui]\n    cursor_style = \"underline\"\n\nIt can also be set for a process with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_CURSOR_STYLE=underline`. The environment variable takes\nprecedence over the saved preference. Both sources accept `block` and\n`underline`; invalid values fall through to the saved preference and\nthen the default block cursor.","tree":{"sha":"dc1d5f53630dc17e158069436eda6b572b017883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dc1d5f53630dc17e158069436eda6b572b017883"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVPTpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW2YQAI9dib8jpZs+n+ckbJGqh5mE\n31Hpiu3gwUIkUKLMQVxfdqAn8Oanekyto2JWip0Bohrv2dF5WpqjzK7JTxlMgTwQ\nzBoB0SR5ki8043o0nOtn9iqfakSj15MOnd/96zEup8QJjZIbQRJXbkxmrfr+SJaQ\n71YAMlZO9cb+5CB6uU0osvYCw2UjYivo+4f43TF0wqKfu0ygJ0IyvFzROzrOVvWN\nEIWmCD4jHFRscP6MfxoNTeoa3cmELRzwW5gWfEzngs9fFJhrVa+qpEtU6Jba3boP\nQh1h97lvraJWMRMtnRVupRYx6HPGztt24PW4/pxtJcHKnl+4TvwZth5V6bazQq0B\neWhW2Ec0T07pRfoFCGNLuz2J48cXSVjWwnuNxLt7K/a26GOjt3cg6AcBDShYDqdt\nESqBn8acmzL/+uXFW87r0OjB8rMfjx2TQlJGTf0ZPCUjyW/rN09NBallbSyNBF+l\nfUk2nqgUMfi2YeehhiBGBFKceiXxn8y2zHkv8A5xDD7ZvbK9DYg1lwpM0SHJvLTz\nYG+R8YXjzWXHWVAW3C6W797sfojbmcYHV7BGZDTZHPuDAmzXQfIlqr73B2qlQpzc\n9CrfBobkqPy64VpTwq/uuAxXTiZm7iRnsh//ouYgKQmNkYI89hKZzYPYqGnnYEym\nZcSTaFhyp0ZgjhYZwRZj\n=/D7T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dc1d5f53630dc17e158069436eda6b572b017883\nparent 2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783952617 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783952617 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add configurable chat cursor style (#4687)\n\nDeep Agents Code now supports `block` and `underline` chat input cursor\nstyles through `[ui].cursor_style` or `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_CURSOR_STYLE`.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code previously rendered the chat input cursor as a block\nwith no way to change its shape. Users can now choose an underlined\ncursor while preserving the block cursor as the default.\n\nThe preference can be saved in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`:\n\n    [ui]\n    cursor_style = \"underline\"\n\nIt can also be set for a process with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_CURSOR_STYLE=underline`. The environment variable takes\nprecedence over the saved preference. Both sources accept `block` and\n`underline`; invalid values fall through to the saved preference and\nthen the default block cursor.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T14:23:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a22484ba2e001fd62fbff0fe916f1b3b93889fc3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e"}]},{"sha":"2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJjNmIxNDc2NzZkZDc0ODg0YTU1ZTY4YjhiOGRlOGI0ODBhNDM0NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T14:15:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T14:15:07Z"},"message":"ci(infra): make CodSpeed benchmarks advisory (#4686)\n\nCodSpeed jobs are intentionally excluded from the required `✅ CI\nSuccess` aggregation, but a benchmark failure still marks the overall CI\nworkflow as failed.\n\nThis makes the regular CI callers opt into advisory benchmark failures\nwhile preserving CodSpeed instrumentation and reporting. The reusable\nworkflow remains strict by default, so scheduled nightly benchmarks\ncontinue to surface failures.","tree":{"sha":"81ced4e9b7d410aedac786581aefba7fa13dbb40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/81ced4e9b7d410aedac786581aefba7fa13dbb40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVPLrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhRsQAH6x1cLlIcXOoe7YGm+QXxH8\noL+OG4kG6/hTDDkqD0znUQHKnRmLpNxvXiZXFunXF9lz3tya1VAd9JZEdvTp9UEu\n7gRHhiWfl7vKP/wdNGPWgPWkfq65qD9uouMoWPdx5beV31gI2dPFTwALO/qjrjoq\nwUp6ABIgY4kPFRXDRj4QLs04BTVkAcVbhYEh3z4YssStXa86oozg/IoWFUmSSQDs\nQQy6Ya8/pBC+4Kn0pAd1IfIlZD9akdQFYELF/kH5NWm9tFBZ9RDVItzRGVp0vaJb\nkfo7dX7b8XNdSpnQuUhmqxgMvY507wcDp6I5MVJ6q9wCLy+PKE11KGRKozh8nhpN\nwF5lQs71aZTGmhAUoloVnGCfqBGmu+uZmZWGGfFjHtIn8ZShJ7Js7/ivYcuE5qPV\nXlOz8jgmMQgKfkiyqZm8VaRlrydwdSGqCy9s0sTiXHDqcad+oHsl/kX0yxKoyefC\n9FedjOGT6xEvbuFcHHFL6XKjof91/k3IddtkXrLhAEgZQpR+fCpHesg3ORGiYhGl\nlX8364NSs17i68UBH2zx/p8HP24nAYZtjhDHf47nAbKmDnEsUlUPf4svm/ozg0eQ\nR2e0N/j1qBkXCz0+3JIZqFrIQJV0c+lvtrDd8uIaIaXfIXsg3DsgLW49D2fW2/Fr\nGG30JbvR2yoU1bVATQSG\n=zfJp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 81ced4e9b7d410aedac786581aefba7fa13dbb40\nparent ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783952107 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783952107 -0400\n\nci(infra): make CodSpeed benchmarks advisory (#4686)\n\nCodSpeed jobs are intentionally excluded from the required `✅ CI\nSuccess` aggregation, but a benchmark failure still marks the overall CI\nworkflow as failed.\n\nThis makes the regular CI callers opt into advisory benchmark failures\nwhile preserving CodSpeed instrumentation and reporting. The reusable\nworkflow remains strict by default, so scheduled nightly benchmarks\ncontinue to surface failures.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T14:15:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c6b147676dd74884a55e68b8b8de8b480a4345e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2"}]},{"sha":"ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVmOWE0YTg3NzBmNGRhZWM3MGU2NDBkNmQyZjIzZGQ3OThkNGVkZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T14:07:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T14:07:47Z"},"message":"fix(code): capture input typed before TUI startup (#4684)\n\n`dcode` now preserves text typed immediately after launch and places it\nin the chat input when the TUI appears.\n\n---\n\nWhen `dcode` starts, terminal input typed before the first TUI frame is\nalready queued for Textual. The default screen initially focused the\nchat scroll container because it appears before the input in the widget\ntree, so those queued keys were delivered to the scroll container and\ndisappeared.\n\nThe main chat screen now selects the chat input during Textual's initial\nautofocus pass. The selector is scoped to the main screen so modal\nscreens retain their normal first-focusable control and keyboard\nnavigation.","tree":{"sha":"0c3124f41db2e6954e9d7a5a0cc218d72a6d39e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0c3124f41db2e6954e9d7a5a0cc218d72a6d39e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVPEzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx8sQAIX6HAsvm5irZ7G4AILHm6Pg\nO00im13mS407kc66nmjIwCw+XQO5+rDTodUSfpshR2RTI4sKVMHINrEmQhNgYdqq\nxw8QJrIpo3wfVHncjELUVOx62PpQX6O67hXdsj6NmHGsOVC4vXZ6PER0C/uMhGeg\nisOMWT2ckUN4pRL1OYYOsXKNDKQ9UvTAEmk64sXMjGX34gPMD56Ssdaid/wkBTN8\nuyZRRoDD/AdXsgOt6BNguQ+Jm1gi8Gjpn7NtC/vB8moAbI+F0dD4ZS39GqoaiwUS\nMLFLPwb4Aq/IqCQMr1uO0B1RM4939NL9Qd0uTjLnnTP0eb3MAjaMBZxpPbnsLvZB\nSLX3kk/zRs/U8hB1zWr9BUKxvmSp0zqZI2gPR4WYXPyWpwEN8Vh+L1cTScxbffDN\n254I3CT1KSTtwhm6lPdwj4QhUfUn+ZZwNNngt4g7OksJVTe20e7yitBsDWc+On56\n4rXOJQRi8TwpFXsKKO9+VyjUXh+xZt6G5PqewdaMfQbqmVrjHTFV8txeZQGdyRi1\n18NV1sOCasZUjt5nW6YEJcxxHxioYvuN/Y7vnXcBcFwhGY4vjcyKkV2jZmW43O7Q\nxQtrtZ1I+C9HB/nX5GO+h4CQi32gHZY3Ixh34qnfE2q+PZTmIwdrMcRdUi18+/KP\nVv477Xv7x3zpu1DGLu+e\n=Te5a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0c3124f41db2e6954e9d7a5a0cc218d72a6d39e8\nparent e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783951667 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783951667 -0400\n\nfix(code): capture input typed before TUI startup (#4684)\n\n`dcode` now preserves text typed immediately after launch and places it\nin the chat input when the TUI appears.\n\n---\n\nWhen `dcode` starts, terminal input typed before the first TUI frame is\nalready queued for Textual. The default screen initially focused the\nchat scroll container because it appears before the input in the widget\ntree, so those queued keys were delivered to the scroll container and\ndisappeared.\n\nThe main chat screen now selects the chat input during Textual's initial\nautofocus pass. The selector is scoped to the main screen so modal\nscreens retain their normal first-focusable control and keyboard\nnavigation.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T14:07:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ef9a4a8770f4daec70e640d6d2f23dd798d4ede2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb"}]},{"sha":"e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU0YzI5YjUyNjQ0MTNkMjNkOGRjNzBjYWJhZTcyZmViNWYzZjNkY2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T13:59:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T13:59:47Z"},"message":"fix(code): sync `ask_user` active-question highlight with focus (#4599)\n\nFixed the interactive `ask_user` prompt so the active-question highlight\nfollows mouse clicks — clicking a question now highlights it instead of\nleaving a different question highlighted while you interact.\n\n---\n\nThe `ask_user` widget highlights one active question and dims the rest,\nbut the highlight was driven only by keyboard/programmatic navigation\n(`_set_active_question`). Clicking a dimmed question moved focus into\nits input or choice list without updating the highlight, so a user could\nnavigate choices or type free text in a question while a *different*\nquestion stayed highlighted.\n\nThis makes the highlight follow focus. The class-toggling logic is split\nout of `_set_active_question` into a focus-neutral\n`_highlight_question`, and a new `on_descendant_focus` handler on\n`AskUserMenu` walks up to the enclosing question and re-highlights it\nwhen focus lands there. It deliberately does not move focus, so the\nwidget the user clicked keeps focus; it's idempotent when the focused\nquestion is already active.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/60f8a2c3-89ae-482f-26f0-bbed49bf671d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"159e6c4daa903338f51392c5ae9bf45277cbfc75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/159e6c4daa903338f51392c5ae9bf45277cbfc75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVO9TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhXkQAJhAaRuGV9PNwSvHTYysNykX\nRnlez8rFa6wiTWEeVY4P5qe1+TU99uutLG1agM6i5REIN8FV9elc0xRr6vISv+BN\nGc0TRoT5P4R4o1zWhjqB7od34DFYxzKDz7Mapeav5SaKEYDKIsEdfUUtSIWopmCC\nDV/NFayqEcdDJs8TLQ6f2LLzZ9cpQCntl9L3qCdqDcFXDufYrPQ8uD/YV1i7OWfA\nkyVPDWQ75znUGehYVnt2jPjDqRzi9hQXsJGrDqRkZ3y6DuFbiFWiC3gQ5DtWwtxm\nHy+hMWqFZMwK+4OqwOpDw12ZWSXXp+6ilTb1QAGqTVXRrUmWpvvUOqjbtMqteOLR\nA9otztwaxLCmYOp5Hhi/MulJg1CjgawB85CEg3+rXosLIcu01u2uworDCqo33tk7\nvvEX6rQ/AK6slqBJTSLDI2sHvR3CGDN9Rf1BCt7FsMGO6o1yNTaKqpA0sLTahigI\nwchCixxIRvygraQx3PfeoTH9Kd/SeF6PLkd669WMWXxe5rCg8VfgpRP4uGxY5uKU\n5qz4src9RgN+8racBnMuCZkRsjBn3IA5Iv5tsWTgAFhrI/c+whj9b6Ib+igweELx\nRaq8KkUEJ9Nm5dCt779/2NUrrxTocDAV962jfs/gGBRfqTywIrbkmEi4iv+u1zo7\nFk1/FexW5qsNZzKyRLTP\n=bXO6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 159e6c4daa903338f51392c5ae9bf45277cbfc75\nparent 724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783951187 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783951187 -0400\n\nfix(code): sync `ask_user` active-question highlight with focus (#4599)\n\nFixed the interactive `ask_user` prompt so the active-question highlight\nfollows mouse clicks — clicking a question now highlights it instead of\nleaving a different question highlighted while you interact.\n\n---\n\nThe `ask_user` widget highlights one active question and dims the rest,\nbut the highlight was driven only by keyboard/programmatic navigation\n(`_set_active_question`). Clicking a dimmed question moved focus into\nits input or choice list without updating the highlight, so a user could\nnavigate choices or type free text in a question while a *different*\nquestion stayed highlighted.\n\nThis makes the highlight follow focus. The class-toggling logic is split\nout of `_set_active_question` into a focus-neutral\n`_highlight_question`, and a new `on_descendant_focus` handler on\n`AskUserMenu` walks up to the enclosing question and re-highlights it\nwhen focus lands there. It deliberately does not move focus, so the\nwidget the user clicked keeps focus; it's idempotent when the focused\nquestion is already active.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/60f8a2c3-89ae-482f-26f0-bbed49bf671d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T13:59:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e4c29b5264413d23d8dc70cabae72feb5f3f3dcb/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595"}]},{"sha":"724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcyNGUyNGEzMTU0NmUxZjMxZmVjYTNiYjIzNDQ3MTc1NTA2ODI1OTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T13:52:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T13:52:59Z"},"message":"fix(code): route explicit `--stdin` + `--skill` to headless path (#4611)\n\n`dcode --skill ... --stdin` with piped input now runs headless instead\nof launching the interactive TUI.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user explicitly passes `--stdin` together with `--skill`, `dcode`\npreviously routed the piped text into the interactive TUI seed\n(`initial_prompt`), which hangs/fails on non-TTY environments.\n`apply_stdin_pipe` now skips the skill→interactive convenience when\n`--stdin` is explicit, falling through to the headless\n`non_interactive_message` path (which already supports `--skill`).\nAuto-detected pipes (no `--stdin`) keep the interactive seeding\nbehavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/057272c4-7946-e220-f7b8-ea929d2fe9ce)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b183d1a3367bc110feb416a5e61d4c1cdc5cb754","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b183d1a3367bc110feb416a5e61d4c1cdc5cb754"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVO28CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFC4QABtoL66pXg/3EOPaiAWSE6ye\n7251nyQZ74B1fYjbT+domXd03b+4M9UhaC9z5M8SuapNH9O3gjMjPkOAB3WmCPJB\npdmhBAKdoZidzIUbW6vrH0J1s60K/kqJtHQApNjOjQ0xR8Q7FHBYxLKQGd+Q+itc\ntTZ8cc1ygrZheyA+JpJ0NiEFfEVGwYNPmoTDwJQL6rNoT8kyuv+ZVrBFxCQYGSA0\neSIgoaulueaBcZ0rnlhk02KuHqixNpj4F+93ta0kgu4eKWEaTKxsP+DOQ6TnBoIs\nuTtFYUHokZU04cN3frL+IGEez0I1XVSIeRcOVn0L7rvNzxwIJNuR4R9/AtT43bRg\nrrc2u9qnsfccBlan3p3PUxbkSGYm2jlax//rCb+yOGlX4NBQzy4u3n/Ed2BENGXl\n+7/dHlAhuBajV2SNP2siWZ9dK37NrJESbtWrMViZF9lw6BOjEk5JzU3bABzatseA\nrJulAT2UXk8B2FMpe42qt7mYCVytUqh4u2iYY2nqUE4aoxJp87W8XhmJh5dfRb+T\nOgMujU9v5XNwIYhlo1IgXc/+TqbRJL5DKLONPX0AMvQgEvDNLxybK6QdtUXLpmlz\nDf8CvNVSioicIJ70XkZ5m5QCivYMdYVC2hzzTDmL4t1VoSx3c1kxtIXEvjNAUiNY\nRkVFGhiDU2RvLY++Lk7J\n=v4O3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b183d1a3367bc110feb416a5e61d4c1cdc5cb754\nparent 7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783950779 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783950779 -0400\n\nfix(code): route explicit `--stdin` + `--skill` to headless path (#4611)\n\n`dcode --skill ... --stdin` with piped input now runs headless instead\nof launching the interactive TUI.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user explicitly passes `--stdin` together with `--skill`, `dcode`\npreviously routed the piped text into the interactive TUI seed\n(`initial_prompt`), which hangs/fails on non-TTY environments.\n`apply_stdin_pipe` now skips the skill→interactive convenience when\n`--stdin` is explicit, falling through to the headless\n`non_interactive_message` path (which already supports `--skill`).\nAuto-detected pipes (no `--stdin`) keep the interactive seeding\nbehavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/057272c4-7946-e220-f7b8-ea929d2fe9ce)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T13:53:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/724e24a31546e1f31feca3bb2344717550682595/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc"}]},{"sha":"7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdhZGQ5MmQyMWMwNmZjMWJjYWJjNDk0OWJlYWRkYjBkNmYxZGI4Y2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T13:46:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T13:46:30Z"},"message":"ci(evals): add unified multi-model Harbor evals workflow (#4651)\n\nHarbor evaluations currently require a separate workflow dispatch for\neach model and benchmark. This makes cross-model comparisons cumbersome\nand leaves Harbor without the multi-model orchestration already\navailable in `evals.yml`.\n\nThis PR adds a unified Harbor entry point that accepts a comma-separated\nlist of `provider:model` IDs and any combination of the autonomous,\nconversation, and context categories.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| Each dispatch evaluated exactly one model. | One dispatch evaluates a\nlist of models. |\n| The dataset and agent implementation were selected manually for each\nrun. | Each category selects the appropriate benchmark and agent\nconfiguration automatically. |\n| Evaluating three categories across several models required a separate\nrun for every pair. | The workflow coordinates the complete model ×\ncategory matrix. |\n| Each run produced an independent result. | Results are combined into a\nleaderboard, JSON summary, and radar chart. |\n| Harbor execution was embedded in the single-model workflow. |\nSingle-model and unified dispatches share the same reusable Harbor\nexecution workflow. |\n\nThe categories map to the existing Harbor-backed evaluations:\n\n- **Autonomous:** Harbor Index with the dcode harness\n- **Conversation:** the tau3 subset with the conversational agent\n- **Context:** the context-retrieval evaluation with the dcode harness\n\nModels are grouped by provider so calls to a single provider are\nserialized while different providers can run in parallel. Per-model and\nglobal concurrency limits are enforced, and shard counts remain\nconfigurable by category. Each `(model × category)` pair is tracked in\nits own LangSmith dataset.\n\nThe final report includes pass@K and avg@K for each pair, a macro\noverall that weights categories equally, and a micro overall weighted by\ntask count. The expected model × category grid is retained so missing or\nincomplete runs are reported rather than silently omitted.\n\nThe existing single-model Harbor dispatch keeps its current interface.\nExtracting its execution into a reusable workflow is an enabling\nrefactor; multi-model, cross-category orchestration and combined\nreporting are the net-new functionality.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a8d23e93e48cba76424639038db932cad908fa1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5a8d23e93e48cba76424639038db932cad908fa1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVOw2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9VYQAIc3pfQ4PjNfTxuhbj8gxlNx\nimJuIZWRZZsi6RSZwnKjJ6CsE/WeSuxi8skPb2sIdA+KbxsbHCr1wAPBnCVJRz+k\nf/GjSlHP4QpzXKEmBK71+h0uNWHGbJ4f0FO0EIaRBsyADXqkHYACB5HdpM7t52x4\npv2cct+Zt0JAw/Mm8y6JwucIjc7P/tOO/suKIhTE4kUeo4VbNShHreI6VDHs/EqY\n4WNII4AKj2I9jRq5V+MlzFE51Zh/A0tkhEnC9XKeooBmfWsU318y5eadd3qBuVCD\nepdfF5Kv3AukbLtDA3zHCuXeJCv9b2fBqn1umVQ9Bw8wB9v5/mPGtnRJJkb+q+cj\nlOj1obPtfyttxigBVelUAzW1yA7W7ZC07YOpawXwcA0axLUXtQ+P1UnNb16abHux\nwfJFXnoUMdTbyAckgvGe3t9OhQWh1o20KYaON0ITdvmHyxvtbaF1IBIw1bWbK9of\nS0cCw5KW+tSJYqRZjCEt0NA3BrMUrhv1IkvEyfKpDlajqPBN+cKsrnKBHTt3BGpy\nmVSJ4pAl+iptk4CXdX/Q28lQNELwixA0aVOms8JB86bqyyu9xYiZMQ3gbM1YHbLu\nWIR1g71IqR1baLsggK8zWC/E3PGBWssTvOrFSiqmyNu1mAfKNB0etZeoyIvUF1Bc\nbRGS0H7wLjFynEgWz9tb\n=nFJS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5a8d23e93e48cba76424639038db932cad908fa1\nparent cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1783950390 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783950390 -0400\n\nci(evals): add unified multi-model Harbor evals workflow (#4651)\n\nHarbor evaluations currently require a separate workflow dispatch for\neach model and benchmark. This makes cross-model comparisons cumbersome\nand leaves Harbor without the multi-model orchestration already\navailable in `evals.yml`.\n\nThis PR adds a unified Harbor entry point that accepts a comma-separated\nlist of `provider:model` IDs and any combination of the autonomous,\nconversation, and context categories.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| Each dispatch evaluated exactly one model. | One dispatch evaluates a\nlist of models. |\n| The dataset and agent implementation were selected manually for each\nrun. | Each category selects the appropriate benchmark and agent\nconfiguration automatically. |\n| Evaluating three categories across several models required a separate\nrun for every pair. | The workflow coordinates the complete model ×\ncategory matrix. |\n| Each run produced an independent result. | Results are combined into a\nleaderboard, JSON summary, and radar chart. |\n| Harbor execution was embedded in the single-model workflow. |\nSingle-model and unified dispatches share the same reusable Harbor\nexecution workflow. |\n\nThe categories map to the existing Harbor-backed evaluations:\n\n- **Autonomous:** Harbor Index with the dcode harness\n- **Conversation:** the tau3 subset with the conversational agent\n- **Context:** the context-retrieval evaluation with the dcode harness\n\nModels are grouped by provider so calls to a single provider are\nserialized while different providers can run in parallel. Per-model and\nglobal concurrency limits are enforced, and shard counts remain\nconfigurable by category. Each `(model × category)` pair is tracked in\nits own LangSmith dataset.\n\nThe final report includes pass@K and avg@K for each pair, a macro\noverall that weights categories equally, and a micro overall weighted by\ntask count. The expected model × category grid is retained so missing or\nincomplete runs are reported rather than silently omitted.\n\nThe existing single-model Harbor dispatch keeps its current interface.\nExtracting its execution into a reusable workflow is an enabling\nrefactor; multi-model, cross-category orchestration and combined\nreporting are the net-new functionality.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T13:46:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7add92d21c06fc1bcabc4949beaddb0d6f1db8cc/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca"}]},{"sha":"cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNmZmM3MzIxM2JmZGNlYzI2Y2I4MmM0MTNmYTdlMjdkYjRhZmMwY2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T13:31:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T13:31:39Z"},"message":"fix(code): wrap MCP viewer navigation (#4677)\n\nMCP viewer keyboard navigation now wraps at list boundaries, with arrow\nkeys moving through every row and `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` moving between\nservers.\n\n---\n\nThe MCP viewer now lets users continue navigating at list boundaries\ninstead of reversing direction.\n\n`Up` and `Down` wrap through every displayed row, including server\nheaders and tools. `Tab` and `Shift+Tab` provide faster server-level\nnavigation by moving to the next or previous server header and wrapping\nat either end. From a tool, `Shift+Tab` returns to that tool's server\nheader, while `Tab` advances to the next server.\n\nThis also makes header-only lists—such as when every server has an\nerror—fully navigable with either set of keys.","tree":{"sha":"bd654eb5cb43208ef07e4c710bcb8c6b30657dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bd654eb5cb43208ef07e4c710bcb8c6b30657dac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVOi7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzV0QAHMeA2uH3sqpxC5GeNqTJgcV\nIcfZCo3xF0l1mFqBd2EtS82HxuXZvPaUxVi4mRHhFlpJ7i+zJuhtGk3l75voIOt6\nHqbo/8NFPGPDMKMUgY4XNM1TNDmSC2r4LEUIiUJjKNAGm1jdp1J7Vn0DD9iyAAaf\n78JXJYSdemkdYnCtxhYi6lQsZLlHefw9nMdqbDMyAqMLhX3UnJ6J6/DViG4mFiEV\n5H486mhVlDnSWc9VvXnvG7o7cTxLQlQuMdrv8EjSlf13WL04peagc2iZ2G+MDd13\nFbGB6dPnSSJHLEcu8FdEkq2UHWlQqF7/8fBi+oAts+l2PkvA2RyIIcnsn/H9B2Y5\nM5pFR8s+VpS+3VzVOi3QpgzSGIKMeEiXV6MgskKAxm1vk+/5r3EKoWMyCjqiDt5N\n4nJEewKvvqDstCxS9e6h/1CnUKWNH55E6D32Ob5mrI+zwxbsswjQGWK2HaNrUUHY\nZAS3nBrGRM2svfNeQMzlDGsbOc8+0lZD/mQKCEOi8n6jRpOi6SPASJGyjlVK6eCl\nxEXuniWgzUv8sbZAr0sRqP+s7buaeq9c80IC66CqySPLuPtluDNfSePfsdIZRin7\nULJqjFpA67MbacLsTFCJj9OaXilGkZqOY7+FWppnDz+EbkHKFBtiJrfIoajEOvf2\nM9nM26kmvrsgKaIzGth/\n=Qmn0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bd654eb5cb43208ef07e4c710bcb8c6b30657dac\nparent b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783949499 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783949499 -0400\n\nfix(code): wrap MCP viewer navigation (#4677)\n\nMCP viewer keyboard navigation now wraps at list boundaries, with arrow\nkeys moving through every row and `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` moving between\nservers.\n\n---\n\nThe MCP viewer now lets users continue navigating at list boundaries\ninstead of reversing direction.\n\n`Up` and `Down` wrap through every displayed row, including server\nheaders and tools. `Tab` and `Shift+Tab` provide faster server-level\nnavigation by moving to the next or previous server header and wrapping\nat either end. From a tool, `Shift+Tab` returns to that tool's server\nheader, while `Tab` advances to the next server.\n\nThis also makes header-only lists—such as when every server has an\nerror—fully navigable with either set of keys.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T13:31:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cffc73213bfdcec26cb82c413fa7e27db4afc0ca/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd"}]},{"sha":"b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIyZDYyY2U0NTY0MGY0OTcwN2ViMDU3YTEzNWRlMGViYzVhNWE2Y2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T07:38:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T07:38:35Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): restore `Shift+Tab` in debug console (#4680)\n\n`Shift+Tab` now moves focus backward in the in-app Debug Console instead\nof being ignored.\n\n---\n\nInside the Debug Console, the app-level priority `Shift+Tab` binding\nintercepted the key before the modal's reverse-focus handler could run.\nAs a result, `Tab` moved focus forward, but `Shift+Tab` appeared to do\nnothing.\n\nThis lets the app binding step aside while `DebugConsoleScreen` is\nactive, allowing the console's existing reverse traversal to handle the\nkey. The integration coverage uses the real `DeepAgentsApp` so the\npriority-binding conflict remains tested.","tree":{"sha":"04f28f3c67f30396015a84c69ae812fff831e0fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/04f28f3c67f30396015a84c69ae812fff831e0fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVJX7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC3sQABp63YJIkxL6A+u8GA/Lx4r2\nI6ys/Lq8wcRDqO8jIuC3EQTUnUghdQ14iPVFlw9JUaTO8xBK5PJxlkjCzSMy4L54\n58rryujbB2uYxr/O49fPcAiioT3QckACKVMvPrsgJUxZVwfcdP9N8K+mA8Yp52a3\nFpntBCmYyTQCftmKJZsyOyxfcuikhUH4rvuwsb2nzfXrsdKX8CEoku2yn8LShvde\nTqYxNXayKz0Himmi7Fbf/eblg8JJnTXeuC3nE5hvZ4tESDP/XUkSXFYPhCJjtz/n\nZYdhbwXzKDhXDwhBwJFIcOMyh/eKY4pSMjhBnx7YW+ajztH2VK7i6OBZGE/tmOTt\nEaQiUWQRnoSbaKThXP+HvYTsJ1hCi/qU8+AaWAO0eOn6iII57C0sTIqW6Fb/gsBZ\nNsJyj4APbhZjjvPLoTVzuiBvVghWdBC4NqSjKIjCro5sz2VH7KA6nIRQjHcpks0g\nro7SZvaiToFtWuLUjjhkH+GGCb8ufxG216oCoLLXn8zBsNvbTl1NpqovAlAqf+BX\n1fLIyInfgXLDxh+6eN9L3NXuWcK6aNA9f83Tq4dOeW56eulwHxOvulE8j1VC4EXZ\nv+VBh63jWliWt26nhb53KFKe2ipuCrLlZMsNr2W/hvW0xwPlgXeqpcFgQ0CmNsBK\ne3Jtyc9Yv0pinKIhEh1J\n=0ydH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 04f28f3c67f30396015a84c69ae812fff831e0fc\nparent 4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783928315 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783928315 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): restore `Shift+Tab` in debug console (#4680)\n\n`Shift+Tab` now moves focus backward in the in-app Debug Console instead\nof being ignored.\n\n---\n\nInside the Debug Console, the app-level priority `Shift+Tab` binding\nintercepted the key before the modal's reverse-focus handler could run.\nAs a result, `Tab` moved focus forward, but `Shift+Tab` appeared to do\nnothing.\n\nThis lets the app binding step aside while `DebugConsoleScreen` is\nactive, allowing the console's existing reverse traversal to handle the\nkey. The integration coverage uses the real `DeepAgentsApp` so the\npriority-binding conflict remains tested.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T07:38:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b2d62ce45640f49707eb057a135de0ebc5a5a6cd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1"}]},{"sha":"4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjZWVkMjRkMzc1ODgwMWVkOWRmMTAyNDYwMmU5MDQ4ODAwNGNlZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T07:19:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T07:19:52Z"},"message":"fix(code): infer additional model providers (#4675)\n\nDeep Agents Code now automatically detects the provider for additional\nbare model names supported by its provider extras — Cohere Command,\nMistral AI, DeepSeek, xAI Grok, and Perplexity Sonar — and recognizes\nAmazon Bedrock model IDs by their vendor-namespaced structure, including\nversioned and cross-region inference-profile IDs.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code resolves a model provider before calling\n`init_chat_model` so it can apply provider-specific configuration and\nreport credential errors clearly. Its local inference table did not\nrecognize several bare model names that LangChain already supports, even\nthough the corresponding dcode provider extras are available.\n\nFor the direct-API providers, mirror LangChain's supported prefix\nmappings: OpenAI `text-davinci*`, Cohere `command*`, Mistral AI\n`mistral*`/`mixtral*`, DeepSeek `deepseek*`, xAI `grok*`, and Perplexity\n`sonar*`.\n\nBedrock is handled structurally rather than by an enumerated prefix\nlist: any `[<region>.]<vendor>.<model>` ID (e.g.\n`meta.llama3-70b-instruct-v1:0`, `mistral.mistral-large-2402-v1:0`, or\nthe cross-region profile `us.anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0`)\nis detected as Bedrock. Keying off the dotted vendor-namespace signature\navoids maintaining AWS's ever-growing vendor list while keeping bare\ndirect-API names (`mistral-large`, `command-r-plus`) routed to their own\nAPIs.\n\nBecause Bedrock IDs can carry a `:<version>` suffix, `create_model` now\ntreats a detected Bedrock spec as a bare model name so the suffix is not\nmisparsed as a `provider:model` separator. An explicit `provider:model`\nspec whose provider is configured still takes precedence.\n\nExisting dcode-specific handling for `o4*`, NVIDIA, credential-aware\nClaude and Gemini routing, and fully qualified Fireworks model IDs\nremains unchanged. `solar*` remains unrecognized because dcode does not\nyet package or configure Upstage.","tree":{"sha":"aa6ce9260b4972a4fd6842aa6de2e5e7b89ad911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aa6ce9260b4972a4fd6842aa6de2e5e7b89ad911"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVJGYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUPIQAKx2372RXlTBOIXWEX/PeWta\nj+u6mQblj49fRVgcARZEFMHIXWKLiYX2IkqqDhl4CMGUVVpvw8Yd1jZBnJkXvKW4\niPLD31RBl1gWJEI6KpC6uWBbnV06FoCeBpEB8st8PYjkrAz1VX2L493yTg4ftKZF\nhkGisVoKjSo4tWR2vmACz4U0A46nF13hzh5blOGpFBADoHbVqk42o2JScq40RAuk\nPAqtjB9cjHvgSdwjK111jv25qKp0ZLViwGD2M+SJskwoOWZYLiQ9qbF6avcJ4Sds\nPjOTdrEhHYLdAWXMFLMDvl+ywFFCsq0nOecdBYVUc/xhe/PiMrIp8MdG1ZDDEPcp\nflUHvlyny14IoLzsRR0P+nGuPHWYnKADy5pTaXwDABhxG+pD0bkmXuYEEt/KrTzg\n4hxO9/GWRw/IFdETFOjMMX3Q07jzVZ0yDZPrwE8IzBAxevhxOW1yQIiRcq23RPMB\nuHUbBG00rW+1sIIC+OnaN1OKYnGjSuwZkwZGXNs3JxhdjcWxDuoyj7fZxEKF9oSJ\nN7kGmG3on0PVf2m6NNe2t6XEFMUsBgXBBcb1P9bhBU6dQXlbwlaN8w454LnmkQxr\nddJWNnIYszAzVbh1JySvogGMp8mavxyQjUdlzNuPvGXQXxqwUN2X1uRADLXabXMT\nTEChRvbsR2waurLninFX\n=9Mg9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aa6ce9260b4972a4fd6842aa6de2e5e7b89ad911\nparent 2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783927192 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783927192 -0400\n\nfix(code): infer additional model providers (#4675)\n\nDeep Agents Code now automatically detects the provider for additional\nbare model names supported by its provider extras — Cohere Command,\nMistral AI, DeepSeek, xAI Grok, and Perplexity Sonar — and recognizes\nAmazon Bedrock model IDs by their vendor-namespaced structure, including\nversioned and cross-region inference-profile IDs.\n\n---\n\nDeep Agents Code resolves a model provider before calling\n`init_chat_model` so it can apply provider-specific configuration and\nreport credential errors clearly. Its local inference table did not\nrecognize several bare model names that LangChain already supports, even\nthough the corresponding dcode provider extras are available.\n\nFor the direct-API providers, mirror LangChain's supported prefix\nmappings: OpenAI `text-davinci*`, Cohere `command*`, Mistral AI\n`mistral*`/`mixtral*`, DeepSeek `deepseek*`, xAI `grok*`, and Perplexity\n`sonar*`.\n\nBedrock is handled structurally rather than by an enumerated prefix\nlist: any `[<region>.]<vendor>.<model>` ID (e.g.\n`meta.llama3-70b-instruct-v1:0`, `mistral.mistral-large-2402-v1:0`, or\nthe cross-region profile `us.anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0`)\nis detected as Bedrock. Keying off the dotted vendor-namespace signature\navoids maintaining AWS's ever-growing vendor list while keeping bare\ndirect-API names (`mistral-large`, `command-r-plus`) routed to their own\nAPIs.\n\nBecause Bedrock IDs can carry a `:<version>` suffix, `create_model` now\ntreats a detected Bedrock spec as a bare model name so the suffix is not\nmisparsed as a `provider:model` separator. An explicit `provider:model`\nspec whose provider is configured still takes precedence.\n\nExisting dcode-specific handling for `o4*`, NVIDIA, credential-aware\nClaude and Gemini routing, and fully qualified Fireworks model IDs\nremains unchanged. `solar*` remains unrecognized because dcode does not\nyet package or configure Upstage.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T07:19:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4ceed24d3758801ed9df1024602e90488004cef1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02"}]},{"sha":"2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJmOGMxMTE3NmY1Y2M5MzUwYzMzMzdiMmRmY2Y5ZjE5ODg2ZDVkMDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T07:14:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T07:14:30Z"},"message":"fix(code): quit with `Ctrl+D` at end of prompt (#4678)\n\nFollow-up to #4626.\n\n`Ctrl+D` now quits Deep Agents Code when the cursor is at the end of the\nprompt, including when the prompt contains text. It continues to delete\nselected text or content to the right of the cursor.\n\n---\n\nAfter #4626, `Ctrl+D` preserves its delete-right behavior whenever the\nprompt contains a draft. At the end of a non-empty prompt, however,\nthere is nothing to delete and the key does nothing.\n\nTreat the end of the prompt like the empty-prompt case: `Ctrl+D` quits\nwhen there is no selection and no content to the right. It continues to\ndelete selected text, delete the next character, or join multiline input\nwhen the cursor is not at the true end of the prompt.","tree":{"sha":"60bcbe60d822c776d9d0b17c01ac87ef30a4bf95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/60bcbe60d822c776d9d0b17c01ac87ef30a4bf95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVJBWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeT0QAF9biNJnW/l/cj41FoGK2/GJ\nLY38mbu7gLcoNIY5vOmL+DSBBWLxI0Rre8l56Ml379pV99x9LjtR05LdQm5nH5ui\nnzsEtaw7jbkuQioDSMxS3nFRvm/w6qlIts9h2AoLOx/STvSN6IJVA9C4i877ohUm\njEPyINj8OZg4939NODYHrOF013YHvPWAx85Z9YEXqIh/qRW8NtNfOTp2wk4enp87\nt7qgoYDUVxtJ+fJ0leYkKu/S+hTK1T9ZQU4ioL5wAcqPPxVsof1ajAEvB5Ems78x\nMzD4CtFvacb1qPwdz+2ej/Osy4MfV/8udsSuGXU5E3b9NGMgQRgDN2/1owgOmV2h\nDTeBehYv/7vQ5UCziKZDCmiBFGMmt+UhxKJiVmElesTuQdA2yIhdVzluW1JdcpIp\nGlz2FizHerjfRGf+WWrX2vjJ8C5dBamlyPP83XyrBxNpVJf+4TW0ALNDOFxv2GZ/\nlrvGPOEuo2UGlAWZYqUv53eqiAFfbk+wWNtWjTklKeqIMpHf8Ih4QWw2Guktyppg\nvWw+9pY4N+bUWZe0TiT6Go3ntbrHs3gd2g7Xof2xy0vR5jdb04Nn1A/809Nr0tu6\nsMyB9xFa65Z6N6pL0GV3HehsgETcC+eSAWfoX9j9N6A0QldSHgKzzd9MYJvWahxR\nSgEgeePV5AEOy8qMqrjf\n=33Gc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 60bcbe60d822c776d9d0b17c01ac87ef30a4bf95\nparent b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783926870 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783926870 -0400\n\nfix(code): quit with `Ctrl+D` at end of prompt (#4678)\n\nFollow-up to #4626.\n\n`Ctrl+D` now quits Deep Agents Code when the cursor is at the end of the\nprompt, including when the prompt contains text. It continues to delete\nselected text or content to the right of the cursor.\n\n---\n\nAfter #4626, `Ctrl+D` preserves its delete-right behavior whenever the\nprompt contains a draft. At the end of a non-empty prompt, however,\nthere is nothing to delete and the key does nothing.\n\nTreat the end of the prompt like the empty-prompt case: `Ctrl+D` quits\nwhen there is no selection and no content to the right. It continues to\ndelete selected text, delete the next character, or join multiline input\nwhen the cursor is not at the true end of the prompt.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T07:14:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f8c11176f5cc9350c3337b2dfcf9f19886d5d02/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c"}]},{"sha":"b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIxNjAwYThkYTc4NDg5OWQ5ZGI1YmRmOTNiZTA3YjRjN2Y1M2E0NmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T07:13:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T07:13:37Z"},"message":"feat(code): `/tools` slash command (#4649)\n\nDeep Agents Code now supports `/tools`, which lists the built-in and MCP\ntools available to the current agent.\n\n---\n\nAdds an interactive `/tools` slash command to the `deepagents-code` TUI\nso users can see the tools available to the current agent, grouped into\nbuilt-in tools and tools from each MCP server. MCP servers that are\ndisabled, need login, or failed to load are shown separately instead of\ndisappearing from the list.\n\nFor managed sessions, built-in tools are enumerated off the UI thread\nwith a credential-free agent compile. For preconfigured local agents,\n`/tools` inspects the active graph directly so custom tool sets remain\nauthoritative. When a custom or remote agent cannot be inspected, the\ncommand explains that limitation rather than incorrectly reporting that\nno tools are available.\n\nMCP entries reuse the metadata loaded for the running agent instead of\nstarting discovery inside Textual's live event loop. If `/mcp`\nconfiguration changes are waiting for a reconnect, `/tools` keeps using\nthe pre-change snapshot so its output continues to match the tools the\nagent can currently invoke.\n\nThe catalog is rendered as a chat message, like `/tokens`, and is\ndiscoverable through `/help`, command completion, and a startup tip.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/626ca1ec-726e-58e8-7dae-4e85363c953d)\n\n## References\n\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/626ca1ec-726e-58e8-7dae-4e85363c953d/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"72a1d984b1eaa541a9bd528abc36a8b665e17d7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/72a1d984b1eaa541a9bd528abc36a8b665e17d7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVJAhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf5wQAGVDlTbaCBau41uyv94BsU7U\nIkgg5Le0PBy4pmNXQKsFTVwJByjOywiXkJX1EIdcHS/HQWfKgCDfMGBGR7KP2YZv\nyMcZJIpiOCNNNrzNoyJIbguj/y3ijRtZLYMgXYMuXAlUQQ1/iS6wFv5pBoqObm+s\n9w9gKdZwK0X7BTN2Btfw6IYC+RBIC8UvvRtkNeiaCC8gpV9QBEAORMoD+d6Vutff\nVX68WBwWtuR2bxoGCSwvLX1FsnQTlnnsf653yeowglbJTRXK8uf3Q7Ep1HTCtoKR\n4YxSKeoPK+fvPNKDjOI0CandO8N7qid1nOD8IaradxthVLhd5Xu6mxDYuLMVwudy\nnW/Apxg2oQ34803LdRHf5bPrmCpr8rRDc8GMexOPweOWwVWMBCCeRgWtDV5wJXP5\nOV8jF0jukUZ9+QqZ+vY2R44xMBHRcOqfmE+Ov6IhqlTUjgi2o1k8FVeFZzPlaY/U\nhum7FBE5A1vBQgU148UBVCreOk4XANTmqgOpF716oKZtE5/uQgb7MCLiZZfGaX9X\nB68TetqYDKfZcGrAzV9TQAiInEY3ycT7TWRotxze3pgDaQq+m6ZP5yvPp243daRy\n4gyUZ7rPPoBcSIxpfz6wo4DwdYzDMu9TRpIEBTcro/IMcZk0yjraIOZ1TjqcjtFO\nbXsqS2w7jlv56lekoru9\n=Jn2d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 72a1d984b1eaa541a9bd528abc36a8b665e17d7e\nparent 4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783926817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783926817 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `/tools` slash command (#4649)\n\nDeep Agents Code now supports `/tools`, which lists the built-in and MCP\ntools available to the current agent.\n\n---\n\nAdds an interactive `/tools` slash command to the `deepagents-code` TUI\nso users can see the tools available to the current agent, grouped into\nbuilt-in tools and tools from each MCP server. MCP servers that are\ndisabled, need login, or failed to load are shown separately instead of\ndisappearing from the list.\n\nFor managed sessions, built-in tools are enumerated off the UI thread\nwith a credential-free agent compile. For preconfigured local agents,\n`/tools` inspects the active graph directly so custom tool sets remain\nauthoritative. When a custom or remote agent cannot be inspected, the\ncommand explains that limitation rather than incorrectly reporting that\nno tools are available.\n\nMCP entries reuse the metadata loaded for the running agent instead of\nstarting discovery inside Textual's live event loop. If `/mcp`\nconfiguration changes are waiting for a reconnect, `/tools` keeps using\nthe pre-change snapshot so its output continues to match the tools the\nagent can currently invoke.\n\nThe catalog is rendered as a chat message, like `/tokens`, and is\ndiscoverable through `/help`, command completion, and a startup tip.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/626ca1ec-726e-58e8-7dae-4e85363c953d)\n\n## References\n\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/626ca1ec-726e-58e8-7dae-4e85363c953d/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T07:13:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1600a8da784899d9db5bdf93be07b4c7f53a46c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043"}]},{"sha":"4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRmOTRhMzBjMTFlZmIxODE5YjA4NjQ3ZDE1YjUwYjliMWU3YmYwNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T06:48:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T06:48:48Z"},"message":"feat(code): in-app Debug Console (#4564)\n\nDeep Agents Code now includes an in-app Debug Console. Press `Ctrl+\\` to\ninspect session details and filter, view, or copy recent application\nlogs without enabling file-based debug logging.\n\n---\n\nDebugging client-side TUI problems currently requires restarting with\nfile logging enabled and tailing a log in another terminal. This adds an\nin-app Debug Console, modeled on Mistral Vibe's console, so users can\ninspect session state and recent application logs without leaving the\nTUI.\n\nOpen the console with `Ctrl+\\` or the hidden `/debug` command. It shows\na point-in-time snapshot of the version, model, thread, working\ndirectory, auto-approve state, sandbox, MCP servers, token usage, and\ndebug-log path. Below that, it tails recent `deepagents_code.*` records\nfrom an always-on bounded in-memory buffer and supports filtering by\nseverity.\n\nThe buffer captures `INFO` and above by default, or the level selected\nwith `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LOG_LEVEL`. `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` continues to\nenable append-only file logging and defaults capture to `DEBUG`.\n`Ctrl+L` clears the current console view without clearing the underlying\nbuffer; `c` copies the visible filtered records retained since the last\nclear, and clicking a record copies only that record.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"36bd1312095fe3c41efee3216fd3d9e0ccfc195f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/36bd1312095fe3c41efee3216fd3d9e0ccfc195f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVIpQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe48QADQVwUMCGZpI5p5sp8LSGLnV\nfGiN/x/Co4gsJ0uysRB5lH6nMUzMZStqdzlz/dAcBARMgKL4ex8m5+cD/8ttZy2w\nniVwprnaUiNrVPVxtAyTWf2gfU/q1RgJ2yan2oLzFlIjyIH9YUGWe83u6THDdFJI\nYH15BfK71ZRqjzc+50V86DEZELHiS+NY34PbPT1fBf6NNebhLSdr1ggR4qSLDW+I\n90pTwaK9L0OIwGm2EN7NknfgjL9t5XqpthLiYLLpvf9AKMUWi9GdEITVe0O1inMZ\n60pDnQJCy7DO6+oWL5CWmQbKruNXai4QpmXHC8HKejSDOuM56JcE952w0eE4ERD8\nIR+ab//SkWp3eiXaR3DhTVqPwFCp/ZC3UmocoFRoUjo7Deh5Lo+XqPInTk8NfEQ6\n7PlqpU8G0D6MA7uEWGqa3zPojdqDi7DWD0iF9fuWOt5lLX2wJHNHTid5AdBH5+Gi\nqh6JORFKz+3TOYiyeb1GleHFsMIj3sm9sHbQhdOA0uHvOsC/rhOTX+DcZyJTkdac\nTSPdOnzJOcHyEFrSiV2SiytB2QRAQWGjiE1ftLg4vJNPcMMAZy5BMW+SeSYh6Ovo\nlhbzkdXtkWLITDVGy2EMg/sZRnqjDSsWAWHWwXiFZ1cK51Fc3NHISC2g9IdBca0G\nqQiRf7ECCEyW5jmdfRhR\n=qE0G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 36bd1312095fe3c41efee3216fd3d9e0ccfc195f\nparent 87b9663ad1b3dc06ce732aac32f6fc06f2a428d7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783925328 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783925328 -0400\n\nfeat(code): in-app Debug Console (#4564)\n\nDeep Agents Code now includes an in-app Debug Console. Press `Ctrl+\\` to\ninspect session details and filter, view, or copy recent application\nlogs without enabling file-based debug logging.\n\n---\n\nDebugging client-side TUI problems currently requires restarting with\nfile logging enabled and tailing a log in another terminal. This adds an\nin-app Debug Console, modeled on Mistral Vibe's console, so users can\ninspect session state and recent application logs without leaving the\nTUI.\n\nOpen the console with `Ctrl+\\` or the hidden `/debug` command. It shows\na point-in-time snapshot of the version, model, thread, working\ndirectory, auto-approve state, sandbox, MCP servers, token usage, and\ndebug-log path. Below that, it tails recent `deepagents_code.*` records\nfrom an always-on bounded in-memory buffer and supports filtering by\nseverity.\n\nThe buffer captures `INFO` and above by default, or the level selected\nwith `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LOG_LEVEL`. `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` continues to\nenable append-only file logging and defaults capture to `DEBUG`.\n`Ctrl+L` clears the current console view without clearing the underlying\nbuffer; `c` copies the visible filtered records retained since the last\nclear, and clicking a record copies only that record.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T06:48:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4f94a30c11efb1819b08647d15b50b9b1e7bf043/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.g