//api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d"}]},{"sha":"8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhjZjU3YWNhOWY0MWMzYzRjYTZkOTc5NmRjMmNiODBkNGIyMmZiNmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T06:14:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T06:14:30Z"},"message":"feat(code): set `prompt_cache_key` for OpenAI models (#4632)\n\nSet `prompt_cache_key` on OpenAI model calls (keyed to the thread ID) so\nGPT-5.6+ models get reliable prompt-cache prefix matching.\n\n---\n\nOpenAI's GPT-5.6 and later model families require `prompt_cache_key` to\nuse the more reliable prompt-prefix matching for both implicit and\nexplicit caching. `ConfigurableModelMiddleware` now injects the active\nthread ID as a top-level `prompt_cache_key` for OpenAI models\n(`ls_provider == \"openai\"`), mirroring the existing Fireworks\nsession-affinity path. It's passed top-level (not via\n`extra_body`/`extra_headers`), which is how\n`langchain_openai.ChatOpenAI` forwards it for both the Chat Completions\nand Responses APIs. Any user-supplied key is preserved.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d948dfb5-805e-b4cf-d194-9d579c86811e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c38aaac27ef7a2c10a009b1b90989d4f5bde0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7c38aaac27ef7a2c10a009b1b90989d4f5bde0bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVIJGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJjIQAHqeKa90Lq4C6c7G3xX11tuM\n8RciMxT8JfxGYXIle0YhSNv3B9zgC/pTJ3Iea9iMbSyfWeNDQStU7zFnjRheoQ5U\nSJQHK8tpkHefduprpKr902YzX29RlNSyo/baR9oMhVFAE38JEsWWAftXHtgW+aTB\nJ0XYICNwqGbQhGGLDo/qtJQW78y499NpjcbCdSY6qgXEUwTSaHcMth5PPCG3kHgN\nk3fKUPgkCfLXHWoXXa6cEm/e6nY8Lvv6X6Pi8IUj7KTLALL/cA2mU8v4abOYlYKX\nRD8r8t7QV9vQ+r8xmJl4FRAEkXWLJKUR58NwdfkX2DOl5f+WpWlSHUpeAfSugS6O\n15RFMwwaWyInvEtuIz2RGj7w6SUMwHi07jHJmlqgvyFATwks91FQNghTN/cap8sZ\nRgZsu4y4arEXNh5WX7DBOpitdfQwYZ0hMFmi1JNKKq2WLd54dcqN/PiizwDigAW3\nVXwliwnNQVCnNwRx70ngpkZgnlVs1nJFBcZas9M8M58UxIQWYiUchZ5C+paFlG+w\n0gKnLZqCdlDiXDXQEBAeKVS59ZcaALklTQk6hn9EYFLwb1QwbDLLOKSu21SGURld\njC2s3LCMXUtZZdF5z/xvv7eD5dYfJikPNKIBtW9/OwdheTGu7wAgr7X8Fkyzg3mp\nuZDVEO1F4BstjYaKmDl7\n=aFWp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7c38aaac27ef7a2c10a009b1b90989d4f5bde0bb\nparent 70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783923270 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783923270 -0400\n\nfeat(code): set `prompt_cache_key` for OpenAI models (#4632)\n\nSet `prompt_cache_key` on OpenAI model calls (keyed to the thread ID) so\nGPT-5.6+ models get reliable prompt-cache prefix matching.\n\n---\n\nOpenAI's GPT-5.6 and later model families require `prompt_cache_key` to\nuse the more reliable prompt-prefix matching for both implicit and\nexplicit caching. `ConfigurableModelMiddleware` now injects the active\nthread ID as a top-level `prompt_cache_key` for OpenAI models\n(`ls_provider == \"openai\"`), mirroring the existing Fireworks\nsession-affinity path. It's passed top-level (not via\n`extra_body`/`extra_headers`), which is how\n`langchain_openai.ChatOpenAI` forwards it for both the Chat Completions\nand Responses APIs. Any user-supplied key is preserved.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d948dfb5-805e-b4cf-d194-9d579c86811e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T06:14:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cf57aca9f41c3c4ca6d9796dc2cb80d4b22fb6d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b"}]},{"sha":"70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcwODI5YzU4NDZiNmJkZGUxY2VlNTFmMGY0OTI5ZTgxOWJhMTAyNmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ccurme","email":"chester.curme@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-13T06:09:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T06:09:18Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Meta model provider (#4650)\n\nAdds the Meta Model API to the model switcher, credential manager, model\ndiscovery, and optional-provider installer.\n\nThe new `meta` extra installs the MIT-licensed `langchain-meta>=0.5.0`\nintegration (published by the `langchain-ai` org), and the base\n`langchain` dependency is bumped to `>=1.3.13` so `init_chat_model`\nresolves the `meta` provider through the standard LangChain provider\npath. Verified against `langchain-meta` 0.5.0: `ChatMetaModel` reads\n`MODEL_API_KEY` for the key and `MODEL_API_BASE` for the base URL.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4010ad30-bfc5-e865-9ab2-c08a10518889)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3d997ea3f7022248de666b6d8fe9f2684f7529e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d3d997ea3f7022248de666b6d8fe9f2684f7529e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVIEOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARM4QAJRDmekIU401YuPNVaJf+p6T\nffafzooqV96jFNrMbxanuLE8rk/BBFn/QgxoXWLto1VkQ2kct9lZCAFx9wf2Ltbe\n3V2Z+6fPQYmi6GFVfeeUpBRVbavLt52dCboh1G6uHGjXgWGlumzPOsjPXfCg/5RE\n+Lz2W84BNXzqT7fs8Q/aReny2KGZAGNGM80AwzegyYqAqypT3Ja9lvhXisCLhqKr\nT+JHKVRwbwePmi4fjWy8DmBVKV2CSbqYyWYimHtf0tedzavHgVNY63u+mktBBdDd\ndbmgwVztyFI49G5TRYMgev4G7c0qSYCJ3Od20I0bKvbZcFtUctqo/CG5iuWUkjfb\nkdocSzB0SWnYH4EH20S0DQYC4Sdhl1gVHkn+RiVzlaWK6ggked/1AtJu6R25Y4U5\nRk/VBsBoDy38s08/adHDXbMd5gVxwd4K3IlAW2k3BLK8SXPDaYiivFZxwO/+Avsq\n2WPhJrAY0AKRU+s+a+wx6evn25Zh/1wrXZQAmrfmFlr+oV18wjSwGy3xRWsZu6mf\nG8obnKtl0Q69X0czqS02Z1aQOoALA4q110n8uuRUur29ZDJ1iaVt87xmOjBhccQK\nze5YpAaXLwrjgKt8IQooUBiZMyRvxIzytDpjXkMBq9vj5VVIQoMow4Ww7vP4Q2FB\nzPk46Inxtn3iItzmvkHe\n=j73u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d3d997ea3f7022248de666b6d8fe9f2684f7529e\nparent aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870\nauthor ccurme <chester.curme@gmail.com> 1783922958 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783922958 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add Meta model provider (#4650)\n\nAdds the Meta Model API to the model switcher, credential manager, model\ndiscovery, and optional-provider installer.\n\nThe new `meta` extra installs the MIT-licensed `langchain-meta>=0.5.0`\nintegration (published by the `langchain-ai` org), and the base\n`langchain` dependency is bumped to `>=1.3.13` so `init_chat_model`\nresolves the `meta` provider through the standard LangChain provider\npath. Verified against `langchain-meta` 0.5.0: `ChatMetaModel` reads\n`MODEL_API_KEY` for the key and `MODEL_API_BASE` for the base URL.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4010ad30-bfc5-e865-9ab2-c08a10518889)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T06:09:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70829c5846b6bdde1cee51f0f4929e819ba1026b/comments","author":{"login":"ccurme","id":26529506,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTI5NTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26529506?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme","html_url":"https://github.com/ccurme","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870"}]},{"sha":"aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhZWFjOTlkOWYxN2I2YTU1ZDY2M2MyMWE0ZDA2MzQ0NGI2YTE4NzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T06:01:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T06:01:58Z"},"message":"feat(code): offer abort in `/threads` cwd-switch prompt (#4583)\n\nThe `/threads` directory prompt now lets you abort a thread switch and\nremain on the current thread.\n\n---\n\nWhen `/threads` selects a thread that was last used in another\ndirectory, the directory prompt now offers a third choice: press `a` to\ncancel the thread switch and keep the current thread and directory.\n\nPreviously, the prompt only allowed switching to the thread’s original\ndirectory or continuing in the current directory. This matches the\nlaunch-time resume prompt while using wording specific to an in-session\nthread switch.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/50cf0c96-66d9-b2ed-0ff1-5c67fa94300f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b0554374af90da5f321173eb747b98e6cf0596b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7b0554374af90da5f321173eb747b98e6cf0596b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVH9WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACzoQAKoFsGdsCOnHnD5KAxzR3wmB\nXzwP13A7S4fdvTZ/WGmMMBjE8DQDWHO9EokUe34vEAix1+9mZ1ujQtIl8qG5zJBL\no+9QTWplVhgVGJGX7wdbje72qi1I1nf4Y10EfHFVEkKNBHgyRH+Ku5qH/sNcQTSB\nMfsCFs7c3z5FRZBx1RBMEshaLUKMT5ZBesagYahmT3oV16gYTrf3aENtnjKfEcEk\nBYXGLJy26ySJGNN+leh4lvzIBTYSi2OiZQ6WtMJBKOvSRzaS+pAXlgYh2+5YYvWo\nuDhskuiL7OHqCKMG5KQejQO90Tz1Q7N3XJJZkBIijUTlS/um2Lhs8yLee5RSJghN\nyUXxFN4dImRV2iDud6A5gRkj9ir74qF9cdzEt8nxbICR3XsmhTPS3iGRqI5Gawnw\nJmo9tPYB/3q3VipPpjGj/5E74K3L4pUkrdrVZM2bYdqJfjruTx7s/apY/SGBpmha\naUSaMwu6DtniTIEIEmBMaFDs8kM0Nrlbhc151kmEmEp4RAKths+of3TXEelL5cTc\nYGX26svIsvraTBArioGpLFnjZoEL/YXym7jPEJm4noT21kYp4So9L1QYnXAx1WuX\nh3jw0kdHCQwihX4GKTw2uq3tqIxKaaE6r69XT5bnTCdmfWbR7DrM/a42g1QJATem\n1g/qFsp9Hy/ygz+/Y26U\n=RyNO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7b0554374af90da5f321173eb747b98e6cf0596b\nparent 4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783922518 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783922518 -0400\n\nfeat(code): offer abort in `/threads` cwd-switch prompt (#4583)\n\nThe `/threads` directory prompt now lets you abort a thread switch and\nremain on the current thread.\n\n---\n\nWhen `/threads` selects a thread that was last used in another\ndirectory, the directory prompt now offers a third choice: press `a` to\ncancel the thread switch and keep the current thread and directory.\n\nPreviously, the prompt only allowed switching to the thread’s original\ndirectory or continuing in the current directory. This matches the\nlaunch-time resume prompt while using wording specific to an in-session\nthread switch.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/50cf0c96-66d9-b2ed-0ff1-5c67fa94300f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T06:01:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aaeac99d9f17b6a55d663c21a4d063444b6a1870/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea"}]},{"sha":"4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRkMmFhOGE5Njg0NjA5ZWVlNDVjZDkzYjBhZjUxNDlkOGRkMDllZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T05:50:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T05:50:31Z"},"message":"fix(code): infer Fireworks provider from qualified model IDs (#4594)\n\nDeep Agents Code now preserves the Fireworks provider when `/model`\nreceives a fully qualified Fireworks model or router ID, so the switch\nconfirmation and status bar display the provider correctly.\n\n---\n\nSwitching models with a fully qualified Fireworks ID such as `/model\naccounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code` succeeded because LangChain\ninferred the provider during model initialization. Deep Agents Code did\nnot make the same inference beforehand, though, so it lost the provider\nname: the switch confirmation showed only the raw ID and the status bar\nomitted the `fireworks:` prefix.\n\n`detect_provider` now recognizes the broad `accounts/fireworks/` stem,\nmatching LangChain's inference for both model and router IDs. The\nexisting, narrower model and router prefixes remain responsible for\nshortening those IDs in the status bar and classifying reasoning-effort\nsupport.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1f74e649-60d9-d586-f671-41b471b5a5d8)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4617fdca945a9a161b142de503451ad0e7cc9506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4617fdca945a9a161b142de503451ad0e7cc9506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVHynCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyAIQAGpKCdEg81TbYgWBbL8TUDPS\npN29ZdXxpV5y2sLKnbtKjj2jci23EZrQoAwrzmyuAvBqh5lT6URFtOAze9DVzzfg\nWMg3iCaDUnHf7cRkW3MIbU6NeH1IiLUkJwAfTgzPbf7L5/wEeFShwJV0NsgJTtxb\n+DLVMd8txTPE+8LBceumRjywiVuY1fgUb6Ou02rdbb3BTjtPzac5r0h/oiJKe70L\nBL+3PzpYtaTKAPbx2cmkWLrCx9V/2s/bHUTJGqV61jzvFY3NCTStfGQhv5erOgfG\nS9rEKJezw3fOzc+lVHvgpQ4igwaNGfUqaHqBME6C8S4j122u/9yV+SbQYE0RrWlY\nBS/Lug8TxTQPOUFYkxj3HvEitRG/Fx4AdspLSoA0EfogTjGdWgMKVOGOCAOOcoST\nV0oAuIq72D6WgXwrpoyKjO3pEE/6A0M8/63BaGkxvX6kOMMdtXKaXC8xjLv7T73i\n0vqrC2AjhZ+zAQHskS0UEUbFpYZDZRY6kLSxvGOIAI4XRVTMoKv9MQ+Ey6OnhwF8\nge3lgx6JHpS4s+SbNAf0DyWVK3nns8YZUtkYrilFWQDBMbLrrNJbjJvLSVg/Z0r6\njAxVMPeESXvAcZX4NlAnME3fouHBdwNrFs8qEYNcMULOiq9KFRB8WtH5jFRfej2h\nhJHdsdLu9FJ+bBD1cWXU\n=Aifc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4617fdca945a9a161b142de503451ad0e7cc9506\nparent 4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783921831 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783921831 -0400\n\nfix(code): infer Fireworks provider from qualified model IDs (#4594)\n\nDeep Agents Code now preserves the Fireworks provider when `/model`\nreceives a fully qualified Fireworks model or router ID, so the switch\nconfirmation and status bar display the provider correctly.\n\n---\n\nSwitching models with a fully qualified Fireworks ID such as `/model\naccounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code` succeeded because LangChain\ninferred the provider during model initialization. Deep Agents Code did\nnot make the same inference beforehand, though, so it lost the provider\nname: the switch confirmation showed only the raw ID and the status bar\nomitted the `fireworks:` prefix.\n\n`detect_provider` now recognizes the broad `accounts/fireworks/` stem,\nmatching LangChain's inference for both model and router IDs. The\nexisting, narrower model and router prefixes remain responsible for\nshortening those IDs in the status bar and classifying reasoning-effort\nsupport.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1f74e649-60d9-d586-f671-41b471b5a5d8)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T05:50:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d2aa8a9684609eee45cd93b0af5149d8dd09eea/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596"}]},{"sha":"4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjNDlhMjRjNGM0ODhmNDU4NTliNDU2MjhjZmE1NzcxOWU1MmY1OTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T05:48:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T05:48:11Z"},"message":"feat(code): hide diff widget for credential files (#4593)\n\nThe interactive coding agent no longer renders diffs/contents of\ncredential files (e.g. `.env`), preventing secrets from appearing in the\nterminal UI.\n\n---\n\nThe file diff widget rendered the contents of `.env` and other\ncredential files, leaking secrets into the terminal UI and scrollback.\nThis adds a filename-based `is_sensitive_file_path` helper in\n`file_ops.py` and redacts both the chat `DiffMessage` and the write/edit\nHITL approval widgets for such files, showing a short notice instead of\nthe contents while preserving change stats for edit approvals.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7d568e82-479c-9e1a-6cde-af3aad536483)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8abe4d53322cc455c2ea7e672adc7d02e330a3c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8abe4d53322cc455c2ea7e672adc7d02e330a3c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVHwbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjgYQAFU34+/tEO38LOfTNZV/g8Rz\n44wg5lamo/3h+Gf4vnAaPnOU5CplgT879pqkocMnDG3AuJYUPcgBErTqRNti2ULP\n4V0ukKxodOPMJxZzUW6P0NHjxGcHB8/IzrWZej3HZBLy9Q8g0pjLM1ih2wHJuL9Q\nOPo0pw/X0FWjLdWCvc45485f+uLXB/+vsAGvB6gE283Fts4PvdtewK1DzqEIgsLf\n66kNbQVASYrw/oASOYSFVkoR4exKr9LbuWa8Fc5b1UL0atvcY4gnNcszs6s8KmCs\nJast1a/4fl/nM6mIcyck8fb2a1mLcWMPURjUr2dBvmGnP+qmRLsoxTrneW5rwmHC\nVmgaGhHBTS0eHf8uFOFBO6FWhuEVSF+EA+bDbHkLq+cAeEcj7KUgGIPWHdaBr+/y\nuRrEmNSAUAKfTlkmabLhPzFO4V7mtlE9adDhISFWhxSEBBH/ooHnIYLvHg+x7djh\n9NvIu0o2dGOo7NIQUe8NcyR8Hwy7+MAMJOExCqEVc8N7JTxX/MfCXDydKL2DmKMw\nA3Xj+U6Ev3encOvATUfq+ejJb1t7Cq7Q6+TMKLPGfZQhseSZ+F8hGA/d5TX5+2Oy\nS8ySANqVQgRj5pbdCts+k4YvMCxmX2WGmU7ApXPTArlj5KvJytFodrkizIQYU2n3\nFqhhOMyuUNlbOKhOEkjh\n=Yd3i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8abe4d53322cc455c2ea7e672adc7d02e330a3c6\nparent d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783921691 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783921691 -0400\n\nfeat(code): hide diff widget for credential files (#4593)\n\nThe interactive coding agent no longer renders diffs/contents of\ncredential files (e.g. `.env`), preventing secrets from appearing in the\nterminal UI.\n\n---\n\nThe file diff widget rendered the contents of `.env` and other\ncredential files, leaking secrets into the terminal UI and scrollback.\nThis adds a filename-based `is_sensitive_file_path` helper in\n`file_ops.py` and redacts both the chat `DiffMessage` and the write/edit\nHITL approval widgets for such files, showing a short notice instead of\nthe contents while preserving change stats for edit approvals.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7d568e82-479c-9e1a-6cde-af3aad536483)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T05:48:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c49a24c4c488f45859b45628cfa57719e52f596/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417"}]},{"sha":"d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQxZjNhZmVjZGMwMTViNWQxYzlmYjA5OGQ2MzQ3YzdkNzE4MGU0MTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T05:46:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T05:46:55Z"},"message":"fix(code): detach owned `langgraph dev` server from terminal (#4642)\n\nFixed dcode hanging when its terminal was suspended or closed while it\nwas running the built-in `langgraph dev` server.\n\nWhen dcode starts its built-in `langgraph dev` server, closing or\nsuspending the terminal could stop the server unexpectedly and leave\ndcode hanging during cleanup. This PR separates the server from the\nterminal on macOS and Linux while keeping dcode responsible for shutting\nit down.\n\n---\n\n## Before\n\ndcode and its built-in server shared the same terminal session. Actions\nsuch as suspending dcode with Ctrl+Z or closing its terminal could\ntherefore affect both processes at once. The server could stop before\ndcode had a chance to clean it up, which could leave dcode stuck.\n\n## After\n\nThe built-in server now runs in a separate session on macOS and Linux,\nso terminal signals intended for dcode no longer stop the server at the\nsame time. When dcode exits, restarts the server, or encounters a\nstartup failure, it still shuts down the server and any child processes\nit started.\n\nThis separation matters in both directions: the server should not be\naccidentally stopped by the terminal, but it also must not be left\nrunning after dcode is gone. Shutdown first gives the full server\nprocess tree a chance to exit cleanly, then forces it to stop if\nnecessary. Safety checks ensure dcode never signals its own process\ngroup. Windows behavior is unchanged.\n\n---\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0c752fd0-cfc3-0b00-87ba-fb1e67b483ce)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"563ece15a3fd8500b9fb1a4f46743d3350a1a146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/563ece15a3fd8500b9fb1a4f46743d3350a1a146"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVHvQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA040QAEvhZExDUJnAlDX6bwWsjD9d\nxqVozUImRI/AdfoUJZSqyDTd59Q3PQAXEoCT/q56JUCPLb3ttx/9aEwNZxkb3pd8\n5/66xa/HONAqGY+Jc43GG0zzhXYRnL7kjFtfJTIeotN+7Omtxqksqe9HR+0FQhTv\nbjxqEeDx8lHvsnRLGUDYD5PQpuVtlsjdCJzElhB20cNGohloBc2DPw4kS3mC3hR4\np+rZ+2sj4Z3g64+fvEKN5eNEe39fXCYqelAUIjFAbYb48E5DQ3aaCoJLV2yMzB7X\np2Eu6/nNYPjPN4F2k+B/NwYwCOWlFZ7IEJ3C0GqpNJDteSsh1SwaoShEvFYDiLbG\nWMvaPF5VUnnsl+z6Ji6kSrL9+pQBgKFdJBoMbCav6aA/dvIouQjXJ9HNllWJPYd6\nT6EQ81N4mZE9ms0UcWZQ7h4PA2CH6Ah0CO5kxCBjquzR2s4txzAvLhM8t4L46Zr2\n35XOitPBrv9w2T834aJLpnRISr+4Cplugr0qjWCOXLrj2fNGxTopY11c72e68hD8\nz9ZwVzn9gHsptesmJfiPSXBjPGpAeotD97eicZdnVKZL5H6ZW9qhrFU9PDGHDJmn\nHgQuNtn46vUpTKsaefAaIymoFfZeiPVxZBA/hrmkmQFWACQMDc4vkD1H37pnSM6l\nrNUb3plveKye9jbNxO3q\n=NK+H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 563ece15a3fd8500b9fb1a4f46743d3350a1a146\nparent f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783921615 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783921615 -0400\n\nfix(code): detach owned `langgraph dev` server from terminal (#4642)\n\nFixed dcode hanging when its terminal was suspended or closed while it\nwas running the built-in `langgraph dev` server.\n\nWhen dcode starts its built-in `langgraph dev` server, closing or\nsuspending the terminal could stop the server unexpectedly and leave\ndcode hanging during cleanup. This PR separates the server from the\nterminal on macOS and Linux while keeping dcode responsible for shutting\nit down.\n\n---\n\n## Before\n\ndcode and its built-in server shared the same terminal session. Actions\nsuch as suspending dcode with Ctrl+Z or closing its terminal could\ntherefore affect both processes at once. The server could stop before\ndcode had a chance to clean it up, which could leave dcode stuck.\n\n## After\n\nThe built-in server now runs in a separate session on macOS and Linux,\nso terminal signals intended for dcode no longer stop the server at the\nsame time. When dcode exits, restarts the server, or encounters a\nstartup failure, it still shuts down the server and any child processes\nit started.\n\nThis separation matters in both directions: the server should not be\naccidentally stopped by the terminal, but it also must not be left\nrunning after dcode is gone. Shutdown first gives the full server\nprocess tree a chance to exit cleanly, then forces it to stop if\nnecessary. Safety checks ensure dcode never signals its own process\ngroup. Windows behavior is unchanged.\n\n---\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0c752fd0-cfc3-0b00-87ba-fb1e67b483ce)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T05:46:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1f3afecdc015b5d1c9fb098d6347c7d7180e417/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231"}]},{"sha":"f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYxMGI4NzdlNWU0OGMzYTFlMTViZDcyZDJjZTA2ZGZiMTYyMDMyMzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T05:42:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T05:42:08Z"},"message":"feat(code): show `(debug enabled)` on splash when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set (#4584)\n\nWhen `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` has a truthy value, the startup splash\ndisplays `(debug enabled)` so users can tell at a glance that debug\nlogging is active. The tag appears before `(local)` when both apply.\n\nThe debug tag remains visible when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_HIDE_SPLASH_VERSION`\nhides the version. Existing privacy behavior is preserved: the version,\n`(local)` tag, and editable-install source path all remain hidden.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/23f30b1b-d342-0b55-0549-193682eb1096)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"054ec6144331ffe5bf3b50687e60bde90605a624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/054ec6144331ffe5bf3b50687e60bde90605a624"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVHqwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhWwQAIRk7yUaxZuJtVz/WzEX+aiY\nslXN0PKygRIJ6P2gNqB6aAY5uqQUH+nVwo5pF51dEs3vXuYTB/nI3/UdWvJ0potP\nYK71Xjmf16mi4UCoHQEC0Dt6koGjjRqRB0WONBYIeGrPtyzXg5ckVoqyOabQdqP0\nE+E5sOd1WsLKm+gBdmzU729oJpJTF/nairhbzD3CYllsCc/NZ+TFa3l4tQUuabmQ\nSSQhoRsdubLUungjh0vRZy33tLfVCejSwui/kvDNl0omLMsABKksYhYLYFFOPIDx\nX3WA61UPE+1xd/XHN0aPNaLxCkBu210Fa01p2Tf8/notl+YfjdqMEFZreVpY8kMO\nTixvwIk+79RKX0+YAOFBF3dxj/FAZPjyBFtv9rJAKvbv9QzKZ8yi2Dk1ngsvwSZh\nuCeVf0PRJgRadlJij7yIHSKf9AtCFgaIymqMJaQR31n55VUupL8ck1CSVsfB982V\n7a3Gi0Z9z7QO6PIQF9bW46qyOwxz48Ecv0SrNXpvNkTsZw6XIy37G9DqESHofNId\nuBRQmugixLf36ZoKDM8QzUbf6+4bEL/Yee7DmyZa22fXCB9MNJc9tiaCoVOu2GjU\nLd2F28NwE3qo8684lQ9bvVzRB7aOLZdOPACA4HBtkrP+rgTTtSCB/0K1HCw0FLQJ\nn9pfB600im6iFS+MYZzS\n=UKOl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 054ec6144331ffe5bf3b50687e60bde90605a624\nparent d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783921328 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783921328 -0400\n\nfeat(code): show `(debug enabled)` on splash when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set (#4584)\n\nWhen `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` has a truthy value, the startup splash\ndisplays `(debug enabled)` so users can tell at a glance that debug\nlogging is active. The tag appears before `(local)` when both apply.\n\nThe debug tag remains visible when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_HIDE_SPLASH_VERSION`\nhides the version. Existing privacy behavior is preserved: the version,\n`(local)` tag, and editable-install source path all remain hidden.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/23f30b1b-d342-0b55-0549-193682eb1096)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T05:42:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f10b877e5e48c3a1e15bd72d2ce06dfb16203231/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da"}]},{"sha":"d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ0NDI2NzM1OGUyNzI1NTNjOGVjZTMzZDM2NzUxNDQzMGJlN2MwZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T05:35:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T05:35:35Z"},"message":"feat(code): resume threads in-TUI with `/threads -r [ID]` (#4609)\n\nThe `dcode` TUI now supports `/threads -r [ID]` to resume a previous\nthread in place, and `/clear` shows the thread you just left with a\none-step resume hint.\n\n---\n\nAfter `/clear` mints a new thread, there was no low-friction path back\nto the thread you just left — the id was dropped and only the modal\n`/threads` selector could find it again.\n\nThis adds an in-TUI equivalent of the launch-time `-r` flag rather than\na bespoke one-level `/go-back`, keeping parity with muscle memory users\nalready have and composing better:\n\n- `TextualSessionState` now records the outgoing thread as\n`previous_thread_id` on every `reset_thread` (`/clear`).\n- `/clear` output names the previous thread (with the same clickable\nLangSmith-link upgrade as the new-thread line) and prints a resume hint.\n- `/threads -r [ID]` resumes without opening the modal: bare `-r`\nreturns to the previous thread (falling back to the most recent thread\non disk), and `-r <ID>` resumes a specific thread. It reuses the\nexisting `_resume_thread` machinery, so behavior matches selecting a\nthread in the modal. Because `/threads` is an `IMMEDIATE_UI` command,\nonly the bare form bypasses the busy queue — `/threads -r …` is queued\nwhile the agent is running, so a resume never races an active turn.\n\nAutocomplete gains an `[-r [ID]]` argument hint and a splash tip\nadvertises the shortcut.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b717ea48-7edd-8049-95cc-64384c56e8a8)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"85a184ccae3dc87a2e402d1ebedcdddf14d152c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/85a184ccae3dc87a2e402d1ebedcdddf14d152c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVHknCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfygQADGkJLCzAsOwHFosz19vddh5\nLkhNK7xgieANklHCMmlZIBm+pgy9K0FNmbDRsjWPa0FHepMGud2NMK45lqrf1jyA\nWCPJMMuyE4sEsb538MHEf0Vg+tMS6NXqcekc6PhSGKD7L5YC62V9TIMe66rEfdnS\nF8oM4BE4L0cgiMDUnxKCcc22MF10Azj+WFnbDl9IlG6RxKRZkxDSylOcWKiq7rWW\n7gvdpE9Bd7DEU/RDOlYh7pIXFi5YzQ2VCmD76m3+2zMhFFlsxIRpJ+uAE6Z638xO\ngMoD99GXejbTahQyv/N79UoE1uck2CLjGaHCDCVw2UNeikThXwdutX8tCSmYWaN6\nIAPCmp+kaKcR+x+MQTulyWDCeJH3RWktbsUO52lhZ2sTZYFhht6K7Wz9AS1Ne3yM\nkEv48O4SFe/2EmsYPd+DWOq1qDY8tna148KKe36VRyITOfQXjdQfziZP/8LAB+oG\n10o1E3d9F/FxBpj58akkfDIriMbI8v63p/tuDqOSD7EYzeFkSDGkJ9pnzfuM4Va8\nzKOnrMaTYB2UktUV6xFBzUoA0vjHaKMdTYD4gU6h9hmcQG7wTt/+M5mslcDxE90P\nHvSWNgWn538hn7izD1/HsyB8I3HmznyQ2eTpJ89YLeXnFMAzXTTt2wmgUDMTCVpD\n4rfCE+TOIav5F8B5eL3t\n=fq6a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 85a184ccae3dc87a2e402d1ebedcdddf14d152c3\nparent ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783920935 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783920935 -0400\n\nfeat(code): resume threads in-TUI with `/threads -r [ID]` (#4609)\n\nThe `dcode` TUI now supports `/threads -r [ID]` to resume a previous\nthread in place, and `/clear` shows the thread you just left with a\none-step resume hint.\n\n---\n\nAfter `/clear` mints a new thread, there was no low-friction path back\nto the thread you just left — the id was dropped and only the modal\n`/threads` selector could find it again.\n\nThis adds an in-TUI equivalent of the launch-time `-r` flag rather than\na bespoke one-level `/go-back`, keeping parity with muscle memory users\nalready have and composing better:\n\n- `TextualSessionState` now records the outgoing thread as\n`previous_thread_id` on every `reset_thread` (`/clear`).\n- `/clear` output names the previous thread (with the same clickable\nLangSmith-link upgrade as the new-thread line) and prints a resume hint.\n- `/threads -r [ID]` resumes without opening the modal: bare `-r`\nreturns to the previous thread (falling back to the most recent thread\non disk), and `-r <ID>` resumes a specific thread. It reuses the\nexisting `_resume_thread` machinery, so behavior matches selecting a\nthread in the modal. Because `/threads` is an `IMMEDIATE_UI` command,\nonly the bare form bypasses the busy queue — `/threads -r …` is queued\nwhile the agent is running, so a resume never races an active turn.\n\nAutocomplete gains an `[-r [ID]]` argument hint and a splash tip\nadvertises the shortcut.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b717ea48-7edd-8049-95cc-64384c56e8a8)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T05:35:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d44267358e272553c8ece33d367514430be7c0da/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b"}]},{"sha":"ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFjMTU3MzI4MTUzMGMxNTY0ZmUwN2Y4YTIxNjA4ZTRkNGRlYzJjM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-13T02:21:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T02:21:07Z"},"message":"fix(code): remove misleading agent names from help (#4671)\n\nThe CLI help used `coder` and `researcher` as examples even though dcode\ndoes not ship those agents. This could make them look built in.\n\nThis replaces the named examples with `NAME` and `SOURCE` placeholders\nin the top-level and reset help.","tree":{"sha":"7a0733a2550f2e2b32ad82e21c69fff94f053b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7a0733a2550f2e2b32ad82e21c69fff94f053b4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVEuTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt24QADPoRyQgvVYUIQSYZnf4UC1G\n9DB1XxXWKJK//7A5YCHu4E5H8DZ71wBwIGahyeYRM1v2SKW0mNEm3U0klkZAaQCT\nFILZ4wXfv1twOPGqKGTjyGW4sX5h47MZZp1HAsL1NpFJL8JRVz6EHAK7D6TCbZrl\ntIcWIQnry3fuXqfmTPc/ZLnSrro3y/B7FC1Igy1AReuidZBIZaaBX7cEWb5piFxM\nSZqhc7hdlh+kUKmy40iOcOHQSHioOw6760R4DoqfmTKYFR1/N/9gRZUFUFqex/MK\nXLlGOcNtJ7XLOrIWV5mkc8xmXoRI76LyjjVrPUdIZH5BzCLtI2+Nahqpfmu2d9z5\npnzBKPNtZN7Hsg+hdqSvBbhlGTpoF0guJou14IAoE377GAQjCIOQqE82WwhaZhPO\nM/YYUJxi4wNLvKBa/+SukJNXNSjEmRxcZb6DofG1hgLRDF3FIcjxBWWZe5sEekgg\nFPxBQzh+DYmmul1ky58nYdDqVssFRZrq0am2puaBdzQOH9qa319dPxWYOtVwCMR4\nmHVnq5seK/W4uHR2lU0eQK7JhPk4TGUb0H0EX0xzfY/QiPDmnaq76y447YgEw+Qh\n6e6yTcZpNSy2o4VE6R36Aljq+9IQ1sZP98GIMXttdEYsGsxCr8m6X0/JWs15QXwb\n8DIeDQwtCW1epXZebyua\n=Xwbd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7a0733a2550f2e2b32ad82e21c69fff94f053b4b\nparent 14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783909267 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783909267 -0400\n\nfix(code): remove misleading agent names from help (#4671)\n\nThe CLI help used `coder` and `researcher` as examples even though dcode\ndoes not ship those agents. This could make them look built in.\n\nThis replaces the named examples with `NAME` and `SOURCE` placeholders\nin the top-level and reset help.","verified_at":"2026-07-13T02:21:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac1573281530c1564fe07f8a21608e4d4dec2c3b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f"}]},{"sha":"14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE0ZjM4NGZjMDA4M2MwN2E3ZjQ0Zjk3NTQzYjQwYjc0Y2Y5M2MxM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-12T00:01:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-12T00:01:24Z"},"message":"fix(code): skip Esc prompt-restore once output generation begins (#4582)\n\nPressing `Esc` to interrupt an agent turn now only returns the prompt to\nthe chat input if the model has not yet started generating output; once\na response has begun streaming, the prompt is left as-is.\n\n---\n\nFollow-up to #4544. That change returns an interrupted prompt to the\nchat input whenever the input is empty, but it does so even after the\nmodel has already begun producing a response. Returning the prompt at\nthat point is confusing: the model already started (or finished)\nanswering, so re-offering the text invites an accidental re-submission\nof an already-answered request.\n\nThis gates the restore on whether the turn has produced any output yet.\n`execute_task_textual` now notifies the app (via a new\n`on_output_started` adapter callback) the first time a turn emits\nstreamed text or a tool call. `DeepAgentsApp` tracks this per turn in\n`_active_turn_output_started` (reset at the start of each send) and\n`_restore_interrupted_message_to_input` skips the restore once it is\nset. The empty-input guard and the Ctrl+C behavior are unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6a02202c-6d98-6070-b0e9-c7a658b2aa05)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"92d7d3a7367040c35044dca0552f339067d1f040","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/92d7d3a7367040c35044dca0552f339067d1f040"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUtlUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADqIQADCj9Cl3GJoqolHm9iqmb6sn\nxzLqHlsni1MM3QzpTLXvAhFxecqmYQCThEF+753chiwzwp9elofKyTaxuYIuKRWs\nBVdEKSWcp5NIALnSIirv0CEVc9ICPWTFJiE/0S1TIF3/Kdevrc1M1cluVGqiIIdg\nXHyifuUSqhsG8YJFBzUsssizYsIuzSmrRYoKrHxcr5nTfaEwsxroXMMnplclSVPI\ndDcUb7gViREO4w75UBOX+ZtcQd5VcLDkt1b+ycZMMWf9W6mPZp1tq7M3Y2cJQC5m\nhloNxNSAlOCMBneAFvWC6qIhjR+1eOVSTn06fnDXxvsMFTJYVY8zEe89e0tPe8F8\nPSXVPycm4V/46g9y7/DTT5rNoJiUmwt91WR7UwCQBZwaAgRZWZdaU9yHJ9Hprwv7\nt8Gm4lay4RrzH0b8MHG/SHK+ARgzXwmfHYhsfWAWixhBMLdMbD3IepdTSLhoL11o\nqQXGkZI+9QdQaBeAbhzKcIptg3ZurK3WJs8jcK9sN/u/N0qy7DprkaGKPaGMA5hI\n8JPzVAUnjIr5XXH6LrzNK5aw/ENKlXjPTFQauRXfJK/1zMDRaAUK48CQQGXuPFca\nq/m/SQceQYs+rhsdyCGrAK6mFvkdTmfFKyM6Ct6kvoYMUbMgcxQBJsmvm9kIoasP\nFRwttD9WIjPZ6Q+vO/+t\n=UlxC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 92d7d3a7367040c35044dca0552f339067d1f040\nparent c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783814484 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783814484 -0400\n\nfix(code): skip Esc prompt-restore once output generation begins (#4582)\n\nPressing `Esc` to interrupt an agent turn now only returns the prompt to\nthe chat input if the model has not yet started generating output; once\na response has begun streaming, the prompt is left as-is.\n\n---\n\nFollow-up to #4544. That change returns an interrupted prompt to the\nchat input whenever the input is empty, but it does so even after the\nmodel has already begun producing a response. Returning the prompt at\nthat point is confusing: the model already started (or finished)\nanswering, so re-offering the text invites an accidental re-submission\nof an already-answered request.\n\nThis gates the restore on whether the turn has produced any output yet.\n`execute_task_textual` now notifies the app (via a new\n`on_output_started` adapter callback) the first time a turn emits\nstreamed text or a tool call. `DeepAgentsApp` tracks this per turn in\n`_active_turn_output_started` (reset at the start of each send) and\n`_restore_interrupted_message_to_input` skips the restore once it is\nset. The empty-input guard and the Ctrl+C behavior are unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6a02202c-6d98-6070-b0e9-c7a658b2aa05)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-12T00:01:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14f384fc0083c07a7f44f97543b40b74cf93c13f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020"}]},{"sha":"c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM1MzQ1Y2MwNGNkODEwYzYyMzhlNDJkZmJmYTE0NDk3YWUxYjkwMjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-11T23:39:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-11T23:39:05Z"},"message":"perf(code): load MCP servers concurrently during graph build (#4659)\n\nDeep Agents Code now discovers MCP servers concurrently, cutting initial\ngraph-load time when multiple MCP servers are configured.\n\n---\n\nInitial Deep Agents Code graph load scaled linearly with the number of\nconfigured MCP servers because `_load_tools_from_config` ran per-server\npreflight and tool discovery sequentially — the dominant contributor to\nstartup time. This runs independent per-server\npreflight/connection-build and discovery concurrently under a bounded\nsemaphore (`_MCP_LOAD_CONCURRENCY = 8`) while keeping deterministic\nserver/tool ordering, per-server error isolation, auth, cleanup, and\nsession-manager semantics unchanged. The adapter-import warmup was moved\ninto `_load_tools_from_config`, so MCP adapters are imported only when\nat least one active MCP server exists.\n\nMeasured (simulated, 0.4s preflight + 0.6s discovery per server): 6\nservers 6.02s → 1.01s (~6x); 10 servers 10.03s → 2.01s (limit=8). Tool\nordering and `server_infos` ordering verified identical to the\nsequential loader. The slow-load warning is untouched and no public APIs\nchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8dfe87f3-154b-050b-93a0-4a2a9af39fee)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c997c4eb32b32e22ce73facb4a891995547718a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c997c4eb32b32e22ce73facb4a891995547718a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUtQZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/YwQAANy8FWD30/qb0v1vX3q4Efg\nWSxiQHdyrzokgPWHmyI5Qx6zm3kJNOZhwoaAmhs8QUMxXcniPru2yCqeqlRusu9Z\nC1SifYiRebq+Dlz4E9bxnNxW6LU5xmYtL2U2v8AvYjcVN7swVV57Wbk/9S7L7Ex5\njXk0dIeABigwFhtLsaH+NyUOQ/yitLd2XMMG4UhHrFpSmGeGKfONz+o2FAecaiCg\nKcuv9LqUbMg3ZWcmiLpF3yRH8zVWu/aWTP75Awgty26IIhan4nJT2q0L5K+TQcyk\nhYF/zNt1RKk+ck2amiZbjaKuu0QMAFOKwCH7Yrq0PhtN+VabYZXGf1wBxYUD02wC\nO3PmDgBpPt8Km8RnFjXmrAEIL1ANt0LgE4eMgq2ZQzYqAMCsUGbZRoOY396Azuh2\nbTcE0uyAZCzik+aJWsiw+AApH0s+KO976DWx3/PAC2T6afStMkqsEmNBupS8WMT4\nUxTZiqjv7ezZRk9iuiXYz4uB5Htzwz2XagPRgoeiqoBJ97UIZc5juILk1KCFNw/C\nmLZvjSbwi/7vwbX/XZsKHPXT+lTnk37NdO+TNORT6HDP6e/3XFRvP1oMcBVkJAmL\nRYLogwFZayQpol/ORiB1zs6vTjHurAlPZD3ROWOFBbhzqhxt5ACTT9SrNlsP2tOJ\n5qu4QNRkpGY8Vtl/6iBF\n=Pcr1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c997c4eb32b32e22ce73facb4a891995547718a4\nparent 1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783813145 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783813145 -0400\n\nperf(code): load MCP servers concurrently during graph build (#4659)\n\nDeep Agents Code now discovers MCP servers concurrently, cutting initial\ngraph-load time when multiple MCP servers are configured.\n\n---\n\nInitial Deep Agents Code graph load scaled linearly with the number of\nconfigured MCP servers because `_load_tools_from_config` ran per-server\npreflight and tool discovery sequentially — the dominant contributor to\nstartup time. This runs independent per-server\npreflight/connection-build and discovery concurrently under a bounded\nsemaphore (`_MCP_LOAD_CONCURRENCY = 8`) while keeping deterministic\nserver/tool ordering, per-server error isolation, auth, cleanup, and\nsession-manager semantics unchanged. The adapter-import warmup was moved\ninto `_load_tools_from_config`, so MCP adapters are imported only when\nat least one active MCP server exists.\n\nMeasured (simulated, 0.4s preflight + 0.6s discovery per server): 6\nservers 6.02s → 1.01s (~6x); 10 servers 10.03s → 2.01s (limit=8). Tool\nordering and `server_infos` ordering verified identical to the\nsequential loader. The slow-load warning is untouched and no public APIs\nchanged.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8dfe87f3-154b-050b-93a0-4a2a9af39fee)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-11T23:39:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c5345cc04cd810c6238e42dfbfa14497ae1b9020/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1"}]},{"sha":"1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFjMDhkMjcwNWY3M2Y2ODcwNjEwODQ5ZTAwOTEwYjk0NDU4YWNjZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-11T23:32:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-11T23:32:08Z"},"message":"feat(code): support Fireworks `/routers` model ids (#4591)\n\nFireworks router model ids (`accounts/fireworks/routers/...`) now\ndisplay compactly in the status bar and support `/effort` reasoning\ncontrols, matching individual Fireworks model ids.\n\n---\n\nFireworks exposes two fully-qualified model-id forms: individual models\n(`accounts/fireworks/models/...`) and routers that dispatch across\nmodels (`accounts/fireworks/routers/...`, e.g.\n`accounts/fireworks/routers/glm-5p1-fast`; see\n[models.dev](https://models.dev/providers/fireworks-ai/)). Previously\nonly the `models/` form was recognized, so router ids rendered with the\nfull prefix in the status bar and never qualified for reasoning-effort\ncontrols.\n\nThis teaches the two places that key off the qualified prefix to accept\nboth forms:\n\n- `ModelLabel`'s `PROVIDER_PREFIX_STRIPS` now strips the `routers/`\nprefix for compact status-bar display.\n- `_classify_reasoning_provider` gates `/effort` on a shared\n`_FIREWORKS_MODEL_ID_PREFIXES` tuple covering both forms, so router\nmodels get the same family-based effort support as individual models.\n\nThe model-family logic (Kimi/GLM/DeepSeek) is substring-based and\nalready works for either form.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/29503e81-c1ee-65e7-b10d-56661b75aa89)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"90a28e0a4e783a1537669ee4ecc2a4eec8adf832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/90a28e0a4e783a1537669ee4ecc2a4eec8adf832"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUtJ4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIksQAH9LjcsPyqkZp0Ni3mBRIiYX\ntUpMHnArwdHzFQxo31p5pwfwoeBipu8JGo3QZW5V9rHfXlO8U/5s8PMxp7OvYAqi\nXE7hpduFBK1Ob/0/QbnrlOSSRMRVvyUQH1LfDWSd+qrZdW4+gt31BvkayBKLaWRh\nDEH4e58LuuYgUJ2lFYUMLTWoE8edy7oYUoX+yzyvrKty4f65iTGqXrnreNjLDq8F\n5Tu682v9794EVqdaHex468TTvuJcLxlYCZob6s88WltqnmzFnejapTKHGYDoXet2\nYTkxwBg2JetaUu8MdvI8bBWwEbUoqQiIyj3+VxtzJaP9s2gZIog3xmIvEcXWA0Vc\nc312R61W7ENgU0f4CdD0KCTkY0/jreIaDIvZOdHPyxpC4JqRDHRrQUP1hagbCz2B\ndGDC1Lczn3ZdlsY1TVVpj24IkN4OhCyrhiR/UKLJesh87Ie3JYfU4YxpHdC+G6y5\n7rRBsPaPmGFuusCAcCr6djLRDlzd/i6f7LZ7HZUJVBmp34jMjMxujZ5NlXkD3JYS\nYL5JHLkjUOtBD9nWe1jBOueek5iYM6gIGs4ma6gsfihWM2MkFH6njvk9+vCbj/N8\np2t0b/TxPEmscmJ5TqyyVcqS98b8063VIojq/N6RVmsvVGcGbLTbqzLvMF23CV4l\nN/PEEqB6wgkY6fRE8WLs\n=dpgj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 90a28e0a4e783a1537669ee4ecc2a4eec8adf832\nparent 518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783812728 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783812728 -0400\n\nfeat(code): support Fireworks `/routers` model ids (#4591)\n\nFireworks router model ids (`accounts/fireworks/routers/...`) now\ndisplay compactly in the status bar and support `/effort` reasoning\ncontrols, matching individual Fireworks model ids.\n\n---\n\nFireworks exposes two fully-qualified model-id forms: individual models\n(`accounts/fireworks/models/...`) and routers that dispatch across\nmodels (`accounts/fireworks/routers/...`, e.g.\n`accounts/fireworks/routers/glm-5p1-fast`; see\n[models.dev](https://models.dev/providers/fireworks-ai/)). Previously\nonly the `models/` form was recognized, so router ids rendered with the\nfull prefix in the status bar and never qualified for reasoning-effort\ncontrols.\n\nThis teaches the two places that key off the qualified prefix to accept\nboth forms:\n\n- `ModelLabel`'s `PROVIDER_PREFIX_STRIPS` now strips the `routers/`\nprefix for compact status-bar display.\n- `_classify_reasoning_provider` gates `/effort` on a shared\n`_FIREWORKS_MODEL_ID_PREFIXES` tuple covering both forms, so router\nmodels get the same family-based effort support as individual models.\n\nThe model-family logic (Kimi/GLM/DeepSeek) is substring-based and\nalready works for either form.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/29503e81-c1ee-65e7-b10d-56661b75aa89)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-11T23:32:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c08d2705f73f6870610849e00910b94458accf1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f"}]},{"sha":"518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUxOGMzMjJlN2RkYTg0MGI1YTc0MDU0MWFmYzg5NTUxNmE3NDkyNWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-11T23:22:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-11T23:22:28Z"},"message":"feat(code): `/model` Ctrl+N toggle for names vs raw specs (#4592)\n\nThe `/model` selector now supports `Ctrl+N` to toggle rows between\nfriendly model names and raw `provider:model` IDs.\n\n---\n\nThe `/model` selector always rendered rows with friendly display names,\nwith no way to see or copy the canonical `provider:model` spec. This\nadds a `Ctrl+N` keybinding that toggles every row between the friendly\nname and the raw spec, mirroring the `/theme` picker's label/key toggle.\n`Ctrl+N` (rather than a bare `n` like `/theme`) is used because the\nselector's filter input is always focused, so a plain letter would be\nswallowed as filter text.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6733d56c-39b6-2387-4daf-02ac68097a13)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e16fdff2facc7d1d98b2ac89f49099dbc766cd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8e16fdff2facc7d1d98b2ac89f49099dbc766cd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUtA0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApvwQACciM4mmWo91vEzFzIfq72Fq\nToUE82gWZBZW5bln6BOf39SZjLDfFKRsymzW88wui0kDz6O8QDAR5gk/WHCSQxzx\nUTMhpTyqQh6rAS+WRB8akkah8RfabqlAvsEhPjuC+CtghH/wOl6/igOw/LS44d1B\nzkpkDthX5KpEb+tCdJ3E5EwjDagsfzM2a0NR3Ag+iCxKF/v9COEV6RDCEn3+3L+P\nEqYsw/jkrEjHn1GUr3Es9V1jxDm4KDzw0M2lJ7joCz0k7JDrPHi1ojakK5/+X9DC\n/wKQ3NI1rcaf/oFdNKVe7VFCsPKnvWn+mQXCU7Ec+V4nVoExCZQ98yPU0l+6dMU2\n4iaAdCfUXirKVYwUwzfs8sVAoqwxjs0ZcOmsR7npaFWMbO2ZinU8fGIx1BWTFM71\nPTxk40Ea6mHPUlWQwPJLSKZTt/geEV1d1Rc7FIXZmEiEhDB/aFtzgzSSC3/+t6ik\nDbya/7B7cq91Fp1QQt0cOtJZhwcwqCq1kZWpD5Bf1ZNLj2AxGHg7L6XzlE+sYZ6Z\nI+yDxh5U4FC408i4hfwkB5tR6BgxLRBvbVjCF9/SI9cpVYENJckU/8OTZjp1/3uC\nBMuxcmVffBEeqhE9UH2tvX9gTYiSTdhfdq1N9KUYClFpbi/iqO/TSuZu9B9H+KlJ\nblherC1qr3y/Fn/lC9ol\n=i2JL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8e16fdff2facc7d1d98b2ac89f49099dbc766cd2\nparent c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783812148 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783812148 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `/model` Ctrl+N toggle for names vs raw specs (#4592)\n\nThe `/model` selector now supports `Ctrl+N` to toggle rows between\nfriendly model names and raw `provider:model` IDs.\n\n---\n\nThe `/model` selector always rendered rows with friendly display names,\nwith no way to see or copy the canonical `provider:model` spec. This\nadds a `Ctrl+N` keybinding that toggles every row between the friendly\nname and the raw spec, mirroring the `/theme` picker's label/key toggle.\n`Ctrl+N` (rather than a bare `n` like `/theme`) is used because the\nselector's filter input is always focused, so a plain letter would be\nswallowed as filter text.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6733d56c-39b6-2387-4daf-02ac68097a13)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-11T23:22:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/518c322e7dda840b5a740541afc895516a74925f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87"}]},{"sha":"c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM5YjdhYzIwNzUyZTQyNzBkMjg2YjRhZjNmY2Y3MTBlN2U1YmVlODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-11T22:56:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-11T22:56:44Z"},"message":"feat(code): add `-s` alias for `--skill` (#4620)\n\n`dcode` now accepts `-s` as a short alias for `--skill`, e.g. `dcode -s\ncode-review -m 'review this patch'`.\n\n---\n\n`-s` was previously unused across the entire `dcode` CLI surface (no\ntop-level flag or subparser claimed it), so it's a safe, ergonomic alias\nfor the existing `--skill` startup flag. This gives skill invocation the\nsame short-flag convenience as other common options and makes `dcode -s\n<name> [-m task]` a quick way to auto-invoke a skill at startup.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/577c1ebd-4ca4-47db-8244-99b4d2f15112)\n\nCo-authored-by: Harrison Chase <11986836+hwchase17@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee9a2ba83e2926b39eee096c0dbbef8b2df23e7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ee9a2ba83e2926b39eee096c0dbbef8b2df23e7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUsosCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa14QAHooMltR+k1A6dcv1AUPnKUr\n2Q3NbOGTQwy1YSctAzpj4WLStONgZ0xxA5m2867TzdUq8CmW/upqKLFObxltd17n\nrDd6/d+V4Rb++/+1Zw9Uq46hfDx8G7bYwMgSMkHGKhh9HdAPnjWJjVZ63DGsa753\n0J8kB1JXM3U3J9Tp0sjawzoBHrSyvBVPZaDdPlvrt4uiTMuvmyB2//zFjL9d5fgL\nMkaoCf0SDp091fR9jTEjSZeg7R49rYdnBjqFE2HE8d7vNScivHvHzgnGbbWK+VU9\nkV28PDSxefLq8mLIG4KMk/+zSD95FdW9g9XlARyYFS1AZcdDffRBG5xzTgPK5OCp\nK9fsxZ1dlO/sRJSX4epUZyXnj5SQxHNF+sI98tmjbvMX3AV9KdvBqGrpYnr1tr1/\nHMN1b5Q7d5iXUwZNGyii8O4TNZ3li+TGFNVL0JRaQf3aCwrd6ZOjvfKZmxSYCDqa\nZnO9PKowHaDn71TzishRFhp6kylI6ARzP6mZunBzKA7pJVGzvw+xUCDOIdSXQmbV\nMlWsYIbCa7LyNZZSgSderfYb4R4R9Xxthf+3cYC500sgpJBwy7oB8d7/aNnTQqWX\nUQb2KcbV/6IbbsZ1n3d23YPSFq5j2/cn6njFFnRL1lSyMThpxjOtvwVzUJiHnKX+\nC1peQKpcYqkMIIiRdGI0\n=3U0F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee9a2ba83e2926b39eee096c0dbbef8b2df23e7c\nparent e9c61304460baab2058a667198600cadef516954\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783810604 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783810604 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add `-s` alias for `--skill` (#4620)\n\n`dcode` now accepts `-s` as a short alias for `--skill`, e.g. `dcode -s\ncode-review -m 'review this patch'`.\n\n---\n\n`-s` was previously unused across the entire `dcode` CLI surface (no\ntop-level flag or subparser claimed it), so it's a safe, ergonomic alias\nfor the existing `--skill` startup flag. This gives skill invocation the\nsame short-flag convenience as other common options and makes `dcode -s\n<name> [-m task]` a quick way to auto-invoke a skill at startup.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/577c1ebd-4ca4-47db-8244-99b4d2f15112)\n\nCo-authored-by: Harrison Chase <11986836+hwchase17@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-11T22:56:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c9b7ac20752e4270d286b4af3fcf710e7e5bee87/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.