34a86be","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFkNzQ1M2Q0ZGZkM2U0N2EyNmRmNDAwYjVjNGIzZjdmZjM0YTg2YmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-10T22:19:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T22:19:39Z"},"message":"docs(acp): call out `dcode --acp` option (#4645)\n\nThe `libs/acp` README only documents running a bare/general Deep Agent,\nbut many users just want a ready-made coding agent. `deepagents-code`\n(`dcode`) can already expose its prebuilt coding agent as an ACP server\nvia `dcode --acp`, so this adds a top-of-README tip and a dedicated\nsection covering install, Zed configuration, and model selection with\n`--model`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4228d9b3-8ca4-4d7f-9a12-e734d40b8b9e)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ffb8361d80d9f1fbc6f22fa5332332074f53683","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7ffb8361d80d9f1fbc6f22fa5332332074f53683"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ad7453d4dfd3e47a26df400b5c4b3f7ff34a86be","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUW/7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbmAQAC9Re7AOtkUJeLoGnbvIVq8a\nhWXRwxyMdNiq/XgMdyr3h19js32aH9SQjD26/GKgbT+7NOXkaDC3qzuX3HBueSV4\nyvwYSAf4oZ9M2xgq6azbhEk/90oKiFw0PPtsdnfs47QI80obpk+rrbEyCQKev1hG\nriE5IKSCqAVyt583uNe+GuPKndCIRBFqnn0k5ESnuu33d3vmHy8q/n6aMI9aX6TR\neQNaktfS8wg6DA5kb/vzFUi/XUjdSX92QC8xItuqKHQpIuOyFk38/BlCAi6TXYqa\nzNxqL1RoIRXtEG2TJRnrAJ9yr3O0ceF+Q/DxYgHRXiEdK2T8/ohuR5r37f46q9/t\nxgZf0GFTBqNtZZG6VTriCPONMZO2ZwuyWBfMK/1+NeELQg0VLu020nbXUSrppptE\nQEGJcVPYZEkTg0rBxkCONolCYiqaqAztjhDZF32q9i0fzJ8MzrsAJCoBmkTJjmoJ\nTV9ijSpaSx13v1bW73gcuCBIzOvLcr0KnxlXAIcEls0jB73o1ouO+MC98jU16iAb\nDN594RzAEY4BCggw3iHpjX6uD1TxoQINF7PamFLZ8G7CylaF/kcpizSxlNWUHars\nlVn4xgX9l35vXFuZfTlYBwE2uF2z1QGWFE+iJfep0953skGL8ss7gH6d4zvbw7Gg\npy0eRtY970SFUvyuTmuf\n=V+oT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ffb8361d80d9f1fbc6f22fa5332332074f53683\nparent c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783721979 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783721979 -0400\n\ndocs(acp): call out `dcode --acp` option (#4645)\n\nThe `libs/acp` README only documents running a bare/general Deep Agent,\nbut many users just want a ready-made coding agent. `deepagents-code`\n(`dcode`) can already expose its prebuilt coding agent as an ACP server\nvia `dcode --acp`, so this adds a top-of-README tip and a dedicated\nsection covering install, Zed configuration, and model selection with\n`--model`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4228d9b3-8ca4-4d7f-9a12-e734d40b8b9e)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-10T22:19:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ad7453d4dfd3e47a26df400b5c4b3f7ff34a86be","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ad7453d4dfd3e47a26df400b5c4b3f7ff34a86be","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ad7453d4dfd3e47a26df400b5c4b3f7ff34a86be/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf"}]},{"sha":"c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM4N2U4ZmU1NThmMGI1NmRiYTNjZTkyYTk5NGNjNmFhYzBjOTNjY2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-10T21:39:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T21:39:20Z"},"message":"docs(code): warn that `system_prompt` override bypasses generated prompt (#4644)\n\nThe `system_prompt` parameter of `create_cli_agent` was documented only\nas \"override the default system prompt,\" which understates its effect.\nPassing an explicit value replaces the auto-generated prompt *entirely*,\ndropping all interpolated dynamic context (model identity, working\ndirectory, sandbox-vs-local execution mode, skills path, and\ninteractive-vs-headless guidance), and rendering\n`sandbox_type`/`interactive` inert for prompt purposes. This clarifies\nthe behavior in general terms — a reader does not need to know the\ninternal prompt-builder helper to understand the tradeoff.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/25d7a0c1-a171-ddde-8532-4424d56578bd)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4320fa56006134907c0c075514c49bca6d409b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f4320fa56006134907c0c075514c49bca6d409b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUWaICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIcIQAGIYebfVFNS7lk/sd4F4He7U\nAxcS1u82mEUzoqupCowrE6CFB/fWFPMXAkmdwN0olkv6UrnUbZJdMkmkF4+NmX/w\nqqjCzTzvmuvBVx9UEYymAGhDIOQfOIado2w0A0nCtbZgTYK4sgxNtYUcByASS1UF\nwpMKHhPY1Cs6XUYqyZsNWGp6AGtW8Pz7sE0272hPDp0RzUaNANVXQeiklZ1vV6o+\nOXz0A350+b17d0elBLHPltTNhXJ638VlUKdaJ60x74My+X32l2TG7hClQKXkmiZc\nQsv6N+4y4rdv4+WXCgeRTMYOwGwVbYswulFskBGNgJjFeR2cae2R1VWlqIlDsB3G\n3F7v3wSmjRh00lD4MO9QrEtkasznousD2kFfh7KdpR4Mb4x/dxtMlvop/ovjmw8i\nvzjLLkbjQOF22YB3UkSdQB3IzNMn/vtuy8EWZBk88EC28CJhUZHl48f+OE/a7XiD\nk+31CpYZLG3U3j/p+6adX0g6TrvWRfRGpK7kyFt+PbGz98z5oxVW25hedm6+GfLq\nrMN8tkp4nWokp0xIMoD2JWsVAzhcvpmXu7uECwzMY5WoMP5qedTNSdUDkpfFaLsY\nIx1ASP3EfuG3D6jEJpxkmlnYPZsv8+pqVanADoE1VR06/gvN6NpoRBrWxOJgDMIG\nNPLbAOlMEiFqgO2x9kWC\n=ZIRf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f4320fa56006134907c0c075514c49bca6d409b0\nparent 4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783719560 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783719560 -0400\n\ndocs(code): warn that `system_prompt` override bypasses generated prompt (#4644)\n\nThe `system_prompt` parameter of `create_cli_agent` was documented only\nas \"override the default system prompt,\" which understates its effect.\nPassing an explicit value replaces the auto-generated prompt *entirely*,\ndropping all interpolated dynamic context (model identity, working\ndirectory, sandbox-vs-local execution mode, skills path, and\ninteractive-vs-headless guidance), and rendering\n`sandbox_type`/`interactive` inert for prompt purposes. This clarifies\nthe behavior in general terms — a reader does not need to know the\ninternal prompt-builder helper to understand the tradeoff.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/25d7a0c1-a171-ddde-8532-4424d56578bd)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-10T21:39:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c87e8fe558f0b56dba3ce92a994cc6aac0c93ccf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262"}]},{"sha":"4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjMWNlMDU5NDFjMTQwMDYyZjNkMDQxZGI3OWVmZjU5MmJlMTYyNjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-10T19:46:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T19:46:45Z"},"message":"feat(evals): add context-retrieval-evals Harbor dataset (30 calibrated Context-Bench tasks) (#4637)\n\nAdds `context-retrieval-evals`: a 30-task Harbor dataset measuring\nmulti-file retrieval + reasoning, derived from Context-Bench (cloud\nsuite). Each task ships the whole corpus so the agent must\nretrieve/join/aggregate rather than guess which files matter.\n\n**Tasks — frozen from calibration** (Opus 4.8 / bare harness / 3\nrollouts): 5 easy (solved cold) · 9 medium (intermittent) · 16 hard\n(failed cold). Context-Bench is bimodal on Opus 4.8, so tiers are\nassigned by measured pass-rate; each task's pass-rate + what it tests is\ndocumented in the dataset README as tier justification.\n\n**Adapter** (`harbor_adapters/contextbench`): generates task dirs from\nthe vendored `filesystem_cloud.jsonl`.\n\n**Corpus single-sourced**: the 64.7K-line corpus lives once under\n`vendor/files/`; per-task `environment/files/` is git-ignored and\nregenerated via `--populate` before runs (CI + local), keeping the diff\nsmall.\n\n**`harbor.yml`**: local-dataset sharding, `n_retries` (→ Harbor\n`--max-retries`), and a corpus-populate step.","tree":{"sha":"231c5cb005814d624849f015b9582221a61c458e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/231c5cb005814d624849f015b9582221a61c458e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUUwlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuFMQAKhgHRmOZehulXPcPdLFwU7f\n1OTYS3JnHsXR9D+/DN8unWGcvMPpfexos6C1EWaxk2Df7MYH+Cq8IaVPf3D6hQyf\nEQwn+BeCBpp/GiIqFHGz7W0u+tE06mdg8zI1Mb+JCZ2TTUFw4phx0gpDEJF/JXZE\nYaDBPvPcVQCSsf+yJCiLmULNOhzgsa67InYGETesgtyUvUo5dcgyyaBVoZnJzM2t\nXIWpDfckRsV6sFnp86dJ9o0M7u/mZZkpy/Ec9QZlf931xM0up739dFKJctdxoeJs\nLsvpzRjvsanI5G2rQDSAIkFRDTCT2xmmoBWNHzgp6gTnTXZ2bvH2ybi/zbmvzYJl\n8XaYrLIqGRUo9p7O2GwkLGxPA2IbpOC9YD4B4Lh9YHgvHi9zzWz0DUpiMkR8dfeJ\nsZr8YCN6LfViai5qGDZ5+N2brJPInzaYH8ae+ixcFCgqs3+HMXGpt3dVVB2y9koW\nl/OYqnh6F9rADC03G5qndFYbpNJhMskMsSoLr55IVEjul3JpjKmZyGn3vfzHejUZ\n73tt/s7HOzS14WbJMqRwIaUftDiLfAqwu4bCtrE2VrZ2CPC55VVGi3x2VVL5KyL5\ny/+xV3nZo/Y+/GFZmqgrgZNIjuiF1Fjemfqebtxbln9w7aac6KajTIsPCyYUqABE\nAa9Or1BJfOC2/QkG0BR4\n=7cza\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 231c5cb005814d624849f015b9582221a61c458e\nparent b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1783712805 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783712805 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): add context-retrieval-evals Harbor dataset (30 calibrated Context-Bench tasks) (#4637)\n\nAdds `context-retrieval-evals`: a 30-task Harbor dataset measuring\nmulti-file retrieval + reasoning, derived from Context-Bench (cloud\nsuite). Each task ships the whole corpus so the agent must\nretrieve/join/aggregate rather than guess which files matter.\n\n**Tasks — frozen from calibration** (Opus 4.8 / bare harness / 3\nrollouts): 5 easy (solved cold) · 9 medium (intermittent) · 16 hard\n(failed cold). Context-Bench is bimodal on Opus 4.8, so tiers are\nassigned by measured pass-rate; each task's pass-rate + what it tests is\ndocumented in the dataset README as tier justification.\n\n**Adapter** (`harbor_adapters/contextbench`): generates task dirs from\nthe vendored `filesystem_cloud.jsonl`.\n\n**Corpus single-sourced**: the 64.7K-line corpus lives once under\n`vendor/files/`; per-task `environment/files/` is git-ignored and\nregenerated via `--populate` before runs (CI + local), keeping the diff\nsmall.\n\n**`harbor.yml`**: local-dataset sharding, `n_retries` (→ Harbor\n`--max-retries`), and a corpus-populate step.","verified_at":"2026-07-10T19:46:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c1ce05941c140062f3d041db79eff592be16262/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8"}]},{"sha":"b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI0ZmMwNzNhYzNiZTFjOWQ5ZTJkYTNiZWQ0OThmZjZkMWQwY2U3YTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-10T19:30:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T19:30:17Z"},"message":"feat(evals): tau3-subset curated difficulty-tiered dataset (#4636)\n\nAdds **`tau3-subset`** — a curated 30-task slice of\n`sierra-research/tau3-bench` (telecom + banking_knowledge), selectable\nas a Harbor dataset, for probing agent conversation behavior.\n\n- **`deepagents_evals/tau3_subset.py`** — 30 tasks (`task_id`, `tier`,\n`justification`) + a derived `INCLUDE_TASKS` constant CI reads.\n- **`harbor.yml`** — a `tau3-subset` dataset option that pulls\n`INCLUDE_TASKS`, runs against `sierra-research/tau3-bench` under a\ndedicated `tau3-subset` LangSmith dataset, and gates `OPENAI_API_KEY` on\ntau3 so the gpt-5.2 user-simulator/verifier authenticate.\n\nTiers are the measured `claude-opus-4-8` pass rate (3 rollouts, full\ntimeout) — easy 3/3, medium 1–2/3, hard 0/3 → **2 / 7 / 21**. Living\nselection: re-tier as the model/tasks change.\n\n_Note: LangSmith tau3 runs need the Harbor docker-daemon fix\n(harbor-framework/harbor#2272) via `harbor_package_override` until it\nmerges._\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d20d84c95523949f3a9d804b1314bc33a0c7d75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1d20d84c95523949f3a9d804b1314bc33a0c7d75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUUhJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhv4QADY4DejZGC5RTjxR1ZdEF5HT\n+t7Lb5Z1GN8B0bOQn9cAwoGMjRIgx0nTIyY38Wxlq40kN5fWkXeTrfAiDK2tdJ7l\ndwCa4IEmLUCof3mAiHgZENmIFo5zyY3C5WpsE8v9Qrw93Zc2lWwtTC0woi4fme3L\nVwXV8J8dx7CWtUk7iquixmcHdScoz4lwc3voYS8SgDf1LSDMNue5khZo/VqqHKQr\nPlDctHyCTR6lVGbKheY1WmS+k1Y/+TLu52ggho+EMGXCv7IrKLHf7hNT5zI/iwcl\nKRl+v2w3oLuYUHo4Ju4lbCqqLWsMRFYuCuxR+YDJMMWQKB9jGu03cmVULHSXO2lI\nzSG4cia7x3y2VgQ+B6Hx9SKcz/IpgACUcj1UI6accGlrroxHbsLh1HlGyNp75ION\nSo17wOT4p6Dcu2F35nrNhpELWXD5C7A0rPMOiNo+lZrpgbSxh5EsAQvoICBn3vxt\nRVIPWWQbbCigvdVVKspd4tVkDmGDfmHyvJlGtPVeU7VLlSc6WnkOB468tewiyAAa\nJ1mAmfjRPdTNWvYiGyFC/JPpfAfL0ZIv7YYXrcV0dINgbEGg03ma2HtIWOxmekk6\n7Vx3/4c4DAfw4iqmJz5C4GTHupUB2ki34n+wsUcD4VQfmK+ycBfgogAy71auEXdq\naEVbGuehPWgpjW8zHOVs\n=bbPA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1d20d84c95523949f3a9d804b1314bc33a0c7d75\nparent 57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1783711817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783711817 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): tau3-subset curated difficulty-tiered dataset (#4636)\n\nAdds **`tau3-subset`** — a curated 30-task slice of\n`sierra-research/tau3-bench` (telecom + banking_knowledge), selectable\nas a Harbor dataset, for probing agent conversation behavior.\n\n- **`deepagents_evals/tau3_subset.py`** — 30 tasks (`task_id`, `tier`,\n`justification`) + a derived `INCLUDE_TASKS` constant CI reads.\n- **`harbor.yml`** — a `tau3-subset` dataset option that pulls\n`INCLUDE_TASKS`, runs against `sierra-research/tau3-bench` under a\ndedicated `tau3-subset` LangSmith dataset, and gates `OPENAI_API_KEY` on\ntau3 so the gpt-5.2 user-simulator/verifier authenticate.\n\nTiers are the measured `claude-opus-4-8` pass rate (3 rollouts, full\ntimeout) — easy 3/3, medium 1–2/3, hard 0/3 → **2 / 7 / 21**. Living\nselection: re-tier as the model/tasks change.\n\n_Note: LangSmith tau3 runs need the Harbor docker-daemon fix\n(harbor-framework/harbor#2272) via `harbor_package_override` until it\nmerges._\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-10T19:30:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b4fc073ac3be1c9d9e2da3bed498ff6d1d0ce7a8/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821"}]},{"sha":"57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU3OTE4ZjZjZWE4MzQ4ZDY0NDU0ZmUyYzhjMmE5MjAwODkxZDQ4MjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-10T19:16:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T19:16:47Z"},"message":"ci(harbor,evals): add Harbor Index dataset + per-dispatch shard aggregation (`pass@K` / `avg@K`) (#4633)\n\n## Summary\n\nReworks #4630: instead of a separate 783-line workflow fork, make Harbor\nIndex a dataset in the shared `harbor.yml` and add general per-dispatch\nshard aggregation.\n\n- **Dataset option** — adds `harbor-index/harbor-index-1.0` to the\n`dataset` dropdown. It runs through the existing model matrix / sharding\n/ LangSmith tracing / concurrency like any other dataset (no fork).\n- **`aggregate` job** — merges the per-shard result artifacts\n(`shard-*`) via `.github/scripts/aggregate_shards.py` into:\n- `summary.json` + `per_task.jsonl` reporting **`pass@K`** (fraction of\ntasks that passed ≥1 of K rollouts) and **`avg@K`** (passing rollouts /\ntotal rollouts), where K = `rollouts_per_task` (keys are serialized\ndynamically, e.g. `pass@3` / `avg@3`);\n- **one combined zip** per run (`harbor-combined-<dataset-slug>`), after\nwhich the per-shard intermediates are deleted.\n- **Eval-a-model defaults + caps** — defaults set to rollouts 3 /\nconcurrency 4 / n_shards 10; a `prep` step caps n_shards ≤ 10,\nconcurrency ≤ 4, and models × shards × concurrency ≤ 40. Per-shard\nuploads renamed `harbor-*` → `shard-*` so the aggregate job can glob\nthem.\n\nThis is the reusable building block for a future \"measure a model across\n3 categories\" harness (autonomous / conversation / retrieval): each\ncategory is a `harbor.yml` run emitting its own `summary.json`, which an\norchestrator can roll into an overall score.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit tests `.github/scripts/test_aggregate_shards.py` (run by CI's\n`check-release-options` job): 8/8 pass.\n- End-to-end smoke run on this branch (haiku / langsmith / 2 shards /\n`n_tasks=2`): `prep` → 2 shards → `aggregate` all green; produced a\ncorrect `summary.json` (`pass@2` / `avg@2`) and a single combined zip,\nwith the per-shard intermediates deleted. Workflow plumbing validated;\nthe two sampled tasks errored for the reasons in **Out of scope** below.\n\n## Out of scope / follow-ups\n\n- Aggregation is **single-model** for now (errors on >1 model);\nmulti-model grouping and the caps/defaults interaction are deferred.\n- The `harbor-index/bix-ordinal-logit-covid` task errors with\n`EnvironmentStartTimeoutError` on a **cold** build — its 7 GB\n`chenzizhao/bixbench` base image plus a build-time HuggingFace capsule\ndownload exceed the task's own 1800s env-start budget. That's a\n**separate dataset/infra issue** (mirror + digest-pin the base image,\nreuse/pre-warm the snapshot, or pre-bake per-task images) and is not\naddressed here.\n\nSupersedes #4630.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"781a3cf21ae405bb34242e19d2c1ba74cacbb247","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/781a3cf21ae405bb34242e19d2c1ba74cacbb247"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUUUfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzIMQAA04a9I+hNgLIg+EAeTn5U2y\nwJucCuQBWeBYeUpxbBPR7Tq1UhVeL2iCru0+zGpvKIBTq8toQ3jJ/rUaLIAaTL03\nYDDar1j7zsRbl8Ph2gsMxgu869737BevVzOIZApysrtqgrVjgn66YdhTpn7eQdBF\n8HRlqjuqVDJkc+Rjrw7pcBYk+vjcW7W6NoF2dqImXwQlmoAJ8adDUv7fzH3/kX66\n99PbjqN04o6NCOjUzTMON4Vi2+MXX6iO+Us6mgA4pfPjmjY61d3ZfdimSF1kh43h\nKyztJZUR1lTzPYMZUnawK70jd5CRmkYEr6hIVt9JCE6W59dd30sOkto6XjeOeOGW\n12IJtIpuWBnPvy5NS+MnXZ3zHbVIJZcDyG0WpU59RlbAUl1oLVceL3vKz5e9gmeE\n2ERt7FYvs/LMsnN9g4tBiuQZuFA4nfBQoWE/XPocVeelTnqscfkKBFED0RwGDcMi\nESCVjAo+K9UEYLFsWg8fdrd0+cIjOf04inmvbOe2jM9lpQ0aEtCH9K8K+KHbdsea\nHEy9O+CxwagBPx3u+e0a9VL8g2eKt28Nwjos4zXBGtKREltFS+U7SzLDF258C1M/\nipaUzLjYLDqs/rVWG93yU7k5QH0k36vDuAGD71Bl8U1MP1aHT6OyfMdS0r0D4SVk\nt/cs/SXr14Iks7cmzEF3\n=MxvF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 781a3cf21ae405bb34242e19d2c1ba74cacbb247\nparent 904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1783711007 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783711007 -0400\n\nci(harbor,evals): add Harbor Index dataset + per-dispatch shard aggregation (`pass@K` / `avg@K`) (#4633)\n\n## Summary\n\nReworks #4630: instead of a separate 783-line workflow fork, make Harbor\nIndex a dataset in the shared `harbor.yml` and add general per-dispatch\nshard aggregation.\n\n- **Dataset option** — adds `harbor-index/harbor-index-1.0` to the\n`dataset` dropdown. It runs through the existing model matrix / sharding\n/ LangSmith tracing / concurrency like any other dataset (no fork).\n- **`aggregate` job** — merges the per-shard result artifacts\n(`shard-*`) via `.github/scripts/aggregate_shards.py` into:\n- `summary.json` + `per_task.jsonl` reporting **`pass@K`** (fraction of\ntasks that passed ≥1 of K rollouts) and **`avg@K`** (passing rollouts /\ntotal rollouts), where K = `rollouts_per_task` (keys are serialized\ndynamically, e.g. `pass@3` / `avg@3`);\n- **one combined zip** per run (`harbor-combined-<dataset-slug>`), after\nwhich the per-shard intermediates are deleted.\n- **Eval-a-model defaults + caps** — defaults set to rollouts 3 /\nconcurrency 4 / n_shards 10; a `prep` step caps n_shards ≤ 10,\nconcurrency ≤ 4, and models × shards × concurrency ≤ 40. Per-shard\nuploads renamed `harbor-*` → `shard-*` so the aggregate job can glob\nthem.\n\nThis is the reusable building block for a future \"measure a model across\n3 categories\" harness (autonomous / conversation / retrieval): each\ncategory is a `harbor.yml` run emitting its own `summary.json`, which an\norchestrator can roll into an overall score.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit tests `.github/scripts/test_aggregate_shards.py` (run by CI's\n`check-release-options` job): 8/8 pass.\n- End-to-end smoke run on this branch (haiku / langsmith / 2 shards /\n`n_tasks=2`): `prep` → 2 shards → `aggregate` all green; produced a\ncorrect `summary.json` (`pass@2` / `avg@2`) and a single combined zip,\nwith the per-shard intermediates deleted. Workflow plumbing validated;\nthe two sampled tasks errored for the reasons in **Out of scope** below.\n\n## Out of scope / follow-ups\n\n- Aggregation is **single-model** for now (errors on >1 model);\nmulti-model grouping and the caps/defaults interaction are deferred.\n- The `harbor-index/bix-ordinal-logit-covid` task errors with\n`EnvironmentStartTimeoutError` on a **cold** build — its 7 GB\n`chenzizhao/bixbench` base image plus a build-time HuggingFace capsule\ndownload exceed the task's own 1800s env-start budget. That's a\n**separate dataset/infra issue** (mirror + digest-pin the base image,\nreuse/pre-warm the snapshot, or pre-bake per-task images) and is not\naddressed here.\n\nSupersedes #4630.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-10T19:16:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/57918f6cea8348d64454fe2c8c2a9200891d4821/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4"}]},{"sha":"904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkwNGZmMDU2MjBhNTc2MTAwZTA1ZmQ2NTgxMGQzODQwNWM0OTQyZDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Will Bradley","email":"williambbradley@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-10T15:30:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T15:30:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): reap langgraph dev server when startup is cancelled (#4629)\n\n## Problem\n\nPressing `Ctrl+D` shortly after launching `dcode` returns you to the\nterminal but leaves an orphaned `python -m langgraph_cli dev …` process\nrunning:\n\n```\n$ ps aux | grep deepagent\nwbbradley  69643  ...  python3 -m langgraph_cli dev --host 127.0.0.1 --port 59934 --no-browser --no-reload --config .../langgraph.json\n```\n\nThis is not intentional — it's a process leak.\n\n## Root cause\n\nTo make the splash screen appear instantly, the LangGraph server is\nstarted in a background Textual worker (`_start_server_background`)\nrather than blocking launch. That worker calls\n`start_server_and_get_agent`, which spawns the `langgraph dev`\nsubprocess early (inside `ServerProcess.start()`) and then spends a few\nseconds polling `/ok` for health + graph readiness.\n\nIf the user quits during that window:\n\n1. `super().exit()` tears down Textual, which **cancels all workers**,\ninjecting `asyncio.CancelledError` into the in-flight `server.start()`.\n2. `start_server_and_get_agent` guarded cleanup with `except Exception:`\n— but `CancelledError` is a `BaseException`, **not** an `Exception`, so\n`server.stop()` was skipped and the exception re-raised.\n3. Because the function never returned, `DeepAgentsApp._server_proc` was\nnever assigned, so the belt-and-suspenders `finally` in\n`run_textual_app` also saw `None` and skipped cleanup.\n\nNet result: the `langgraph dev` subprocess is orphaned. When the server\nhas fully finished starting before the quit, `stop()` runs correctly and\nthere is no leak — the leak is specific to quitting *during* startup.\n\n## Fix\n\nCatch `BaseException` (which includes `asyncio.CancelledError`) around\n`server.start()` / `wait_for_graph_ready()` so a cancelled startup still\nstops the half-started subprocess, then re-raise to preserve\ncancellation/shutdown semantics. This matches the existing\ncleanup-on-cancel-and-reraise pattern already used in `skills/trust.py`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"4279c1024fa63db43d07ffdde621f0cb4c836abe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4279c1024fa63db43d07ffdde621f0cb4c836abe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqURAICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6JoQAIUz0sgO0rpCkxTBhkiwOO+c\nGD4DgU1JiV34MPkDADqvlTUyGqqnTIEIM9T+IKTJp8io3Y1i2X9lwHHuDbzOsgqO\ne8hnsRRHnoZwhKs5pWC594FawLKlW1owUGAPGqJ27BO7/b0Yd0H+7YpldM5kOdVo\nWrFdS0AU74Cy0e4Dx/D/VFmHo3XUWC2haqtCmHx4nfGCIvaysw51Lldh+Lbyfbb4\nniwo6l9sGvocjDZKo5bc3Ns0B0R3ujJsbo67iS8Gbjdp1BSqPXjPt/pEKcmf2wyA\n6ynHip9HTTcXRux2ETv0aEdwktkRaieLDTINJ/P7Zwd10HjcmYAMZcGFWF6JDB/z\nuReXuduwBOrOWozAcwYD0BrYr5PDATcHVdnXjEZWidX4XFBzMe5k2b74ncMxEyz6\n90LT3oHw2yNwtf5FeDIXfwwqTd6sgyDgSKjFaf6LtB4Tg1I+9GtL4RikpoxyJ59j\n53IS6E/zxqtoPRsMJ7Kkcu5JB1jVIBYHAB9aIW6VJAKE7w+HSC8aFJmVmVJsPoyr\noj5dxmEoST5rVIRfwH1x19oFBrShoi23gMUcxRAA7eO96viA5opBH+u58i+n+n+V\n1D2WlUNK/gfUuAl4c/rDwxVyCkYxv6PJNhggCskZMgd4QWtcBxorN29TSpFxreo4\ntN93kWkjp08pyfxByq7s\n=IKzI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4279c1024fa63db43d07ffdde621f0cb4c836abe\nparent 3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223\nauthor Will Bradley <williambbradley@gmail.com> 1783697416 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783697416 -0400\n\nfix(code): reap langgraph dev server when startup is cancelled (#4629)\n\n## Problem\n\nPressing `Ctrl+D` shortly after launching `dcode` returns you to the\nterminal but leaves an orphaned `python -m langgraph_cli dev …` process\nrunning:\n\n```\n$ ps aux | grep deepagent\nwbbradley  69643  ...  python3 -m langgraph_cli dev --host 127.0.0.1 --port 59934 --no-browser --no-reload --config .../langgraph.json\n```\n\nThis is not intentional — it's a process leak.\n\n## Root cause\n\nTo make the splash screen appear instantly, the LangGraph server is\nstarted in a background Textual worker (`_start_server_background`)\nrather than blocking launch. That worker calls\n`start_server_and_get_agent`, which spawns the `langgraph dev`\nsubprocess early (inside `ServerProcess.start()`) and then spends a few\nseconds polling `/ok` for health + graph readiness.\n\nIf the user quits during that window:\n\n1. `super().exit()` tears down Textual, which **cancels all workers**,\ninjecting `asyncio.CancelledError` into the in-flight `server.start()`.\n2. `start_server_and_get_agent` guarded cleanup with `except Exception:`\n— but `CancelledError` is a `BaseException`, **not** an `Exception`, so\n`server.stop()` was skipped and the exception re-raised.\n3. Because the function never returned, `DeepAgentsApp._server_proc` was\nnever assigned, so the belt-and-suspenders `finally` in\n`run_textual_app` also saw `None` and skipped cleanup.\n\nNet result: the `langgraph dev` subprocess is orphaned. When the server\nhas fully finished starting before the quit, `stop()` runs correctly and\nthere is no leak — the leak is specific to quitting *during* startup.\n\n## Fix\n\nCatch `BaseException` (which includes `asyncio.CancelledError`) around\n`server.start()` / `wait_for_graph_ready()` so a cancelled startup still\nstops the half-started subprocess, then re-raise to preserve\ncancellation/shutdown semantics. This matches the existing\ncleanup-on-cancel-and-reraise pattern already used in `skills/trust.py`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-10T15:30:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/904ff05620a576100e05fd65810d38405c4942d4/comments","author":{"login":"wbbradley","id":3030224,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzAyMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3030224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley","html_url":"https://github.com/wbbradley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wbbradley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223"}]},{"sha":"3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMwMTY3NjlkNmM0ODBmZGM2NjFhMWNjMjIwZDhjZDIxY2M5MDYyMjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-10T15:25:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T15:25:28Z"},"message":"ci(repo): defer release-please on hotfix push instead of failing guard (#4634)\n\nWhen a hotfix commit reaches `main` while a merged release PR still has\na failed matching release run, defer release-please with notice\nannotations and a successful `skip=true` output instead of failing the\nguard. Non-hotfix pushes keep the existing loud failure behavior,\nallowing the operator to repair and manually re-dispatch the failed\nrelease first.\n\n## Maintainer story\n\nA maintainer merges a release PR, but its package release workflow fails\nbefore anything is published. They fix the underlying problem and merge\na `hotfix(...)` commit to `main`, intending to manually re-dispatch the\nfailed release afterward. That hotfix push also starts release-please,\nwhile the merged release PR is still marked `autorelease: pending` and\nits matching release run is still failed.\n\nPreviously, the guard treated that expected recovery state as another\nerror and failed loudly. With this change, it recognizes that the\ntriggering commit is the maintainer's hotfix, reports the failed release\nas notices, and skips release-please successfully. The maintainer can\nthen re-dispatch the repaired package release without release-please\nrecomputing releases against the incomplete state.","tree":{"sha":"82e9dec86378521f09aaea94466d8e810cb29745","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/82e9dec86378521f09aaea94466d8e810cb29745"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUQ7oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7+QQAA1mphoLhSll5OSCWVWLmEbz\naZMeDWxKAEqrfazwJXvUlW585aeUtO51sH2F+fCvbrpx37EEhxL/4Uzu9mraeGyv\nbmW0Yfn5gBmaNi6lmAthDLE4ScliUWYD3cELj6XDkcBi+XDaT0q7VJnHU1zAlbrs\nNMhwvkZcsTBHdVZ37jNIh4I0qsz2QXiQzjbe7AWYUCNz8dmTYyr9GtF0o+sahYfS\nnY5GnwXP+H6bgAyMfv1Ud3zO/1WnMOOPkCkAOdL5SfznvTcz3GECJYmE3GbNdMKW\nwC7ZRYvm9Otm+5eBP5z2PoRQJ6S4Z8Ivqx6fKTx2HmRn+laPhzmQrM54bBz6X4zx\n/xcvEYQF1639Fk81ULuLf5UT3TOYlkHF19z3p9yXk+jV+tz+78w/KySjoYYUq+Dt\nHvH36Wi/HoW1HYf1iTo69JPr281cQHhACUMBWLTNaGKBAJ06nrRtqreHcyQZebRD\nwvNg3hNGvjW6JorJ1fFNUc5whRgaJQ2KuL9NKqRe2INpN4FK9X1vdiB9sh+cuEOH\n6IlBDv6QGdTOvpuJz5eXH9p6bvsI9+u8C0KO5fj8qbI/w4UugYNhLJPqPmyWtqNE\nouNd90EC2xXURULOZN2FCTFixID/z8ev/YlgDiYEW7w86qYJJ9Yk5ZMERPLqOnXj\n5IrmM6gKwA1lrL3RLTNk\n=HCos\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 82e9dec86378521f09aaea94466d8e810cb29745\nparent 17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783697128 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783697128 -0400\n\nci(repo): defer release-please on hotfix push instead of failing guard (#4634)\n\nWhen a hotfix commit reaches `main` while a merged release PR still has\na failed matching release run, defer release-please with notice\nannotations and a successful `skip=true` output instead of failing the\nguard. Non-hotfix pushes keep the existing loud failure behavior,\nallowing the operator to repair and manually re-dispatch the failed\nrelease first.\n\n## Maintainer story\n\nA maintainer merges a release PR, but its package release workflow fails\nbefore anything is published. They fix the underlying problem and merge\na `hotfix(...)` commit to `main`, intending to manually re-dispatch the\nfailed release afterward. That hotfix push also starts release-please,\nwhile the merged release PR is still marked `autorelease: pending` and\nits matching release run is still failed.\n\nPreviously, the guard treated that expected recovery state as another\nerror and failed loudly. With this change, it recognizes that the\ntriggering commit is the maintainer's hotfix, reports the failed release\nas notices, and skips release-please successfully. The maintainer can\nthen re-dispatch the repaired package release without release-please\nrecomputing releases against the incomplete state.","verified_at":"2026-07-10T15:25:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3016769d6c480fdc661a1cc220d8cd21cc906223/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5"}]},{"sha":"17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE3ZmQwOWU1OTJjMGUyZTBkNTE4ZTE1OWI1MTYxOTY4MTgyNjcxZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-10T15:04:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-10T15:04:23Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump mistune from 3.2.1 to 3.3.0 in /examples/deep_research (#4631)\n\nBumps [mistune](https://github.com/lepture/mistune) from 3.2.1 to 3.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/releases\">mistune's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v3.3.0</h2>\n<h3>   🐞 Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Resolve O(n^2) DoS in parse_link_text (CWE-400)  -  by\n<strong>bhanugoudm041</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/b6b499d\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(b6b49)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Resolve O(n^2) DoS in parse_link_text (CWE-400)-Type\nhandling/testing done  -  by <strong>bhanugoudm041</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/b3af85d\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(b3af8)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>block</strong>: Avoid quadratic ref link scans  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/2b04d7b\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(2b04d)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>cli</strong>: Add entrypoint and utf-8 output  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/2f2449d\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(2f244)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>directives</strong>: Constrain include targets  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/1bef343\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(1bef3)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>formatting</strong>: Avoid quadratic marker scans  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/96d0f57\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(96d0f)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>image</strong>: Validate figure width option  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/e3e51de\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(e3e51)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>inline</strong>: Avoid bracket parsing DoS  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/25f2503\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(25f25)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>math</strong>: Reject currency patterns and cross-line\nmatches in inline math  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/geopanther\"><code>@​geopanther</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/566e173\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(566e1)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>math</strong>: Support display and backtick math  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/1141eec\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(1141e)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>renderer</strong>: Render plugin list and table nodes  -  by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/614b019\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(614b0)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>renderer</strong>: Block encoded unsafe URL schemes  -  by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/c7101fc\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(c7101)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>toc</strong>: Avoid generated id collisions  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/c4093c4\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(c4093)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>   🏎 Performance</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Improve performance  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/bf95c32\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(bf95c)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5>    <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/compare/v3.2.1...v3.3.0\">View\nchanges on GitHub</a></h5>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/blob/main/docs/changes.rst\">mistune's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 3.3.0</h2>\n<p><strong>Released on Jun 21, 2026</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Improve CommonMark compatibility and parser performance.</li>\n<li>Add command line entrypoint with UTF-8 output.</li>\n<li>Support display and backtick math.</li>\n<li>Render plugin list and table nodes in Markdown renderer.</li>\n<li>Escape leading block markers in Markdown renderer.</li>\n<li>Fix RST renderer for block quotes nested in lists.</li>\n<li>Avoid generated heading ID collisions in TOC.</li>\n<li>Harden URL, image, figure, and include directive handling.</li>\n<li>Fix quadratic scans in inline links, reference links, and formatting\nmarkers.</li>\n<li>Fix math escaping, currency pattern matching, and cross-line\nmatching.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/15c3b79325125272263d7d42492ec8f757447191\"><code>15c3b79</code></a>\nchore: release 3.3.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/bdc01ade171c7c2cd1099e2531ddf8c275a2f64c\"><code>bdc01ad</code></a>\ntests: increase run time on pypy</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/7cf181483e6201184bcecdbae13225d45ebab4c4\"><code>7cf1814</code></a>\ntests: increase run time for pypy</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/6dfdc3dae490c7a21499ff1063f4dd9b7357d4c5\"><code>6dfdc3d</code></a>\ntests: add more tests</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/17c50f6c0572027c1dad2c2501e7c97cea0b0b43\"><code>17c50f6</code></a>\nchore: fix mypy issues</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/63abe4b8e9adccc711c953e6727400ee7ba1084c\"><code>63abe4b</code></a>\nchore: use ruff check and format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/e6c1b184461beab8887c7375621c64dffaf652c5\"><code>e6c1b18</code></a>\nchore: resolve mypy issues</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/dcf89020c1ee697b2267387064b3e4580e0b83c5\"><code>dcf8902</code></a>\ntest(math): cover escaped math output</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/c4093c4742ed0d10d9332fb8edb455869b7b581b\"><code>c4093c4</code></a>\nfix(toc): avoid generated id collisions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/e3e51de9cf0a72dc30191248dccf22087c57f046\"><code>e3e51de</code></a>\nfix(image): validate figure width option</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/compare/v3.2.1...v3.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=mistune&package-manager=uv&previous-version=3.2.1&new-version=3.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fd9aa220f13abb0f04d7f449bc0dfaf11bd65828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fd9aa220f13abb0f04d7f449bc0dfaf11bd65828"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUQn3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzr0QAKc1NXt2aRjCNAzEQYjdXyLI\n3toqBSCVdpv26NOI4gybMYysWMiq8wkWr92nmi8NpUgY4Ey0vmIAw6lo6r+OMHdj\ngBqEioFRPlIYAUdjql5vE6C7UDNdC8gdcfUdUZ0/Y5qLF266h6d3VgG4UeFvTlnH\n0abBB/ukVuhfOPqwN1++5IvjthWmdMY34TNfNMEIH9124PZpTMaWHp5W3WNtI5vM\n/L1JBqWw/3LXH7MTkW0vg03PwziUq0WWqvkPNT7/H1o+D5WGd9ph4e8fXz9H76LS\nDe01iC37O03BHY/12e2TJc/byH/ha9r6BC13AdjBBVsmo+V8FaWlhgF6JglAMXLd\nfQnfsON53vI/PVB+7+j5QG/swahAqTg/ySrPf5oP86auRlaa67Z7fl57al90q75I\npA1HsXYVWZbqdSqm1N403uB8V+SLp3ae+uJHn0ZmV9TwtU77w4longzF0Yl/JFiv\nF23VDMjNZk/PCGyt1fwN/j8oE6K4ekv2iWjsKmTQRYc+YoRk4iBQ27R/RooyMXsW\n/+LsEbFGcShbS+mF43XQdsE9gMO3bu3uUo3GK7Glii/KYw41Cx7R+hW5zR7LZhGP\nEoa0e7TKyJAWhCr6CAu1kk1wcKVd3EbEQ7IG1wDymAjtxPXSx0lG/CZqHWpEE7jW\n0kH2+mbWBbJsEHJbMHYd\n=suop\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fd9aa220f13abb0f04d7f449bc0dfaf11bd65828\nparent 2915644e055f6de8c0b6a66d8568ec3ce96c2a74\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1783695863 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783695863 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump mistune from 3.2.1 to 3.3.0 in /examples/deep_research (#4631)\n\nBumps [mistune](https://github.com/lepture/mistune) from 3.2.1 to 3.3.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/releases\">mistune's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v3.3.0</h2>\n<h3>   🐞 Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Resolve O(n^2) DoS in parse_link_text (CWE-400)  -  by\n<strong>bhanugoudm041</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/b6b499d\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(b6b49)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Resolve O(n^2) DoS in parse_link_text (CWE-400)-Type\nhandling/testing done  -  by <strong>bhanugoudm041</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/b3af85d\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(b3af8)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>block</strong>: Avoid quadratic ref link scans  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/2b04d7b\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(2b04d)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>cli</strong>: Add entrypoint and utf-8 output  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/2f2449d\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(2f244)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>directives</strong>: Constrain include targets  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/1bef343\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(1bef3)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>formatting</strong>: Avoid quadratic marker scans  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/96d0f57\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(96d0f)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>image</strong>: Validate figure width option  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/e3e51de\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(e3e51)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>inline</strong>: Avoid bracket parsing DoS  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/25f2503\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(25f25)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>math</strong>: Reject currency patterns and cross-line\nmatches in inline math  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/geopanther\"><code>@​geopanther</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/566e173\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(566e1)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>math</strong>: Support display and backtick math  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/1141eec\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(1141e)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>renderer</strong>: Render plugin list and table nodes  -  by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/614b019\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(614b0)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>renderer</strong>: Block encoded unsafe URL schemes  -  by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/c7101fc\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(c7101)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>toc</strong>: Avoid generated id collisions  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/c4093c4\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(c4093)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>   🏎 Performance</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Improve performance  -  by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture\"><code>@​lepture</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/bf95c32\"><!-- raw HTML\nomitted -->(bf95c)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5>    <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/compare/v3.2.1...v3.3.0\">View\nchanges on GitHub</a></h5>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/blob/main/docs/changes.rst\">mistune's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 3.3.0</h2>\n<p><strong>Released on Jun 21, 2026</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Improve CommonMark compatibility and parser performance.</li>\n<li>Add command line entrypoint with UTF-8 output.</li>\n<li>Support display and backtick math.</li>\n<li>Render plugin list and table nodes in Markdown renderer.</li>\n<li>Escape leading block markers in Markdown renderer.</li>\n<li>Fix RST renderer for block quotes nested in lists.</li>\n<li>Avoid generated heading ID collisions in TOC.</li>\n<li>Harden URL, image, figure, and include directive handling.</li>\n<li>Fix quadratic scans in inline links, reference links, and formatting\nmarkers.</li>\n<li>Fix math escaping, currency pattern matching, and cross-line\nmatching.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/15c3b79325125272263d7d42492ec8f757447191\"><code>15c3b79</code></a>\nchore: release 3.3.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/bdc01ade171c7c2cd1099e2531ddf8c275a2f64c\"><code>bdc01ad</code></a>\ntests: increase run time on pypy</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/7cf181483e6201184bcecdbae13225d45ebab4c4\"><code>7cf1814</code></a>\ntests: increase run time for pypy</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/6dfdc3dae490c7a21499ff1063f4dd9b7357d4c5\"><code>6dfdc3d</code></a>\ntests: add more tests</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/17c50f6c0572027c1dad2c2501e7c97cea0b0b43\"><code>17c50f6</code></a>\nchore: fix mypy issues</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/63abe4b8e9adccc711c953e6727400ee7ba1084c\"><code>63abe4b</code></a>\nchore: use ruff check and format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/e6c1b184461beab8887c7375621c64dffaf652c5\"><code>e6c1b18</code></a>\nchore: resolve mypy issues</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/dcf89020c1ee697b2267387064b3e4580e0b83c5\"><code>dcf8902</code></a>\ntest(math): cover escaped math output</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/c4093c4742ed0d10d9332fb8edb455869b7b581b\"><code>c4093c4</code></a>\nfix(toc): avoid generated id collisions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/commit/e3e51de9cf0a72dc30191248dccf22087c57f046\"><code>e3e51de</code></a>\nfix(image): validate figure width option</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lepture/mistune/compare/v3.2.1...v3.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=mistune&package-manager=uv&previous-version=3.2.1&new-version=3.3.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-10T15:04:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/17fd09e592c0e2e0d518e159b5161968182671e5/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url