sers/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c"}]},{"sha":"09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA5ZGFhYjU3NzJmZjBhOGIxZmI4ZTIzNzNmNTI4MWViMjVjZmQ1NmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-09T04:28:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T04:28:28Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.35 (#4574)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.35](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.34...deepagents-code==0.1.35)\n(2026-07-09)\n\n### Features\n\n* Restore interrupted prompt to input on ESC\n([#4544](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4544))\n([fccf037](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70))\n* Add `[startup].mode` default approval mode\n([#4573](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4573))\n([7c5bf54](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41))\n* Offer restart after saving Tavily key via `/auth`\n([#4560](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4560))\n([12df81a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd))\n* Reload env from `/auth` modal via Ctrl+R\n([#4566](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4566))\n([f07d638](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb))\n* Toast on saved `/auth` API key\n([#4558](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4558))\n([ee3c264](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Harden approval content rendering\n([#4581](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4581))\n([38446fd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0))\n* Preserve transcript order during virtualization\n([#4549](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4549))\n([f6ee70c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361))\n* Run stdio MCP server pre-flight check off the event loop\n([#4434](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4434))\n([c9636e2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9636e22725a5bd32c1f8b9e739b02b4aa7c3dc7))\n* Avoid duplicate \"criteria ready\" message on `/goal` revisions\n([#4559](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4559))\n([1110497](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a))\n* Restore welcome banner tips\n([#4528](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4528))\n([3f1e55e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3f1e55eafbc1fde79cb75f631561cf35d4b8ff4c))\n* Clarify managed `rg` install failures\n([#4578](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4578))\n([434c84a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70))\n* Dedupe update/install log path output\n([#4553](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4553))\n([1398fee](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f))\n* Keep notification center open for API-key entry\n([#4568](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4568))\n([6e89417](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb))\n* Queue `/mcp login` sent before the server connects\n([#4533](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4533))\n([edac82c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d))\n* Serialize MCP OAuth token refreshes to prevent reuse revocation\n([#4565](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4565))\n([c37100d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3da0f5c8505a5afeb40e23c08e9acd80c8db6ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b3da0f5c8505a5afeb40e23c08e9acd80c8db6ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTyNsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB4oQAIb20HsnqPOaKrXhzH8zsWvy\nq+eiiBHUOfBfugIkn7MF47j/mAA4WdwWLvK+dOCPwWEWw2wFeMtXXTu4qqYegIcX\neXpaSblxMMuIxujw8Lm732KMJAMOU0NAOwe4y1dYk0hJTkhSe/341HjVCewJq7zY\ny1UH6IJO0uyYBOxpL4y8qobEGg3Lyy9I10BAHwYOzWfMdf13mHtpFXB9IiU6CoFK\nipi6pfNAmJcuYGNf7S9CK2D9DHxK7E472C3pN/kI4A1UgHAfVD6RFxUl3HT1UlQC\nWsciQteJ6N91/kgQA6EGkL4xyzwWtYnj0cF40sojzHhMxk+2zsvjivKlhyYv93qm\nl2fzWSxR0R8H/H+Bjb7izK+f6OcvH4WyB54bsCAB5F3zUKYVr2/SRywF0jIUK4Kq\nKBNjlyDhdt5gew50TXCb6wrtfBtCu2yC0LsEOP6Bxz006gmnNDlw8gexnkfFFll7\n4cbf6zLkuoasv/soEN/qheO9/yVo3pHi0ZOBZjTw1y7Ha6ym4TQxPHxW8F1SXBm+\n5hbS/4gucdtam5zmShV+KALhbiFj4/AE3PHtzumnC39G7z50OLr1PeHDaqqvUIp8\ndYajLyKmFXR3lKoq4lWxwcIGpw7GbcYQlw1jtW3NCiz51tXXDs8ZOVvsewHS+MXN\nmLx5qNPFyFHkccs4ScSl\n=+hMV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b3da0f5c8505a5afeb40e23c08e9acd80c8db6ed\nparent 38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1783571308 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783571308 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.35 (#4574)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.35](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.34...deepagents-code==0.1.35)\n(2026-07-09)\n\n### Features\n\n* Restore interrupted prompt to input on ESC\n([#4544](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4544))\n([fccf037](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70))\n* Add `[startup].mode` default approval mode\n([#4573](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4573))\n([7c5bf54](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41))\n* Offer restart after saving Tavily key via `/auth`\n([#4560](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4560))\n([12df81a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd))\n* Reload env from `/auth` modal via Ctrl+R\n([#4566](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4566))\n([f07d638](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb))\n* Toast on saved `/auth` API key\n([#4558](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4558))\n([ee3c264](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Harden approval content rendering\n([#4581](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4581))\n([38446fd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0))\n* Preserve transcript order during virtualization\n([#4549](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4549))\n([f6ee70c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361))\n* Run stdio MCP server pre-flight check off the event loop\n([#4434](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4434))\n([c9636e2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9636e22725a5bd32c1f8b9e739b02b4aa7c3dc7))\n* Avoid duplicate \"criteria ready\" message on `/goal` revisions\n([#4559](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4559))\n([1110497](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a))\n* Restore welcome banner tips\n([#4528](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4528))\n([3f1e55e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3f1e55eafbc1fde79cb75f631561cf35d4b8ff4c))\n* Clarify managed `rg` install failures\n([#4578](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4578))\n([434c84a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70))\n* Dedupe update/install log path output\n([#4553](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4553))\n([1398fee](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f))\n* Keep notification center open for API-key entry\n([#4568](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4568))\n([6e89417](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb))\n* Queue `/mcp login` sent before the server connects\n([#4533](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4533))\n([edac82c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d))\n* Serialize MCP OAuth token refreshes to prevent reuse revocation\n([#4565](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4565))\n([c37100d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T04:28:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09daab5772ff0a8b1fb8e2373f5281eb25cfd56c/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0"}]},{"sha":"38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM4NDQ2ZmRhNjQ5Yjg5MWRkODYwNGU3ODg3MDFlYWJlNzM5YzFkZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T02:05:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T02:05:31Z"},"message":"fix(code): harden approval content rendering (#4581)\n\nCloses #4575\n\nDefend against crashes where malformed streamed file-edit tool arguments\ncould break the manual approval screen before the tool call was\nvalidated.\n\n---\n\nThe manual approval UI renders tool-call arguments before the filesystem\ntool schema has a chance to validate them. If a streamed `write_file` or\n`edit_file` call contains malformed non-string content, the approval\nwidgets could call string methods on raw objects and crash the TUI.\n\nThis change makes approval rendering defensive by formatting arbitrary\nraw content into displayable text before line counting, diff generation,\nor Markdown rendering. Valid string content still passes through\nunchanged; malformed objects are JSON-formatted when possible and fall\nback to `str()` otherwise.","tree":{"sha":"28c441d78e3d273d444ffbc4aecb3a019522c6c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/28c441d78e3d273d444ffbc4aecb3a019522c6c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTwHrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXhwQADzjpGKrH09vMm6DlvrYSmmT\n5hH3NLTmVL5oG+x6rwNFRv9ERIHjagzKfP/+kzCvyVuxW/0ixUde5TqsGusiEeRh\nZB6DC3aHcBcsb1d4tHsWAEUaT80l3XmLVtPR1IEUwBK/GrHVVlYsmnQU+RcrIgY5\nBfuig3X8tcVGCjoRUIJd73j/eOry7zqImQx8+ROmOrG/4cCFRD2lCP7pYI9cgQKy\nkVa2JK7rSJ8j8b03IS7vXku+ZeJ68pmDaKTstvxO34O23q5MKwESbRQgXkJQXcNV\nB56vvLnHh4vk5iLq59xLZK4fl+gr+Z6Vs4SiY9GlRrHwBhuwEDLsig52CyOWjNt/\nlqTG225SgTE8F0Sm/QG57gFSqYsLebXqoczHN17M4Sp5K2f4zjXp87uuGAWbs9la\n839iDL5LBPW5RGo0wVdlOh6oabQi+2zzL3l0CxB528qWX6ozViuogCFGJam57Wo7\nLKebXwhnYQx2oFliSdwOBGsSnOmINEtwMrjdSL5+kyIQnP1X/4kHoOFawi0eLkwJ\nI3LDgBLUNe3YlZd9wll/PlCzjuswEAY0i14mzQQzIkeT5YpJ1r4zsvues6y1byQp\n3Zltbj8AwS+ZouWP0CMoNvUgmd+3RP90rW2/DbgFmfEliNuPj+At1RpX+yY3y/xH\nbe7Q5I3kXiZUF3eOZgFD\n=7lwc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 28c441d78e3d273d444ffbc4aecb3a019522c6c4\nparent 58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783562731 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783562731 -0400\n\nfix(code): harden approval content rendering (#4581)\n\nCloses #4575\n\nDefend against crashes where malformed streamed file-edit tool arguments\ncould break the manual approval screen before the tool call was\nvalidated.\n\n---\n\nThe manual approval UI renders tool-call arguments before the filesystem\ntool schema has a chance to validate them. If a streamed `write_file` or\n`edit_file` call contains malformed non-string content, the approval\nwidgets could call string methods on raw objects and crash the TUI.\n\nThis change makes approval rendering defensive by formatting arbitrary\nraw content into displayable text before line counting, diff generation,\nor Markdown rendering. Valid string content still passes through\nunchanged; malformed objects are JSON-formatted when possible and fall\nback to `str()` otherwise.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T02:05:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/38446fda649b891dd8604e788701eabe739c1dd0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a"}]},{"sha":"58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU4ZGIyYjc4ZjRmZjFlYTBiMWUwOWM5OWVmYjcwNWE4NmE1OTQ5NmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T01:51:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:51:34Z"},"message":"refactor(code): rename in-app nomenclature to `dcode` (#4556)\n\nRebrand in-app references from \"Deep Agents Code\" to `dcode`.\n\n---\n\nSwitches the in-app product name in `libs/code` from \"Deep Agents Code\"\nto `dcode` so the running app matches the `dcode` CLI/branding. Covers\nuser-visible runtime strings only: Textual TUI widget copy (auth,\ninstall-confirm, launch-init, update-progress, agent-selector),\nCLI/console output in `main.py`, user notices in `app.py`/`config.py`,\ninstall/update status messages in `update_check.py`, and the\nsystem-prompt title (with its snapshot). Related UI test assertions\nupdated to match.\n\nIntentionally left unchanged (not in-app nomenclature): external\ncontract/metadata identifiers `CODING_AGENT_RUNTIME` and\n`_OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE` (coding-agent-v1 validator + attribution),\ndocstrings/comments, and markdown docs. Standalone \"Deep Agents\"\n(SDK/framework) references were also left as-is since the request\ntargeted \"Deep Agents Code\".\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/60a3d442-7e8d-bd18-4575-a533ca9f9614)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6cda4682747df92b98fd7ea82ca75ad6ff0d936b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6cda4682747df92b98fd7ea82ca75ad6ff0d936b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTv6mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuEMQABMQyKsXn0Fb0eI0pnEMRRoj\nA4lSkstvZPywR540cHh1GHh3MJNHfRa/GoeJwweK4/QCzELOx20pxN0c0JPxnXKX\nDp+qKQHRvs1kLdTW/OhmkmnMTpswE8AWTQfBtFvLFXhdM/q8v70GXHWHGJbDCpHB\n0kDO8ww1M9UznbKmPQEeUk5Z/yag8EhXcrACpnXV9d8CDnFqO8V7xSoF+0eZk22m\nC8gveGOiSA/UMEcSQ0+DaRTRO/0AWNtfNKw5JQ+5UPfeqhvK6LD8H8vz54YaqJl7\nIYGCLp4Qpi1/20+HjNCvw6g/opmmXeBojYydRX8+Bc0JAWW3KLPiXeQAhSjQJCfn\nCbqHQJDU6EuOsnZiCONOAEL7/WOF7v4Y1n9oIksyD6vlGzhVc0dO7bsyTqKt5KBv\nZU16AqxdvrIhMe2kb07n/yGSoRF8SGaadAPmtOrW9Q7PdXvbH1ngtyZc2S6PCFfv\n2DIqFQTZy0ekNrvvOv0I4X9AsgUYK6uIgv2RbzxD52Wk7vpsyUaKzJIKLb5ZFdEK\n50ecFo3m+rScAYnXBaACmgSKFsd76RD+CLZ54LGseuYVfP2mqc+tGX94mYk5HCDf\nL+hgmAFE66BOWzZkK0jSqwa4iDTmDJ/8FaezMitg5neNXZo4QEm6a9kkwggLwZtG\nH1qoFsyM7136qHzkeD1k\n=njI8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6cda4682747df92b98fd7ea82ca75ad6ff0d936b\nparent c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783561894 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783561894 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): rename in-app nomenclature to `dcode` (#4556)\n\nRebrand in-app references from \"Deep Agents Code\" to `dcode`.\n\n---\n\nSwitches the in-app product name in `libs/code` from \"Deep Agents Code\"\nto `dcode` so the running app matches the `dcode` CLI/branding. Covers\nuser-visible runtime strings only: Textual TUI widget copy (auth,\ninstall-confirm, launch-init, update-progress, agent-selector),\nCLI/console output in `main.py`, user notices in `app.py`/`config.py`,\ninstall/update status messages in `update_check.py`, and the\nsystem-prompt title (with its snapshot). Related UI test assertions\nupdated to match.\n\nIntentionally left unchanged (not in-app nomenclature): external\ncontract/metadata identifiers `CODING_AGENT_RUNTIME` and\n`_OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE` (coding-agent-v1 validator + attribution),\ndocstrings/comments, and markdown docs. Standalone \"Deep Agents\"\n(SDK/framework) references were also left as-is since the request\ntargeted \"Deep Agents Code\".\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/60a3d442-7e8d-bd18-4575-a533ca9f9614)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:51:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/58db2b78f4ff1ea0b1e09c99efb705a86a59496a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640"}]},{"sha":"c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMzNzEwMGQ0NzYzZTUyN2ZjZTEyZmE0NDUxNzk0Y2EyNWRlZDc2NDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T01:15:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:15:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): serialize MCP OAuth token refreshes to prevent reuse revocation (#4565)\n\nFixed frequent LangSmith MCP OAuth timeouts/re-auth prompts caused by\nconcurrent token refreshes invalidating the session; refreshes are now\nserialized across dcode processes and provider instances.\n\n---\n\ndcode stores MCP OAuth tokens per-server under\n`~/.deepagents/.state/mcp-tokens/`. The MCP SDK's `OAuthClientProvider`\nserializes refreshes with an in-memory `OAuthContext.lock`, which only\ncovers a single provider instance. Two dcode processes — or two provider\ninstances in one process (e.g. a throwaway discovery session created\nduring tool loading alongside the cached runtime session) — can each\nread the same refresh token from disk and `POST` the `refresh_token`\ngrant concurrently.\n\nThe LangSmith OAuth server (in `langchainplus`) rotates refresh tokens\nand, on replay of an already-rotated token, treats it as reuse and\nrevokes every active refresh token for that identity+client. That is why\nthe LangSmith MCP worked for a few minutes (one access-token lifetime)\nand then hung until a full re-auth.\n\nThis adds a cross-process lock (`filelock`) keyed on a sibling `.lock`\nfile next to each token file. Before refreshing,\n`_ExpiryAwareOAuthClientProvider` acquires the lock, reloads tokens from\ndisk (so a peer's rotation is observed and the refresh is skipped when\nthe token is already valid), and only then performs and persists the SDK\nrefresh grant. The lock wait is bounded (falls back to a best-effort\nrefresh on timeout so a crashed peer can't hang tool calls), and all\nblocking file IO runs in a worker thread to keep the\n`blockbuster`-guarded server loop responsive. The lock file holds no\ntoken material.\n\n`filelock` is added as a direct dependency (`>=3.12,<4.0.0`); it was\nalready resolved transitively (via `huggingface-hub`) at `3.29.4`. It is\nMIT-licensed and actively maintained.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2c15284a-7a9d-8076-66e9-3c97ab30976c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"72b48124db8b92cae931139e07dc355d8b06e8cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/72b48124db8b92cae931139e07dc355d8b06e8cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvYkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADuQQAJWfU655ojdce84e0a/ZRCWC\nhVweoKDxUenIetuD/U9e4qRYww4Mh/5XqoKVq8lSr8gwvaySR+0O+/+1LgYozSvz\nv8NYleiF+lC6Snh48ELSXbMO7aFPsPsE+Q/wGu7iHSezXXQDwEaCIiOZ7I+5VAc6\nuzzKTOXAcOY6bBrAeqGyM5MR3RBHcj79QMepo/5wWpCDBfcMKtah+pNL3dcAjXGN\ncfOJnQPdLFHbdpWHsGt24QtfAF8KczMX5uCkF0z1LwHl1nQtD2hq5ayInllzPicr\nr9vkjtZme3ABVmbKiJK5Tkp/xrP4q4nAlO3SaZ9JcfSpHLm7DgkNFgHFyTMlNaV5\naiorNDxixeZdOiYWutdOae3Jdzk3U6l+6PFCPHS4c4cBgEkb12XGehc7lKB3lriZ\nQ5xJDc2/mWv0GmhCdrHvhjFAZt+dQ2kojQrG9khhIxDQQDhgSQyEU3lTJ17lqhyV\nz5hpJ89SsPfsS/dNeFI+o8mJFvsH5m/+tt4xo2C4+AQ7taFccjF84OGjPsbvQqZK\nJYi1SkI2qI4o+O1rNtlPSORlbESJmdIz+tkOc0X7R17CStfeo+DjvErK/03i0Qaq\n2/KJecdnyhK1A95Qtuof/njFX2uig5p8j+KgIN9FSABIn1M7flHPuB/UdFb3hEta\nNmzL3kOvuiBJ7rGAe12U\n=+juy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 72b48124db8b92cae931139e07dc355d8b06e8cb\nparent 12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783559716 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783559716 -0400\n\nfix(code): serialize MCP OAuth token refreshes to prevent reuse revocation (#4565)\n\nFixed frequent LangSmith MCP OAuth timeouts/re-auth prompts caused by\nconcurrent token refreshes invalidating the session; refreshes are now\nserialized across dcode processes and provider instances.\n\n---\n\ndcode stores MCP OAuth tokens per-server under\n`~/.deepagents/.state/mcp-tokens/`. The MCP SDK's `OAuthClientProvider`\nserializes refreshes with an in-memory `OAuthContext.lock`, which only\ncovers a single provider instance. Two dcode processes — or two provider\ninstances in one process (e.g. a throwaway discovery session created\nduring tool loading alongside the cached runtime session) — can each\nread the same refresh token from disk and `POST` the `refresh_token`\ngrant concurrently.\n\nThe LangSmith OAuth server (in `langchainplus`) rotates refresh tokens\nand, on replay of an already-rotated token, treats it as reuse and\nrevokes every active refresh token for that identity+client. That is why\nthe LangSmith MCP worked for a few minutes (one access-token lifetime)\nand then hung until a full re-auth.\n\nThis adds a cross-process lock (`filelock`) keyed on a sibling `.lock`\nfile next to each token file. Before refreshing,\n`_ExpiryAwareOAuthClientProvider` acquires the lock, reloads tokens from\ndisk (so a peer's rotation is observed and the refresh is skipped when\nthe token is already valid), and only then performs and persists the SDK\nrefresh grant. The lock wait is bounded (falls back to a best-effort\nrefresh on timeout so a crashed peer can't hang tool calls), and all\nblocking file IO runs in a worker thread to keep the\n`blockbuster`-guarded server loop responsive. The lock file holds no\ntoken material.\n\n`filelock` is added as a direct dependency (`>=3.12,<4.0.0`); it was\nalready resolved transitively (via `huggingface-hub`) at `3.29.4`. It is\nMIT-licensed and actively maintained.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2c15284a-7a9d-8076-66e9-3c97ab30976c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:15:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c37100d4763e527fce12fa4451794ca25ded7640/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd"}]},{"sha":"12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDEyZGY4MWFkMDBkODE0YzU3MGI0ZDI0YTJiMDZkZTliMThkNTFhYmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T01:13:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:13:59Z"},"message":"feat(code): offer restart after saving Tavily key via `/auth` (#4560)\n\nSaving a Tavily API key via `/auth` now offers to restart the agent\nserver so web search activates without relaunching.\n\n---\n\n`web_search` is bound only when Tavily is configured at server spawn\ntime (`server_graph._build_tools`), so a Tavily key added to an\nalready-running server never activates web search until the server\nrespawns. Previously `/auth` only auto-resumed the server when a saved\nkey unblocked a credentials-blocked *model* startup, so saving a Tavily\nkey mid-session silently did nothing.\n\nNow, saving a Tavily key in the `/auth` manager arms an optional restart\nprompt that fires once the manager closes (deferrable with Esc),\nmirroring the post-install restart offer.\n`AuthManagerScreen.CredentialSaved` carries the saved service so the app\ncan react to spawn-time-gating credentials, `RestartPromptScreen` gained\n`verb`/`body` overrides, and the post-install restart offer was\nrefactored into a shared `_offer_server_restart` reused by both flows.\nThe stored key is exported to the environment eagerly so a later\n`/restart` (offered or manual) picks it up on reload.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/95be92ba-5015-b080-9309-3b7a9f8bf85f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7ce4aebae240eb656f4918eb7688d11e3485412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c7ce4aebae240eb656f4918eb7688d11e3485412"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvXXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj/cQACOcuKKAEqhrjptivU2OMz5r\nEg+FZkyRtuogavaAMpiqnwqVz9WrVzRK+5vASgzzqszhMBMQ3jvTI9jsbhoRsMST\nNekGAaPOqoGMI5f5Q4r4txjpQVFXs/6aCVuV6GRVQeRm2Nw2IthXBFtWhqWvA1/+\nK9C69jRBFlvYJh1O0nXbp2yF3GeLfkslY90cL5N0QEnib4MG9oAM0F953cpn6j0E\nD56PBIqGXFSCzORmNXd5IZ5R0hdYrJMXJ9IfVZVYW5qh9N8PI0m4IphsiSgTadgR\n+nUvNLpmq4sQgaH94BzqeeLgt5e0KnNOaj8mSVYPRjEbOhLGWt2caYnhDIe8Dox6\n+7cdqv5/3H2s8U/36YqPt9avpG8NeGzFSaevYZpa9lGFfPIw/eOStIO888k5mN6D\ne1VdLY6af8FZM7PnuXfqGV+57Qm+cz2UxS8390mF48U9syzMIH9OtmiX0M7mSIPm\noo3069ssTiUWAvKozHd90ur+DGFLBfqbCixJ/TFXqIX2rTXafkH5pyDgYAG/4IUu\ndshvknOxvA5YIMLtJwO1lCvQ1fASNXeAaPiQkHISNADwL+3JcSYP/6JPfrNxfFal\nLZ+OEqwuF8l1zAY9e3cN8zcXVE1FguuHyOY4KDgoL3O9TcCiSlFA2PdJT+efBcRC\nr1okxeklRM7riOjLWE29\n=zC8P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7ce4aebae240eb656f4918eb7688d11e3485412\nparent 1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783559639 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783559639 -0400\n\nfeat(code): offer restart after saving Tavily key via `/auth` (#4560)\n\nSaving a Tavily API key via `/auth` now offers to restart the agent\nserver so web search activates without relaunching.\n\n---\n\n`web_search` is bound only when Tavily is configured at server spawn\ntime (`server_graph._build_tools`), so a Tavily key added to an\nalready-running server never activates web search until the server\nrespawns. Previously `/auth` only auto-resumed the server when a saved\nkey unblocked a credentials-blocked *model* startup, so saving a Tavily\nkey mid-session silently did nothing.\n\nNow, saving a Tavily key in the `/auth` manager arms an optional restart\nprompt that fires once the manager closes (deferrable with Esc),\nmirroring the post-install restart offer.\n`AuthManagerScreen.CredentialSaved` carries the saved service so the app\ncan react to spawn-time-gating credentials, `RestartPromptScreen` gained\n`verb`/`body` overrides, and the post-install restart offer was\nrefactored into a shared `_offer_server_restart` reused by both flows.\nThe stored key is exported to the environment eagerly so a later\n`/restart` (offered or manual) picks it up on reload.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/95be92ba-5015-b080-9309-3b7a9f8bf85f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:14:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/12df81ad00d814c570b4d24a2b06de9b18d51abd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a"}]},{"sha":"1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDExMTA0OTdlMTdmYWM2ZGVjZWI5ZDFkNmU1MzBmOTE5N2JmYzBkNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T01:08:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:08:04Z"},"message":"fix(code): avoid duplicate \"criteria ready\" message on `/goal` revisions (#4559)\n\nFixed `/goal` showing a duplicate \"Proposed acceptance criteria are\nready.\" message when revising proposed criteria.\n\n---\n\nWhen using `/goal` and going through revision cycles of the proposed\ncriteria, `_propose_goal_rubric` re-announced \"Proposed acceptance\ncriteria are ready.\" on every regeneration, so the transcript\naccumulated a duplicate message each cycle. This suppresses the success\nmessage when regenerating from feedback (the review widget is remounted\nwith the updated criteria anyway) while still surfacing any\nunsaved-state warning.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2b61a2fb-628a-5e98-6e33-5cc275d5d42a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b436c88b1a7f0e1b941bade8496a13f6adfc823","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0b436c88b1a7f0e1b941bade8496a13f6adfc823"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvR0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf/0QADZIdjScqmy3H/WH0lD9290g\nXa3vNmnEBzBDXXiryU9CYA6exO+MKsbeQwoqMBa9CuNS7hagtDG1OqxTlh68MME4\nTtYWIkApMVW86X6bw/9zak1DPc5JYp4V+84A1qodm35Wz3eYoKFmV+Q8seIKSTJE\nrd5wNFQ/2vGMRKX03bynwrL3Uge+U2ZhCCaCh3ybELkuvUzYxwvqjiOtHhienbuR\nF4SMCsWNiIsQT3VxwJGX9RjH/E5yhUfzYXGE4tN3QMqnlED/WW8hc5vYBhoBJwkN\nYOf34SWDUCMotOrOw+1+pHnlgOX+a4sEIE4+JU3upBN3dhcNuHbYNsI4YoWOoJ7E\n+/K6/xGdqPwtN8uGxCymQeARR3SL4NiWWm8MjfJFvkhqnO1YBBFFuiBGJxE2DLWt\n37E5UbrGZrw0vhYX2aeNtPH6ebRCr7HSzFjleMEJaJLGl3BF6owd9XClTFj1KeB5\nyJBcFwt9BjeqcHT4+nsHSHzCrwC2ezeDbApdYF5mNXzXz2SL4+gJ53BqEt/VCblJ\nEgJh4EYRXfozO7rD3OHtq669pmD4nhD96yhv+JUJEB82bdhSspXjaZcocgTGny5Q\n9DZQ6U1Uu5chrmrV+B2SIYub8KhO/O1/j48YrflMooPMZHwNLfagPkkU563OBmzT\nQbBD73OMK+Vw1lCPls6k\n=Cg4F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0b436c88b1a7f0e1b941bade8496a13f6adfc823\nparent ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783559284 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783559284 -0400\n\nfix(code): avoid duplicate \"criteria ready\" message on `/goal` revisions (#4559)\n\nFixed `/goal` showing a duplicate \"Proposed acceptance criteria are\nready.\" message when revising proposed criteria.\n\n---\n\nWhen using `/goal` and going through revision cycles of the proposed\ncriteria, `_propose_goal_rubric` re-announced \"Proposed acceptance\ncriteria are ready.\" on every regeneration, so the transcript\naccumulated a duplicate message each cycle. This suppresses the success\nmessage when regenerating from feedback (the review widget is remounted\nwith the updated criteria anyway) while still surfacing any\nunsaved-state warning.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2b61a2fb-628a-5e98-6e33-5cc275d5d42a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:08:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1110497e17fac6deceb9d1d6e530f9197bfc0d4a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e"}]},{"sha":"ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVlM2MyNjQxNWJlODRlMzY5YjgyOWZlZmIyMTQ2MWM4ZWMyMTBhNWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T01:07:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:07:53Z"},"message":"feat(code): toast on saved `/auth` API key (#4558)\n\nThe `/auth` prompt now shows a confirmation toast when an API key is\nsaved.\n\n---\n\nPressing Enter in the `/auth` key prompt persisted the credential and\nsilently closed the modal, giving no confirmation. This adds a\n\"Successfully saved key for PROVIDER\" toast on a successful save so the\naction has visible feedback. The provider label reuses\n`provider_display_name`, so it honors configured/built-in display names.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/cd83cc67-e5bc-6845-8bbe-dc0c8fc8d4bc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"142b87379a8dc18ab52c192e7d423877c541ebcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/142b87379a8dc18ab52c192e7d423877c541ebcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvRpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAye0QAIpo1EHx3rKZKtvPucEja9K8\nXKcvSgqf/YPIgRpP+O/D05y6527JZ+1faOe6USD3m0citv3+F5+UbfJQN+HFFnFR\nLBfU3WdHNYW+h/2yoGE80tsieRMyVcEgl4srbBYihBYD8rd3TrjKmnBXJM5ZNYPX\nvdrnktIRmu3svwo7Rs6GukuuVCTBYTTU0Uv2G48HASYn4nJYLGBaE6hkl+xr2xS0\njG3dL+u27aph9pRueeqjkY7wJVQhGCiR+xEA9gVD3r3laHZ0eok7p9CYYj27cfcw\ntldZzMhyHFJ/OzHk31uEkbothn4XO2xvgkGR6NVpf/kWIA/fzoe27+z+H+snQmK5\nLdrPy9PHHdE+IvUEujlJcITQomymeIzHaPwuLowATI9NJ0XYLWuEfkqlDQfsRtwR\nZzEQCJ0fVd4JRipD6qwp1AoAI8PQTM87pN/S4PYnSYEsT+rn1UkWzNo9Wxr4JZXl\nkgcWr53ENpCAbGOEPf57yNoligtxeysY042K0+NWKVQxjEgXVm0PGwb4hok0UZnm\nNuQTg2aSVktTrN8ULvI3dMguzfjaUelvcl5gAk2DrsXhHzU1p+uZven8tIYAYtqL\nHZXM/WnuQG7oyIQMFXZbjsFyt3cAtfcRGx3qZoEpIi9eANHk6iZzXJmbbmMkcM+V\nudaMVI9uygTHzOtKzKpY\n=4zhi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 142b87379a8dc18ab52c192e7d423877c541ebcc\nparent 841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783559273 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783559273 -0400\n\nfeat(code): toast on saved `/auth` API key (#4558)\n\nThe `/auth` prompt now shows a confirmation toast when an API key is\nsaved.\n\n---\n\nPressing Enter in the `/auth` key prompt persisted the credential and\nsilently closed the modal, giving no confirmation. This adds a\n\"Successfully saved key for PROVIDER\" toast on a successful save so the\naction has visible feedback. The provider label reuses\n`provider_display_name`, so it honors configured/built-in display names.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/cd83cc67-e5bc-6845-8bbe-dc0c8fc8d4bc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:07:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ee3c26415be84e369b829fefb21461c8ec210a5e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8"}]},{"sha":"841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg0MWNmOWM1NGRjODA1MTQ0OTRkNjM1MWFlZGMxNTMxMGRjZGVjZjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T00:53:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:53:04Z"},"message":"fix(infra): scan PR commit messages for banned trailers (#4580)\n\nThe banned trailer check currently validates only the would-be squash\nmerge message. That catches trailers in the PR title or description, but\nmisses trailers embedded in individual commit messages that would still\nbe pushed to `main` when a PR is merged with a rebase or merge commit.\n\nThis updates the workflow to scan PR commit messages in addition to the\nsquash merge message. It also fails closed when the workflow cannot\ninspect every commit, so the check does not report a PR as clean when an\nunscanned commit could still be rejected by the `main` ruleset.","tree":{"sha":"886928fcfe62ec0ef51ca2a0cbd590d402cb3e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/886928fcfe62ec0ef51ca2a0cbd590d402cb3e5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvDwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAngcQABRjx3nHS09JA2tCrUGmJjXO\nwCdl3sf6R/yuTBpT3F3xGFnL9Disz1fXgzizBQ7OAee32BtLfQcbdFrzq+2xmvnC\n1Dusau6+Eddp9zaapcpHvoEbP5TPSrgobWgP3s0qJFl3PkckyG8kQbPJsrsEE9IK\n+qq4X3dpvyDtXrDhiKpDIYjiwBleG9MCQmaX+Pe7ePH1qjKPnJ3GPtmMyEIgiBrd\nbF2fhrD/220ssIVkGVUOYbUA2G1MwiEXbjKeS+2S26Rui7AuoVQan0DUxf6hUmPk\nkhTbn8jtnh6FQKqLkwCJMKfYKXeBWY3zCuSDs3+1IWxeU1M+nE/bdGsHxO2x4WpE\nPZ9LNLHdC5QwNf3fHFizN8KLJrkBmud4ucBzNSK0hCZTSp+nQVRJ0NN5vThg2Vax\nm3wQ3QTebYRDGzmuzubX2M4nRN2X4xaKxDJYxcPoo6sTNT4fCHuJ4W3E0Dqla/mJ\n0xEL9FKh/10ntxHRUcjx0TvJx53JzXHRFDNysE9dajcm+GUrjJwuld+7INs5xaQU\n+hyJwD0RQsd4RhggvhzskvEoldyTNOpc+iZvIBykXCy8QE7WeLqMiOKQTcUkSEyu\n44G8rLmczDJ/tOt4cfX4jMGEWpE1xjMY7gk5W6VhEk4SUA17DoyAF6EpmmBHpxA/\n66q9ZLjQ4jrJLawft4+w\n=y5tk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 886928fcfe62ec0ef51ca2a0cbd590d402cb3e5d\nparent f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783558384 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783558384 -0400\n\nfix(infra): scan PR commit messages for banned trailers (#4580)\n\nThe banned trailer check currently validates only the would-be squash\nmerge message. That catches trailers in the PR title or description, but\nmisses trailers embedded in individual commit messages that would still\nbe pushed to `main` when a PR is merged with a rebase or merge commit.\n\nThis updates the workflow to scan PR commit messages in addition to the\nsquash merge message. It also fails closed when the workflow cannot\ninspect every commit, so the check does not report a PR as clean when an\nunscanned commit could still be rejected by the `main` ruleset.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:53:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/841cf9c54dc80514494d6351aedc15310dcdecf8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb"}]},{"sha":"f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYwN2Q2Mzg3YjdkYzFmMGU4ODBmNzc3ODQ5MDVjMmFhOTQxNDNhZGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T00:45:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:45:07Z"},"message":"feat(code): reload env from `/auth` modal via Ctrl+R (#4566)\n\nThe `/auth` API-key modal now supports `Ctrl+R` to reload credentials\nfrom `.env`/environment without restarting the app.\n\n---\n\nThe `/auth` advanced tab tells users they can set a credential env var\ninstead of pasting a key, but once they do there's no way to make the\nrunning app pick it up without a full restart — the modal becomes a dead\nend. This adds a `Ctrl+R` binding to `AuthPromptScreen` that mirrors the\nexisting `/reload` command: it re-reads `.env`/environment, re-probes\ncredential status, and — when the provider was blocked and is now\nresolvable — dismisses with `SAVED` so the caller retries the original\noperation. Otherwise it refreshes the modal in place (preserving any\nin-progress input) and toasts the outcome.\n\nA reload can only pick up `.env` files (project and global) and\nvariables present at launch; a variable `export`ed in a *separate* shell\nafter startup is invisible to the running process and genuinely needs a\nrelaunch. That caveat is now surfaced in the Advanced env-var copy and\nin the \"no credentials detected\" toast so users aren't left guessing.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/114be5ea-e7ae-9927-573f-c68a0331a448)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/114be5ea-e7ae-9927-573f-c68a0331a448/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6d07c452507dd414e99ffc9f1118a5461b55aaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f6d07c452507dd414e99ffc9f1118a5461b55aaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTu8UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA430QAGcahfZ+Z4BEVtduzwpZKdRF\nMY1moHC7FOKJubbh0Jbuqv311XJzgK8PvFxPjpX7aiCVunh0ldOtFLOn8hiFY5ng\npD7IpsXws/KpJmuQSdR8551/1EnrVz+mlf5cdDJRGdks9EwwskgPKC4bWenqpWsE\nhXCfIiteamcU5em4fOwRwlOkey1Tyots+jbe/PbI94gxCfDtOIIuHokUxixgGu35\n+QiZ8CAGiwx8CGV+0gclCGF5V77LaNyf2vq7FuSG0a/ivjJybh0kspbw4Pu2Y1ri\n9UO4pe6aOqZ8HNSjvV7y3CG7MemX5IWVWPSCPhRSkZff3ZDNBIqWujqpa87kZBFX\n3HcM2LK7yB9alhgdULsKn0aGkkzFee7lMe/ERl8L2dbuAX6dWoBnBv+IABJRx7RQ\n+62RzLqtvDev81vsnP+LA1djmavnarNV8EB/kq+Lvpz3PzBV6oDZ+J44YGA7wlrN\n3dqTar+4pzNG1aWDf5W7zpZhWC1SywrgtKZ/phs+TWW0L4oqhNPeCpAcaIA+q7v3\nbCblR3ORy/mVDF3XUBe0eFnH6RA6x9Y8izBwid1MTOzkb87EyIAizWrBZHkGYQBx\nXA/Wv8o3qjHh5erVJasEnWGwyDwmt+Fr2dteaLD+YYaWKmclhH6DEk+OZILhjo8U\nJpmK6jIvun2Q/BjelTln\n=+1YZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f6d07c452507dd414e99ffc9f1118a5461b55aaa\nparent 7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783557907 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783557907 -0400\n\nfeat(code): reload env from `/auth` modal via Ctrl+R (#4566)\n\nThe `/auth` API-key modal now supports `Ctrl+R` to reload credentials\nfrom `.env`/environment without restarting the app.\n\n---\n\nThe `/auth` advanced tab tells users they can set a credential env var\ninstead of pasting a key, but once they do there's no way to make the\nrunning app pick it up without a full restart — the modal becomes a dead\nend. This adds a `Ctrl+R` binding to `AuthPromptScreen` that mirrors the\nexisting `/reload` command: it re-reads `.env`/environment, re-probes\ncredential status, and — when the provider was blocked and is now\nresolvable — dismisses with `SAVED` so the caller retries the original\noperation. Otherwise it refreshes the modal in place (preserving any\nin-progress input) and toasts the outcome.\n\nA reload can only pick up `.env` files (project and global) and\nvariables present at launch; a variable `export`ed in a *separate* shell\nafter startup is invisible to the running process and genuinely needs a\nrelaunch. That caveat is now surfaced in the Advanced env-var copy and\nin the \"no credentials detected\" toast so users aren't left guessing.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/114be5ea-e7ae-9927-573f-c68a0331a448)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/114be5ea-e7ae-9927-573f-c68a0331a448/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:45:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f07d6387b7dc1f0e880f77784905c2aa94143adb/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41"}]},{"sha":"7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdjNWJmNTQyYzJmNThmYTQ2ZWNkNzA4YzY2Y2QxODE3YTBlYmRjNDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T00:36:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:36:51Z"},"message":"feat(code): add `[startup].mode` default approval mode (#4573)\n\nAdd a `[startup].mode` option to `~/.deepagents/config.toml` for\n`deepagents-code`, accepting `manual` (default) or `dangerously-auto`,\nto set the interactive TUI's default approval mode without passing\n`-y`/`--auto-approve` each launch.\n\n---\n\nLets users pick the interactive TUI's default approval mode in\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml` instead of passing `-y`/`--auto-approve` on\nevery launch. The `[startup].mode` option accepts `manual` (default,\nhuman-in-the-loop approvals) or `dangerously-auto` (auto-approve gated\ntool calls at launch).\n\nPrecedence: an explicit `-y`/`--auto-approve` flag still wins; when\nomitted, `[startup].mode` decides; the built-in fallback is `manual`, so\nexisting behavior is unchanged. Implemented by switching the flag's\nargparse default to `None` (so \"omitted\" is distinguishable from \"set\")\nand resolving the effective value at interactive dispatch. A new\nvalidated `load_startup_mode` loader mirrors the existing\n`[threads].sort_order` pattern and falls back to `manual` on\nunset/unreadable/invalid values. Follows the `config.toml`-only approach\n(a `ConfigOption` in the manifest for `dcode config` discovery, no new\nenv var). Non-interactive (`-n`) mode computes its own approval behavior\nand is untouched.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/82b4ad9e-f42e-7f73-ae2f-5a0830f3f8cc)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/82b4ad9e-f42e-7f73-ae2f-5a0830f3f8cc/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"784e1f9f2b9fd5b46c3c0664b53cddd2157f4e5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/784e1f9f2b9fd5b46c3c0664b53cddd2157f4e5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTu0jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ7MQAGO9mJeGcOEq496NI0HoBCQS\nEK4Dus2NSbm1aAo1AxVCYNhI6pZacm430EHIYc+C+37naPLswPP9NgnEkOF1xLyn\nsW0U7/ARCwLgss4UTiHD1sPyKJ53gylbVaAtNht/k5YCqs7TgszOIQPKNFMlg57h\nTJZBvKQBpKoS0j/VW4kOenNIgpNYKLX3VYOTCUTp4A95c2BWcH2m2ygLWqHfBv8a\nHsJ6ZS8Kxdiln/7y2y97gA5VIz0J+bxa4eV+Ee2SGne4f0pMTXaxx+b56QCXvArH\nfMIBrAsQbmRlz1hDyRBjCRf3vy8mG9zN4YPAAoZoW7avGEXvxi0QCSA3fpY8LW+N\nkRIe9WCe8D//29KsoeLC5ScWM5oSR/rhiF2iMDJ98PAKFo4xGA9ff5LEvJyXLobE\nxeoV6JblGmVlVplPcry0U5Zs7JP90g58j7OoPj3ozvLmrkJRlRlKehtByOenigju\ndQtb+Ss8QXPRz4bWqfyjTQMe2I0dcToG8rXFnSUVSgYbsRmFaN2cSIQvuNPlw8u0\nYVQ2i/d9SfkBv0mUCiBVAzwJHa3IbT6zRkGbKpVTDRka/6BjbKzwQGtFWCxLiuQH\n1AC79djEazXKFtgeCL4OtuHzyKGu1kagUgoy0+soB/6uXxdE4J/zpCY7LPfQRlhP\n+nH+TXSYL3+P+Lhh2BoX\n=EyGl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 784e1f9f2b9fd5b46c3c0664b53cddd2157f4e5e\nparent 6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783557411 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783557411 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add `[startup].mode` default approval mode (#4573)\n\nAdd a `[startup].mode` option to `~/.deepagents/config.toml` for\n`deepagents-code`, accepting `manual` (default) or `dangerously-auto`,\nto set the interactive TUI's default approval mode without passing\n`-y`/`--auto-approve` each launch.\n\n---\n\nLets users pick the interactive TUI's default approval mode in\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml` instead of passing `-y`/`--auto-approve` on\nevery launch. The `[startup].mode` option accepts `manual` (default,\nhuman-in-the-loop approvals) or `dangerously-auto` (auto-approve gated\ntool calls at launch).\n\nPrecedence: an explicit `-y`/`--auto-approve` flag still wins; when\nomitted, `[startup].mode` decides; the built-in fallback is `manual`, so\nexisting behavior is unchanged. Implemented by switching the flag's\nargparse default to `None` (so \"omitted\" is distinguishable from \"set\")\nand resolving the effective value at interactive dispatch. A new\nvalidated `load_startup_mode` loader mirrors the existing\n`[threads].sort_order` pattern and falls back to `manual` on\nunset/unreadable/invalid values. Follows the `config.toml`-only approach\n(a `ConfigOption` in the manifest for `dcode config` discovery, no new\nenv var). Non-interactive (`-n`) mode computes its own approval behavior\nand is untouched.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/82b4ad9e-f42e-7f73-ae2f-5a0830f3f8cc)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/82b4ad9e-f42e-7f73-ae2f-5a0830f3f8cc/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:36:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7c5bf542c2f58fa46ecd708c66cd1817a0ebdc41/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb"}]},{"sha":"6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZlODk0MTc3NmNkY2MzNTkwOWRhMzA1ZjNiYjM5NTAwYzBmNDc5Y2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T00:27:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:27:44Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep notification center open for API-key entry (#4568)\n\nPressing `Esc` in the API-key entry prompt reached from a notification\nnow returns to the notification center instead of closing all open\nmodals.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user opens the notification center with `ctrl+n`, selects a\nservice notification, and chooses **Enter API key**, they are still\nworking through that notification. If they decide not to enter a key\nyet, `Esc` should take them back to the notification details so they can\nreview, suppress, or choose another notification — not drop them back\ninto the main chat screen.\n\nBefore this change, selecting **Enter API key** dismissed the\nnotification center before the API-key prompt opened. Because the center\nwas already gone, pressing `Esc` in the prompt fell through to the base\nchat screen instead of returning to the notifications viewer.\n\nFor example:\n\n- Before:\n  1. Press `ctrl+n` to open notifications.\n  2. Open a Tavily API-key notification.\n  3. Select **Enter API key**.\n  4. Press `Esc` in the API-key prompt.\n5. The prompt closes and the user lands in the main chat screen, losing\nthe notification context.\n- After:\n  1. Press `ctrl+n` to open notifications.\n  2. Open a Tavily API-key notification.\n  3. Select **Enter API key**.\n  4. Press `Esc` in the API-key prompt.\n5. The prompt closes and the user returns to the notification center,\nwith the notification details still available.\n\nThe fix treats `ENTER_API_KEY` as an in-place action, mirroring the\nexisting `SUPPRESS` handling: instead of dismissing the center, the\ndetail modal posts a `NotificationActionRequested` message. The app\nhandles it in a worker so the message pump is not blocked while the\nprompt awaits input, pushes the `AuthPromptScreen` on top of the\nstill-mounted center, then reloads the center once the action resolves.\nSaving the key drops the notification entry, and the center dismisses\nonly when the list becomes empty.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7f8edaca-58bc-3065-4243-6edc6d5d3449)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b0af8d146e987c6031476da8a11a0e76947b43a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2b0af8d146e987c6031476da8a11a0e76947b43a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTusACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATosQAICwvDKcZ7d4dsiBpgWpNGtY\nRF9ZjFzf0eEA1H5XLciXq5soaUCFNElw03l3GaIDdXUG9Esf/qRdd3I9FKwCi5zc\nzczV58zgrxjWAPjBeayHycia8qCz3FtrddtbUG5uBandG4KGu1OOVjduOimfHVTk\nPo+7bx+U7EZ5gbRX7AhHduFHCqGiT7yFZ8hTGv5jTDguemjYwIG06mix81K+eoMS\n6Ya+IQoqatxVgVlQB43kDPNAODeT1EJXlOh/bTOzVeuj+9YAFdC6kl+7d7+VCIGD\nrcp8rFW6nOXU5upzjU/X6weHfDraf4WNNXC+ADc4bG5cX02yul/+xZsv7PpEuuM3\ncoqbZWrwuQ6VRTu+8M1Kl+N3foXFk1+LErTpsEJV5X//CJStd2vkAR3PNId5NTd3\n6g++q7X9pNqbi0juwxoawIeTahgTZNzARdSYZ025Lh92p2GuYHJ/k0aZE6l4+78y\nB2J8ImLwvyzmKpDsHIQszLWGVk1/mHk9iHv0Pykv3a2riZnAhqFEJWEKIgIDQLUL\n9d4Qmnl6Y3CZoA7vTxEpAIULNlIRlajpBEdfSvrpqHUria2kgV2lzrxZJ4XjQzo9\nbaOkjZlLHx2noeXqCOspZak2L5f54xurCWuSfVJFGMlsl9siuPH5F/FTWgTk2ray\nIPwgLxxnjc1MCY2gCaM3\n=08iy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2b0af8d146e987c6031476da8a11a0e76947b43a\nparent 1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783556864 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783556864 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep notification center open for API-key entry (#4568)\n\nPressing `Esc` in the API-key entry prompt reached from a notification\nnow returns to the notification center instead of closing all open\nmodals.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user opens the notification center with `ctrl+n`, selects a\nservice notification, and chooses **Enter API key**, they are still\nworking through that notification. If they decide not to enter a key\nyet, `Esc` should take them back to the notification details so they can\nreview, suppress, or choose another notification — not drop them back\ninto the main chat screen.\n\nBefore this change, selecting **Enter API key** dismissed the\nnotification center before the API-key prompt opened. Because the center\nwas already gone, pressing `Esc` in the prompt fell through to the base\nchat screen instead of returning to the notifications viewer.\n\nFor example:\n\n- Before:\n  1. Press `ctrl+n` to open notifications.\n  2. Open a Tavily API-key notification.\n  3. Select **Enter API key**.\n  4. Press `Esc` in the API-key prompt.\n5. The prompt closes and the user lands in the main chat screen, losing\nthe notification context.\n- After:\n  1. Press `ctrl+n` to open notifications.\n  2. Open a Tavily API-key notification.\n  3. Select **Enter API key**.\n  4. Press `Esc` in the API-key prompt.\n5. The prompt closes and the user returns to the notification center,\nwith the notification details still available.\n\nThe fix treats `ENTER_API_KEY` as an in-place action, mirroring the\nexisting `SUPPRESS` handling: instead of dismissing the center, the\ndetail modal posts a `NotificationActionRequested` message. The app\nhandles it in a worker so the message pump is not blocked while the\nprompt awaits input, pushes the `AuthPromptScreen` on top of the\nstill-mounted center, then reloads the center once the action resolves.\nSaving the key drops the notification entry, and the center dismisses\nonly when the list becomes empty.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7f8edaca-58bc-3065-4243-6edc6d5d3449)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:27:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6e8941776cdcc35909da305f3bb39500c0f479cb/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f"}]},{"sha":"1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDEzOThmZWVjYTUwN2NhYjllYzUxYTY2NjA0ZDQ2Yzc0N2Y3ZmNkMmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T00:26:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:26:14Z"},"message":"fix(code): dedupe update/install log path output (#4553)\n\n`dcode update` and install commands no longer print the same log path\ntwice.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, update and install flows printed the log path once by itself\nand then repeated it in the tail command:\n\n```text\nUpdate log: /tmp/deepagents-update.log\nTail progress: tail -f /tmp/deepagents-update.log\n```\n\nNow they print a single copy-pasteable command next to the log label:\n\n```text\nUpdate log: tail -f /tmp/deepagents-update.log\n```\n\nThe same before/after applies to `Install log:` output for both extras\ninstalls and arbitrary package installs. This keeps the path visible\nwhile avoiding duplicate path output in the terminal.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/91e79ce5-84aa-d27e-8cd5-dae63b3546c1)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"317eabdc7ccf093083f793c8fa6472f9f1bdf575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/317eabdc7ccf093083f793c8fa6472f9f1bdf575"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTuqmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARU0QAHiNyI2PTGtf7v0JQxlaKvPh\npVZoDURcUfhVl8/HewOjcpsoyedDzVVgU65t4AKj/Yd8JmVRhswD127tQrFkurR8\nR8gLGSVtLV0vD2me+KgI/MApne4JXIHdI8AfisBykUd9KJ9CrmLvlUjvwhOw9Vsf\nUz/+0c7ydP3I4goRgZB2OBLyMLkZ36JtLN8hMUlX0B+3tl0/HLzMkrCImu9Rc2Nr\nOOTfh9+0vnSPbYw5Gzg1Yjp854tEztSkQSyyYyzM9F3+lNorZtuHEzENLG0oiwgc\no7IAMy193HRoU1rBTb6H0Etj8ufY611/GwxnC5W7cXl7hz3wQOpy75PgU9o3chHa\nOUdaRepEd4dwaM7TvmdhOBbba52ii3AVNBTb16KHUqJtR4+NT0nUruzAS33PNSUh\n3zZi0NMXVwIc5NZ+U1Kvny5tk57XY1wJGTbWVlzM5fhp7mRfQt6/oWc1GDdFy053\n/JOprYAP7lw0IfucgnSNs8Vyfiwq1PVOsA1Vbswz3y2p+W18oB51pZaXm0o/M64W\ncUvPQpx5hfB5qWeFRpR7A/v3Whk96yRAmKM7nRaDE54Wjjgy1pT+iOLj6T3ajhcn\nTLFSeaCMjtIh4cHcPo9cBeObLAXSpo2CLZFmy/FDzgUhU5qHzVw0SIpvpwkMcXFS\nNx9YmidSI5v88zhqoC8K\n=Cg/b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 317eabdc7ccf093083f793c8fa6472f9f1bdf575\nparent 434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783556774 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783556774 -0400\n\nfix(code): dedupe update/install log path output (#4553)\n\n`dcode update` and install commands no longer print the same log path\ntwice.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, update and install flows printed the log path once by itself\nand then repeated it in the tail command:\n\n```text\nUpdate log: /tmp/deepagents-update.log\nTail progress: tail -f /tmp/deepagents-update.log\n```\n\nNow they print a single copy-pasteable command next to the log label:\n\n```text\nUpdate log: tail -f /tmp/deepagents-update.log\n```\n\nThe same before/after applies to `Install log:` output for both extras\ninstalls and arbitrary package installs. This keeps the path visible\nwhile avoiding duplicate path output in the terminal.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/91e79ce5-84aa-d27e-8cd5-dae63b3546c1)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:26:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1398feeca507cab9ec51a66604d46c747f7fcd2f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70"}]},{"sha":"434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzNGM4NGFlMTQ0YjAzMTlhZmUzN2Q2ZjJkYmFkZmQ3ZjVmYzlmNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-09T00:06:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:06:53Z"},"message":"fix(code): clarify managed `rg` install failures (#4578)\n\n`dcode` now gives clearer messages when managed ripgrep is unavailable\nfor the current system or missing from the pinned upstream artifacts,\nand POSIX managed ripgrep installs now use a relative symlink to a\nversioned binary for better portability.\n\n---\n\nManaged ripgrep setup used to collapse permanent gaps and transient\ndownload failures into the same generic failure path. This makes those\ncases distinct and makes POSIX managed installs more portable.\n\n## Before\n\n- As a user on an unsupported system, I saw a generic managed ripgrep\ninstall failure and could not tell whether retrying would help.\n- As a user whose pinned managed ripgrep artifact was missing upstream,\nI saw the same kind of failure as a network outage.\n- As a user who moved, restored, or bind-mounted `~/.deepagents`, a\nmanaged helper link could bake in the old absolute path or become stale.\n- As a user with a broken managed `rg` symlink, dcode could fall back to\nanother `rg` on `PATH` instead of repairing the managed install.\n\n## After\n\n- As a user on an unsupported system, I get a direct message that\nmanaged ripgrep is not available for my platform and can install ripgrep\nmanually or opt into the system installer path.\n- As a user whose pinned managed ripgrep artifact returns HTTP 404, I\nget a message that the artifact is unavailable for the pinned version,\ninstead of a generic network failure.\n- As a user with transient download trouble, I still get the normal\ndownload-failure path and can retry.\n- As a user who moves or bind-mounts `~/.deepagents`, the `rg`\nentrypoint is a relative symlink to a versioned managed binary, so it is\nless fragile.\n- As a user with a dangling managed `rg` symlink, dcode treats it as\nmanaged state and repairs it rather than silently substituting a system\nbinary.","tree":{"sha":"cc2b51e705e04eb64817116a09890bbc4323c28d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cc2b51e705e04eb64817116a09890bbc4323c28d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTuYdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK3kQAE+E7OOLOHkRUb5IrEHjUCTM\nPZvQcLeUlvFf5SQ4O2bRA9tQIqq0TZAYpU6bxiFZlRgU9TWEP87H814RP+FKUAbJ\nSgf6Bv0Mn+r5nQbvlqU3bHLYIuUdZcMEYfSfiOeoTB0Dhf8urC8jN650RE5TJY0Z\nP0jMaJg/GkKzL/uNUnjtroAgEs9y/Tl2YwpKF35DufBICMBA0G5FDRQLCumm9avs\nDY67i0LWuen+IsFScQx7waeBU+tlvyqwJNaMQGPfvF0hlxa3Z/FcWCQf/VVYzlIf\nn6iwAb3quo6nltWZaQGQUgGeS2v2lqsw/Ga+yV76t3RXiFuuCS59VB9fyUOu/2Qr\nOyVu08kW0L/c1SxLSdNjKdfPeTFB9MEYXWyzCBey6hzKouF1r28r30xsmE/ZciqU\ncwPrNJRmYpenxlTnzKTJBf1nly3UBnwBPwqJ4d+kPe5LYm8MtcKfCAJkI4Qix9cF\nPoD57ulqMozo3nv2gKO6sfuEz795paeDC+Hiz/VDYy9at4gkxy2ve8vxQZR0sODA\njfEhpQ4czTLTBr4x425E/9yunbBrcQ5hYZdFTAMedK96adDmsQ+bB3cHaUWShBOY\nSdUkZDS9oZ6f5TWnLVctrSy0OUNtxbfSNY3UDytbi00kVyzQjw+bvuRa/z69whLx\n5ch4F83GVNhbpPpZ/JEI\n=f0aI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cc2b51e705e04eb64817116a09890bbc4323c28d\nparent f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783555613 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783555613 -0400\n\nfix(code): clarify managed `rg` install failures (#4578)\n\n`dcode` now gives clearer messages when managed ripgrep is unavailable\nfor the current system or missing from the pinned upstream artifacts,\nand POSIX managed ripgrep installs now use a relative symlink to a\nversioned binary for better portability.\n\n---\n\nManaged ripgrep setup used to collapse permanent gaps and transient\ndownload failures into the same generic failure path. This makes those\ncases distinct and makes POSIX managed installs more portable.\n\n## Before\n\n- As a user on an unsupported system, I saw a generic managed ripgrep\ninstall failure and could not tell whether retrying would help.\n- As a user whose pinned managed ripgrep artifact was missing upstream,\nI saw the same kind of failure as a network outage.\n- As a user who moved, restored, or bind-mounted `~/.deepagents`, a\nmanaged helper link could bake in the old absolute path or become stale.\n- As a user with a broken managed `rg` symlink, dcode could fall back to\nanother `rg` on `PATH` instead of repairing the managed install.\n\n## After\n\n- As a user on an unsupported system, I get a direct message that\nmanaged ripgrep is not available for my platform and can install ripgrep\nmanually or opt into the system installer path.\n- As a user whose pinned managed ripgrep artifact returns HTTP 404, I\nget a message that the artifact is unavailable for the pinned version,\ninstead of a generic network failure.\n- As a user with transient download trouble, I still get the normal\ndownload-failure path and can retry.\n- As a user who moves or bind-mounts `~/.deepagents`, the `rg`\nentrypoint is a relative symlink to a versioned managed binary, so it is\nless fragile.\n- As a user with a dangling managed `rg` symlink, dcode treats it as\nmanaged state and repairs it rather than silently substituting a system\nbinary.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:06:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/434c84ae144b0319afe37d6f2dbadfd7f5fc9f70/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361"}]},{"sha":"f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY2ZWU3MGMwMGFjNmFkN2IxYjE4MDE1NTAxOGI3OTQzMDhhMTgzNjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-08T23:38:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T23:38:58Z"},"message":"fix(code): preserve transcript order during virtualization (#4549)\n\nFixes long `dcode` conversations so transcript virtualization preserves\nmessage order, keeps the scroll position stable when loading older\nhistory, and avoids older or newer messages disappearing when scrolling.\n\n---\n\n- Make `MessageStore` the canonical source for virtualized transcript\ngeometry with height estimates, protected live rows, and spacer-backed\nscroll ranges.\n- Keep rendered transcript rows chronological around spinner/queued\nwidgets by mounting all transcript content above the bottom spacer.\n- Sync live tool state back into `MessageStore` so hydrated rows\npreserve status, output, expansion, and rejection details.\n- Hydrate the hidden tail before appending fresh output, and only\nadvance `_visible_end` on `append` when already at the tail, so new live\noutput never skips messages hidden below the window.\n\n## Correctness & robustness (review pass)\n- **Fix scroll-anchor double-count on hydrate-above.** The top spacer\nalready shrinks by the hydrated rows' height, so `scroll_y` now stays\nput instead of jumping the viewport down by ~a screenful when scrolling\nup through history.\n- **Keep the mounted window contiguous on partial failure.** Both\nhydrate directions now mount from the window edge outward and stop at\nthe first failure, so the count-based\n`mark_hydrated`/`mark_hydrated_below` can't desync\n`_visible_start`/`_visible_end` from the DOM.\n- **Fail safe when syncing tool state.** If a tool widget can't be\nserialized, its row stays protected (we can't prove it's terminal); an\nunknown/unmapped status no longer unprotects a still-live row. The\nadapter's tool-sync hook is now total (never raises), so a sync failure\ncan't abort a turn.\n- **Reason-keyed protection.** `MessageStore` tracks protection reasons\n(active stream vs. live tool) independently, so releasing one source\nnever revokes another's protection.\n- **Remove dead/speculative API.** Dropped `MessageWindow`,\n`get_window_for_viewport`, `prefix_height`, `total_estimated_height`,\nand `get_protected_messages` (unused by the feature); the live path uses\n`estimate_height`/`range_height`.\n- **Single clamped write path for `height_hint`** (`set_height_hint`),\nplus docstring/comment fixes for the now-populated height hints and\nprotection semantics.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"7eec5b8ca6cb25740cdc91c6d4acab11c7f44527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7eec5b8ca6cb25740cdc91c6d4acab11c7f44527"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTt+SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPVMQAHuKvLuG4AEO/mHclwc1ADTW\n7YaqGBGvGZNLXzSoOekOdmI+B+ArZbw8JLIj17Fq87wBW9emS3WeNjFzDtzynerU\nPuLeGLaoEPev7i/0qK8w39mWnleua+WB8bZ9cBTcksCOQi2xN9TZ4r2LUqzfrcv1\nIllbdPULQhRWKxdkJhO+Pov3q1oqppWTYLpvYXJNx6gVLQYB/tsIf96EgZv+3/kt\nEGqYc/FtysU4F7tnKG+rIG3t/1gqsWh+DVLgfpvfGZLGdPg8A3euEjjKteM2prQp\n0Q8oo7CoTM1wugyYlDwU/b8xbmjKSmaJT2+fViFqt8TF26UskC4F5h6NPKkdTeV0\njNtR6t4ntVUb7r3Xk98N7tK7Fnr7/g+mHMOXfTgcQpWcYjEjzaskTgB8+OJgyJ3T\nHK+BUpiyFAYtj80Hig/b77ReYbGBxgp/ip8ZPjjy13FXKiMypKzAtXage0YfUfKm\niUPp9JIUHrmnT8VWAFVFAC4IVohzY08zJA/upNRJXsNfM0eV1k0GbkdqCdJqbUAk\nJmzowpqfQrjAUv6BNWWo2u4ApsA0+pWRkfyBW/O86bgcnqzlsbD39/gFG9qX8CAg\nar/WEWgNhIqBc50/3an51eDdX8Ln2WyitVxcyj0iOSa0mVraqSM7T04idHx2W4/7\nHP3GCPTpBtHFoZP683IX\n=55QD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7eec5b8ca6cb25740cdc91c6d4acab11c7f44527\nparent fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1783553938 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783553938 -0400\n\nfix(code): preserve transcript order during virtualization (#4549)\n\nFixes long `dcode` conversations so transcript virtualization preserves\nmessage order, keeps the scroll position stable when loading older\nhistory, and avoids older or newer messages disappearing when scrolling.\n\n---\n\n- Make `MessageStore` the canonical source for virtualized transcript\ngeometry with height estimates, protected live rows, and spacer-backed\nscroll ranges.\n- Keep rendered transcript rows chronological around spinner/queued\nwidgets by mounting all transcript content above the bottom spacer.\n- Sync live tool state back into `MessageStore` so hydrated rows\npreserve status, output, expansion, and rejection details.\n- Hydrate the hidden tail before appending fresh output, and only\nadvance `_visible_end` on `append` when already at the tail, so new live\noutput never skips messages hidden below the window.\n\n## Correctness & robustness (review pass)\n- **Fix scroll-anchor double-count on hydrate-above.** The top spacer\nalready shrinks by the hydrated rows' height, so `scroll_y` now stays\nput instead of jumping the viewport down by ~a screenful when scrolling\nup through history.\n- **Keep the mounted window contiguous on partial failure.** Both\nhydrate directions now mount from the window edge outward and stop at\nthe first failure, so the count-based\n`mark_hydrated`/`mark_hydrated_below` can't desync\n`_visible_start`/`_visible_end` from the DOM.\n- **Fail safe when syncing tool state.** If a tool widget can't be\nserialized, its row stays protected (we can't prove it's terminal); an\nunknown/unmapped status no longer unprotects a still-live row. The\nadapter's tool-sync hook is now total (never raises), so a sync failure\ncan't abort a turn.\n- **Reason-keyed protection.** `MessageStore` tracks protection reasons\n(active stream vs. live tool) independently, so releasing one source\nnever revokes another's protection.\n- **Remove dead/speculative API.** Dropped `MessageWindow`,\n`get_window_for_viewport`, `prefix_height`, `total_estimated_height`,\nand `get_protected_messages` (unused by the feature); the live path uses\n`estimate_height`/`range_height`.\n- **Single clamped write path for `height_hint`** (`set_height_hint`),\nplus docstring/comment fixes for the now-populated height hints and\nprotection semantics.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T23:38:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f6ee70c00ac6ad7b1b180155018b794308a18361/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70"}]},{"sha":"fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZjY2YwMzczMjE0MGQzOTc0OWU3MGU4ZmM2Y2I3ZDczMTI0YTFkNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-08T23:34:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T23:34:24Z"},"message":"feat(code): restore interrupted prompt to input on ESC (#4544)\n\nPressing `ESC` to interrupt the agent now returns the interrupted prompt\nto the chat input when the input is empty.\n\n---\n\nWhen `ESC` interrupts a running agent turn, the prompt that was being\nprocessed is now moved back into the chat input if the input is empty,\nso it can be edited and resubmitted. This mirrors the existing\nqueued-message pop behavior. A non-empty draft in the input is left\nuntouched so typed text is never clobbered.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4708dd80-b2c2-8688-8b1c-ab77cb51228f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"61bfeef49bef7505e66a821a5f9196d6ebb22985","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/61bfeef49bef7505e66a821a5f9196d6ebb22985"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTt6ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd2MQAGaP1GET7UERGNU/m8/9hyQW\nl+ZnAY1xJBqvDfSwXs1GYUJjWaDvq2MSjwf2HsHT1lDfzoC+xD0qkKOj5LuJYkT9\nl1AdJcQpN+f/IbVmUc/3hSKMv3YQpLpMv1rRH1iumOg0rAcOEYxK4M7kSymJ34Cm\nj56CcT1DWTc8UGtq5upzkQh8sN0E/QdnYs3Rzrfsul0asaPilY+5COGqo/9IFwCG\nNOrTsGSrUTi7HgnoyIxcVZ1nrLEowJLdLf+4yKVInJippOM81FSOyvRqemsBQkZY\niCqXryd8lHV5fPegyGpcAQqG0x/U3Qblw01gDj4eDGnxaG+JfQjEvrxNgCbblPPg\nIdNZQpL/uc1tezoxdd/GCbpiCi1xnWiLPBPyJPwHh/t/6JEOm+U1QQlq80zC0hio\nWscSzRaAJ7xOxbJPqTxhlG1zgvoUr9kkasgUuXI2QceH7RL+rHLpcqK9IJoHOtSU\nZ6ubck8dPan2Snv5nein1xLJjwO4KK/tzBWG40vXvBB1dbnmOcnVxiT868qYiQLV\nJ1NKHiNBYKpfOyyx61tFuaqalZ8Kk4Q8uMf+OShHmswlVhSgZdeAc4ckieiAT2ui\n1dUV3NwsuyNwAUxOzhuagcFqIRaIJN8s3iMJ4C4zDsGmoZNCJMTafBD1gRLgp2z4\njEkd2rNiIxYOOb0ADZht\n=nDMr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 61bfeef49bef7505e66a821a5f9196d6ebb22985\nparent edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783553664 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783553664 -0400\n\nfeat(code): restore interrupted prompt to input on ESC (#4544)\n\nPressing `ESC` to interrupt the agent now returns the interrupted prompt\nto the chat input when the input is empty.\n\n---\n\nWhen `ESC` interrupts a running agent turn, the prompt that was being\nprocessed is now moved back into the chat input if the input is empty,\nso it can be edited and resubmitted. This mirrors the existing\nqueued-message pop behavior. A non-empty draft in the input is left\nuntouched so typed text is never clobbered.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4708dd80-b2c2-8688-8b1c-ab77cb51228f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T23:34:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fccf03732140d39749e70e8fc6cb7d73124a1d70/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d"}]},{"sha":"edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVkYWM4MmM4MzdkZThlMTJiNThiOTdhYzI1YWNjMzFmNzQzZDRjNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-08T23:23:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T23:23:30Z"},"message":"fix(code): queue `/mcp login` sent before the server connects (#4533)\n\n`/mcp login <server>` was rejected with a warning when the local server\nwas still connecting (or its subprocess didn't yet exist), forcing users\nto retry. This queues the login via the existing deferred-action\nmechanism so it runs automatically once the server is ready — matching\nhow a mid-run login already defers.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b1b39843-c3e1-4537-459a-8eb8cc86a1c3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"491bd8e9545b70e34a7e430d59514c8f5211dafc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/491bd8e9545b70e34a7e430d59514c8f5211dafc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTtvyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoAAQAKdnL9uyc07Gq5rD10BLZoOS\npExqcvUB5K8yNhI/FFgWgGQWxtZz1Znll/yQhhUmQB1NetgxGTxb6dxOczCefYvP\nSPVD43CK9UDS6+kl0CvaLwFqAxg+4gX2dCKNZH86eoynHTTnVq+noOCUmgfVMlxB\nMxqCyqi41lNnZq0qI73o1xshDoGrvgNkIouAsVTtMc91hJ/FJFlGDb8IwclahrcH\nyGL+AMJ8jgyCaMQBiA0ZWM9/1d2rN4JZeO2Z8kTuoT1JhA0lxjJLbG0dtT2JHrtx\nkD3D0ugTkpfHVfZ6EMBKEyZ9D6/cZpSPlOtRbbnFQ35RQq3r21Ad/RUXf+KZ2J9c\nUVrrz5FWDu5yf0w/usJHG/LckS2c+eapH/QsfZDL2JIsUcvITOOdNvhcKtSN+rfr\nkuhnoA0J14rLxTPmttRSEGEB1WRkjMRBV91B+bD1lB27vpiIWy4HGOotFdHWwxAO\n7hcitT6DCd8wTXnlHGsVb6uZU+CQtin5tXRe4dvpZIvpCl75ha4zyWea4/wsghe0\nFHy5Uu8WPvpuR0NTgtPcQ60PYBgvHxMVSUixOu0MXZAPPYHOfgpNhbwfs4tastvt\nU6HedczAI0l0wo7USivH4ncxJsGN1p/e+/ocV2ihzM9lpAy5JfszLQytRFpg8ZXz\nRF+hH7EYqWkOI7A++KO/\n=W+oH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 491bd8e9545b70e34a7e430d59514c8f5211dafc\nparent aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783553010 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783553010 -0400\n\nfix(code): queue `/mcp login` sent before the server connects (#4533)\n\n`/mcp login <server>` was rejected with a warning when the local server\nwas still connecting (or its subprocess didn't yet exist), forcing users\nto retry. This queues the login via the existing deferred-action\nmechanism so it runs automatically once the server is ready — matching\nhow a mid-run login already defers.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b1b39843-c3e1-4537-459a-8eb8cc86a1c3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T23:23:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/edac82c837de8e12b58b97ac25acc31f743d4c5d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34"}]},{"sha":"aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhZDUzMGMwOTlhODdhNjBmOTExNWQyNDFkOWUxZThiMzc0YWZkMzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-08T22:50:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T22:50:56Z"},"message":"chore(code): compare installs by inode in shadowing check (#4577)\n\nThe installer no longer prints a spurious \"shadowing install\" warning\nwhen `~/.local/bin` appears on `PATH` under a non-normalized alias (such\nas `~/.local/share/../bin`) that resolves to the same directory.\n\n---\n\nThe `deepagents-code` installer printed a spurious \"shadowing install\"\nwarning on every run for users whose `PATH` contains a non-normalized\nalias of `~/.local/bin` — most commonly `~/.local/share/../bin`, where\n`share/..` collapses back to `.local`. Some third-party tools write that\nun-normalized spelling into a shell profile (derived from\n`$XDG_DATA_HOME/../bin`), and it can sort before the canonical entry.\nBoth spellings resolve to the same uv-tool symlink the installer just\ncreated, but `detect_shadowing_install` compared `PATH` strings, so the\nalias looked like a separate, older install.\n\nThe primary fix makes the guard compare by inode using bash's `-ef` test\n(same device+inode, resolves `..` and symlinks) in addition to the\nexisting string equality, so same-file aliases short-circuit and never\nwarn. Both operands are guaranteed to exist at that point, and a\ngenuinely different binary at a distinct inode still fails `-ef` and\ncorrectly warns, so only the false positive is suppressed. Secondarily,\n`local_bin_in_profile` now also recognizes the `~/.local/share/../bin`\nspelling so the installer doesn't append a duplicate `~/.local/bin` PATH\nline; this covers the common alias only and isn't a full path\nnormalizer.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/870c16ab-41c7-3eee-e0d1-55385367ec4f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6554f20a1313f965742e8d0cdb94709cd1832002","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6554f20a1313f965742e8d0cdb94709cd1832002"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTtRQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA640QAEPRhcjSaItoStljMszipyAz\nxHk1vdHIPeB+BONgMODQq0eP5+K6g4UkxgjpbLpZa24UwzjO/DX/zwvWR2umy3kL\nv4eSJJAkXwTsTj6E9hIDvaxawWTga5+ddCKF7ogO9UMJUCkKE5bwIteCJneH9ayQ\nofRJSWPAzlzcA6p1NPkyivJ+QvGP39XxHNkfZw/wheobuOzpITvin52ve1It9B6U\nmWHUGzK+z7w1CL5dYHxwrqZT8R54KgWYCtBHGzV6s5W1WUUsdTAxpOAH4pXbgGhM\nRvSPaDnN6H3gISrBkZ9hCE3q3mIGRxenATXsu4MdH+wefLDs9QamQ/KF1X4ERMOu\nX2b54HdrM9DIXtjc4o1sHEsYWl1HAbmUprvG+qFuR9RyyfS0YfAUDC98s/OCuV46\n2+X18FzHqmGVtX5ctkByYOQtP7Ea531LSkgHy9UHwFqbHQw4FWZF0YuA/z+2uJAt\nrbbESGWZSRdxP6zMG5L2Rca/15hEOpd0dPtxEO+YyhO/FvF5xKe1OpBeH1EyC4UN\n4pfJNKSLLkXC7tZ/eluxhCEseUG4O4Ab6EL0PM3rCzoxtJriJLcRT29ivyvsDaeG\nLLiLm8/7Vjz3IBkjUZ+2u9pgstSVXYfTZbsQNU59YGYtVZHmiSiq7KMyy8b0XJAS\nealC+Y1Af9dDuWc3BUO+\n=W57B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6554f20a1313f965742e8d0cdb94709cd1832002\nparent cac389c34493a2e06a274e7fa710e8ff4bba032e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783551056 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783551056 -0400\n\nchore(code): compare installs by inode in shadowing check (#4577)\n\nThe installer no longer prints a spurious \"shadowing install\" warning\nwhen `~/.local/bin` appears on `PATH` under a non-normalized alias (such\nas `~/.local/share/../bin`) that resolves to the same directory.\n\n---\n\nThe `deepagents-code` installer printed a spurious \"shadowing install\"\nwarning on every run for users whose `PATH` contains a non-normalized\nalias of `~/.local/bin` — most commonly `~/.local/share/../bin`, where\n`share/..` collapses back to `.local`. Some third-party tools write that\nun-normalized spelling into a shell profile (derived from\n`$XDG_DATA_HOME/../bin`), and it can sort before the canonical entry.\nBoth spellings resolve to the same uv-tool symlink the installer just\ncreated, but `detect_shadowing_install` compared `PATH` strings, so the\nalias looked like a separate, older install.\n\nThe primary fix makes the guard compare by inode using bash's `-ef` test\n(same device+inode, resolves `..` and symlinks) in addition to the\nexisting string equality, so same-file aliases short-circuit and never\nwarn. Both operands are guaranteed to exist at that point, and a\ngenuinely different binary at a distinct inode still fails `-ef` and\ncorrectly warns, so only the false positive is suppressed. Secondarily,\n`local_bin_in_profile` now also recognizes the `~/.local/share/../bin`\nspelling so the installer doesn't append a duplicate `~/.local/bin` PATH\nline; this covers the common alias only and isn't a full path\nnormalizer.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/870c16ab-41c7-3eee-e0d1-55385367ec4f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T22:50:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aad530c099a87a60f9115d241d9e1e8b374afd34","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/de